\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Up Late On Yen; SGD Uninspired \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2 787 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 10:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar continued to be left out in the cold, uninspired by the gains of other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The relatively stable yen - which buoyed most of the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - and the rupiah's rise to new six-month highs failed to check the Singapore dollar's descent past the psychologically important S$1.8500 threshold to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar skidded to an 11-week low of S$1.8507, as participants continued to cover their short U.S. dollar positions - as the near-term rebound in the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  they had been waiting for didn't materialize. \par \par \uc2  However, the U.S. dollar retreated swiftly after a large Singapore bank unloaded the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  all the way from around S$1.8500 to S$1.8470, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar late in the day extended its correction, as local banks led the selling in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0910 GMT (4:10 a.m. EST), the Singapore dollar was quoted at S$1.8439 to the U.S. unit, little changed from S$1.8438 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  U.S. dollar sales by \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  banks sparked concerns of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but some observers said such fears were unjustified as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained well within the MAS' undisclosed policy band. \par \par \uc2  They noted that the MAS has largely given participants a free rein in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market - provided the Singapore dollar was within the policy band - since the middle of last year as the authority moves to gradually liberalize the city-state financial markets. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar has weakened about 1.2% against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its major trading partners over the last two days, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the middle part of its estimated trade-weighted band from the stronger end earlier this week, said Jimmy Koh, head of treasury research at UOB Group. \par \par \uc2  Given Singapore's improving economic outlook, analysts doubt if the MAS will leave the Singapore dollar to trade in the weaker half of the band. \par \par \uc2  Some observers attributed the U.S. dollar's retreat to the increasingly expensive cost of shorting the Singapore dollar - Singapore dollar offshore swaps have moved to the right. This should restrain the U.S. dollar's rise, at least for now. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  participants were also keen to square positions ahead of the long weekend. Singapore's markets are closed for Good Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah relinquished its gains after having earlier extended its climb to a six-month high of IDR9,525 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Short-covering in U.S. dollars and demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from local corporations needing to meet foreign debt repayment pushed the rupiah back to IDR9,630 late in the day, little changed compared with IDR9,620 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah had recently staged a strong recovery after U.S. investment fund Farallon Capital's acquisition of the Indonesian government's 51% stake in PT Bank Central Asia - the country's largest retail bank - earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  Returning capital inflows, political stability and optimism surrounding Indonesia's meeting with the Paris Club of official creditors next month helped reverse the rupiah's fortunes. \par \par \uc2  Mild gains in the yen, traditional month-end U.S. dollar sales by domestic exporters and foreign equity fund inflows bolstered the South Korean won and the New Taiwan dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar finished at 1,327.0 won, lower than KRW1,329.3 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Seoul's benchmark stock index jumped 2.4% to a two-year closing high Wednesday. After a selling spree over the last four days, foreign investors turned into net buyers of South Korean shares, picking up KRW16.1 billion worth of stocks. \par \par \uc2  Against the New Taiwan dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at NT$35.024, lower than Tuesday's NT$35.037. \par \par \uc2  Foreign institutional investors bought a net NT$2.81 billion worth of shares on the Taiwan Stock Exchange Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine Dealing System, the U.S. dollar closed at 51.005 pesos, from PHP51.145 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Month-end U.S. dollar sales by exporters and the trimming of long positions in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the Easter holidays buoyed the peso, dealers said. Markets in Manila are closed Thursday and Friday. \par \par \uc2  Supported by its regional peers, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was slightly stronger at 43.335 baht to the U.S. dollar, compared with THB43.360 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4043; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020327dy3r000mm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
