\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ASIA: Singapore Dlr's Dive Won't Scuttle Uptrend \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2 1,224 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 09:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    A Dow Jones Newswires Column\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar plummeted to an 11-week\par low Wednesday - but analysts believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell by the wayside\par largely because of transient factors and little to do with fundamentals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  They said market participants were caught short in U.S. dollars when their hopes for a near-term rebound in the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't materialize. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, Singapore will likely be one of the first to recuperate from the region-wide economic malaise, with the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  poised to recover to S$1.7800 against its U.S. counterpart by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  Recent economic data have reinforced the growing optimism surrounding the Singapore economy. Although industrial output fell 11.3% year-on-year in February, it was still better than the average decline of about 16% that analysts were expecting. \par \par \uc2  A rebound in the Singapore dollar - which as one of the most actively traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region often sets the direction for other Asian units - will likely support other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly the Thai baht and the Philippine peso which tend to mimic its movements. \par \par \uc2  But in the near term, dealers don't rule out the possibility that the Singapore dollar could retest its 11-year low of S$1.8552, reached on Dec. 27 last year, given the yen's fragility. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said that level would likely pose as a strong support for the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Extending its recent precipitous decline, the Singapore dollar briefly skidded past the psychologically important S$1.8500 threshold against its U.S. counterpart to hit an 11-week low of S$1.8507 earlier Wednesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Trade-Weighted SGD Within Policy Band - Observers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar pulled back after a large Singapore bank unloaded the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  all the way from around S$1.8500 to S$1.8470, sparking fears\par that it could have been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , also\par known as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore, or the MAS.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It gave the market the impression that the MAS was in," said the head\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at an Asian bank. Most dealers believe the\par bank is an MAS agent bank, through which it regularly deals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After that brief dive, the Singapore dollar stabilized around S$1.8470\par most part of the morning, before resuming its correction to S$1.8435 at\par 0845 GMT as local banks led the selling in the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Late\par Tuesday, the Singapore dollar was trading around S$1.8438.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The MAS uses the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , not interest rates, as its primary\par monetary-policy tool to maintain brisk growth and low inflation. The\par Singapore dollar is guided within a trading band against a basket of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the country's major trading partners.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some observers doubted, however, that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as\par the trade-weighted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar remained well within the MAS'\par undisclosed policy band.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They noted too that the MAS has largely given participants a free rein\par in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market - provided the Singapore dollar was\par within the policy band - since the middle of last year as the authority\par moves to gradually liberalize the city-state's financial markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Instead, they attributed the U.S. dollar's retreat to the increasingly\par expensive cost of shorting the Singapore dollar - Singapore dollar\par offshore swaps have moved to the right, observers said. This should\par restrain the U.S. dollar's rise, at least for now.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  participants are also keen to square out of their\par positions ahead of the long weekend. Singapore's markets are closed for\par Good Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar - which has depreciated by almost 2% against its\par U.S. counterpart since early March - has ostensibly taken over the\par rupiah's unenviable position as the black sheep of Asia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets since the end of last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah's fortunes have changed for the better after U.S.\par investment fund Farallon Capital's acquisition of the Indonesian\par government's 51% stake in PT Bank Central Asia - the country's largest\par retail bank - earlier this month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Returning capital inflows, political stability and optimism\par surrounding Indonesia's meeting with the Paris Club of official\par creditors next month helped propel the rupiah to a six-month peak of\par around IDR9,525 against the U.S. dollar earlier Wednesday, observers\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But even a combination of the rupiah's 3.7% rally, the stable yen and\par firmer Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has failed to salvage the Singapore dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As a result, the Singapore dollar has weakened about 1.2% against the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of its major trading partners over the last two days, pushing\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to the middle part of its estimated trade-weighted band\par from the stronger end earlier this week, said Jimmy Koh, head of\par treasury research at UOB Group.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Given Singapore's improving economic outlook, analysts doubt if the\par MAS will allow the Singapore dollar to trade in the weaker half of the\par band.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Options Market Reaction Subdued\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The reaction in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options market to the Singapore dollar's\par sharp drop was fairly subdued, as market participants wonder whether the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's downward momentum could be sustained - especially after it\par appeared to be finding support around S$1.8500 against the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The options market wasn't too flustered with the spot move," said a\par dealer at a U.S. bank. "There are no substantial positions."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities implied by one-month U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options edged up about 0.3 point to trade at 4% earlier\par Wednesday, following the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's brief spike above S$1.8500.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One-month quarter delta risk-reversals remained well bid, favoring\par U.S. dollar call/Singapore dollar put options by 0%/0.8%, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Risk-reversals measure the market preference for either put or call\par options by the premium or discount applied. Delta measures the change in\par the option value for a change in the underlying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market watchers blamed the unwinding of short U.S. dollar positions\par against the Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by international investors - particularly\par U.S. investment houses - for the Singapore dollar's relentless slide in\par recent sessions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These investors were taken aback by the apparent weakness in recently\par issued data, which were distorted by the fewer working days in February\par this year. The Lunar New Year holidays fell in February this year; last\par year, the holidays were in January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Superficial weakness in some headline economic indicators for\par February, a product of fewer working days due to the Lunar New Year,\par appears to be the main culprit," J.P. Morgan Chase Bank said in a report\par Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore's key non-oil domestic exports - a barometer of the\par trade-dependent city state's economic health - fell a\par steeper-than-expected 23.4% in February year-on-year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To a lesser extent, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's move last\par week to further liberalize its policy of non-internationalization of the\par Singapore dollar - in its bid to lure international investors to the\par country's capital markets - also undermined the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as\par participants, betting on further yen weakness, braced for more volatile\par trading, observers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-421-4807;\par netty.ismail@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4258 5095 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020327dy3r000kp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
