\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Asian  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  recover, Sing dollar lags. \b0\par\par\uc2 964 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 09:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, March 27 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  regained their composure late on Wednesday as the dollar backed \par \par \uc2  off against the yen. \par \par \uc2      Once again, the Singapore dollar lagged behind the other \par \par \uc2  regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though it managed to escape its day's low \par \par \uc2  point of 1.8510 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2      Claudio Piron, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \par \par \uc2  Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore, said the Sing dollar also \par \par \uc2  coincidentally had the strongest correlation with the yen in \par \par \uc2  recent months. \par \par \uc2  On a three-month average, the Sing dollar has mimicked the \par \par \uc2  yen's movements 68 percent of the time compared with 63 percent \par \par \uc2  for the Thai baht, 43 percent for the Taiwan dollar and 33 \par \par \uc2  percent for the Korean won, Piron said. \par \par \uc2  "There are three reasons for this, Singapore is a very open \par \par \uc2  economy. It's the most liquid market in the region. And it's \par \par \uc2  got deeper capital markets compared with the rest of the \par \par \uc2  region, and is a more 'freely-floating' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  notwithstanding the policy bands," he said, referring to the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band in which the trade-weighted Singapore \par \par \uc2  dollar is allowed to trade. \par \par \uc2  Given that correlation, the Sing dollar has a rocky ride \par \par \uc2  ahead. The yen was expected to put up a fight later in the day \par \par \uc2  because of last minute yen orders ahead of fiscal year-end, but \par \par \uc2  the dollar was still holding its own even after a Federal \par \par \uc2  Reserve official called it a little overvalued. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was trading around 1.8430/40 compared \par \par \uc2  with 1.8425 late on Tuesday. But it recovered from a fresh \par \par \uc2  11-week low of 1.8510 touched earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said players were still in a dollar-buying mood \par \par \uc2  early in the day following Tuesday's pummeling of the local \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when a number of stop-loss dollar buy levels were \par \par \uc2  triggered. \par \par \uc2  However, as the dollar/yen took a break, the dollar/Sing \par \par \uc2  later ran into resistance around 1.8510, where interbank \par \par \uc2  players and corporates decided to take profit on the dollar's \par \par \uc2  recent strong surge. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said a dollar/Sing at 1.8510 brought the \par \par \uc2  trade-weighted Sing dollar to the lower end of its policy band, \par \par \uc2  prompting players to be wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  manages the \par \par \uc2  Sing dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah took a breather after soaring to 9,530 against \par \par \uc2  the dollar, its highest level since September last year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later eased back to 9,583, with local \par \par \uc2  corporate buying of dollars and some profit-taking on the \par \par \uc2  rupiah tempering this week's rally, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      Local players were also spotted squaring positions ahead of \par \par \uc2  Friday's national holiday. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buoyed by hopes for more capital \par \par \uc2  inflows into local markets, with the government expected to \par \par \uc2  secure debt rescheduling agreements during crucial talks with \par \par \uc2  Paris Club creditors next month. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won eked out gains thanks to month-end dollar sales by \par \par \uc2  exporters and a steadier yen. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers in Singapore said the won's upside was \par \par \uc2  capped by equity-related demand for the dollar, though the \par \par \uc2  market saw signs of hope that net selling by foreign investors \par \par \uc2  was starting to ease. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors sold about 37 billion won worth of local \par \par \uc2  stocks on Tuesday, against 222 billion won worth of shares on \par \par \uc2  Monday. And they turned net buyers on Wednesday, purchasing a \par \par \uc2  net 16.0 billion won worth of shares. \par \par \uc2      The won hit a session high of 1,326.5 as exporters \par \par \uc2  offloaded their foreign earnings for month-end requirements. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht was a bit firmer around 43.30, from early lows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 43.37, aided by equity and investment related inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said there was talk of some dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par purchases by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , though Singapore-based names\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continued to offer dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said some resistance to baht's rise was expected at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 43.25 where dollar bids by onshore players and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporates were believed to be lined up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar lingered within its well-worn range\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around the 35 per dollar level, supported by equity-related\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows and a steadier yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors continued to be net buyers of local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks, picking up 2.82 billion Taiwan dollar worth of local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They have bought a net 16 billion Taiwan dollar worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local scrips in the past seven sessions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was again spotted in the market capping\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Taiwan dollar's gains above the 35 level. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has been active on both sides of the market recently to to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par protect export competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso went nowhere in slow, thin offshore trade. Markets\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in Manila were closed, and will re-open next Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0812 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     132.82       132.66         -0.12\par  Sing dlr      1.8446       1.8425         -0.11\par  Taiwan dlr    35.024       35.037         +0.04\par  Korean won   1327.00      1329.3