\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Recovering yen helps, rupiah shines. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,074 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 10:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, March 26 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  took \par \par \uc2  advantage of the yen's bounce back late on Tuesday, with the \par \par \uc2  Indonesian rupiah standing out among regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar proved to be the laggard, suffering \par \par \uc2  from stop-loss dollar buying when key levels were triggered \par \par \uc2  during the course of the day. \par \par \uc2      The rupiah climbed to five-month highs of around 9,585, \par \par \uc2  aided by a sheer lack of dollar demand in the market as well as \par \par \uc2  slightly improving sentiment towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as Jakarta \par \par \uc2  tries to tackle its many political and economic woes. \par \par \uc2  But dealers in Jakarta said the rupiah's comeuppance was \par \par \uc2  around the corner simply because local corporates need to buy \par \par \uc2  dollars to service foreign debt. \par \par \uc2  "This rally is very overdone. I think the genuine demand \par \par \uc2  (for the dollar) will be back and hit the rupiah," said a \par \par \uc2  foreign bank dealer in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2      Elsewhere, the yen's bounce aided some of the regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Thai baht, Korean won and Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2      However, analysts were skeptical that the yen could extend \par \par \uc2  its gains given the poor state of the Japanese economy and the \par \par \uc2  widely accepted view that the country may experience outflows \par \par \uc2  at the end of the month when the fiscal year finishes. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah rose to new five-month highs of 9,585, \par \par \uc2  continuing its recent steady progress. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said local corporates have just been \par \par \uc2  absent from the market, and that's helped the rupiah as they \par \par \uc2  are usually seeking dollars to meet debt obligations. \par \par \uc2  Some said the market was also buoyed by hopes for more \par \par \uc2  inflows into local markets, with the government expected to \par \par \uc2  secure debt rescheduling agreements during crucial talks with \par \par \uc2  the Paris Club next month. \par \par \uc2  However, charts showed the dollar/rupiah was very oversold \par \par \uc2  with a 14-day relative strength index reading of 26.658. This \par \par \uc2  could trigger a huge correction in the rupiah, especially if \par \par \uc2  the corporates return to the market to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar slipped through 1.8400 to hit lows not \par \par \uc2  seen since January amid talk it would be dragged along with the \par \par \uc2  yen to weaker levels after the Japanese fiscal year ends. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said stop-loss Sing dollar sales hit around 1.8427 \par \par \uc2  sent it to a low of 1.8445, a level last seen on January 11 \par \par \uc2  when it touched low of 1.8455. \par \par \uc2  But profit-taking on the dollar's sharp rise with offers \par \par \uc2  lined up beyond 1.8438 capped the Sing dollar's losses, helping \par \par \uc2  it bounce back to levels around 1.8425. \par \par \uc2  Market talk of the yen settling into a weaker 133-135 range \par \par \uc2  and recent data showing Singapore's economy still under \par \par \uc2  deflationary pressure encouraged players to sell the Sing \par \par \uc2  dollar without fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The February consumer price index fell 0.6 percent on the \par \par \uc2  year but was up 0.3 percent from January. \par \par \uc2      There was little response to February manufacturing output \par \par \uc2  data, issued Tuesday, showing a drop of 11.3 percent on the \par \par \uc2  year versus January's 4.3 percent rise. The fall was mainly \par \par \uc2  attributed to plant closures for the Lunar New Year holidays. \par \par \uc2  Meanhwile, charts show the dollar overbought against the \par \par \uc2  Sing dollar with a 14-day relative strength index reading at \par \par \uc2  79.3, suggesting room for more profit-taking on the dollar's \par \par \uc2  gains. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar stayed on the wrong side of 35 within a \par \par \uc2  tight range, aided by equity-related inflows, a rebound in the \par \par \uc2  yen and month-end dollar sales by exporters. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said wariness over recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept most players on the sidelines, \par \par \uc2  reluctant to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  either way. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors were net buyers of T$1.34 billion worth of \par \par \uc2  local stocks on Tuesday, taking net buying over the past six \par \par \uc2  sessions to 13.19 billion. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won managed to turn around its fortunes, ending the day \par \par \uc2  higher at 1,329.3 versus Monday's close of 1,331.5. \par \par \uc2  Month-end dollar sales by exporters helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \uc2  stand up against steady dollar demand from foreign investors \par \par \uc2  who have been dumping local stocks. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors were again net sellers of local stocks, \par \par \uc2  but only sold some 37 billion won worth of shares on Tuesday \par \par \uc2  compared with a net 222.3 billion won on Monday. \par \par \uc2  While these sales have hurt the won, sentiment towards \par \par \uc2  Korea was generally upbeat, especially after Finance Minister \par \par \uc2  Jin Nyum said earlier in the day he expected Moody's to upgrade \par \par \uc2  the country's sovereign ratings by two notches to 'A.' \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht was a touch stronger at 43.33 compared with \par \par \uc2  the previous close at 43.38 as it rose in line with the yen. \par \par \uc2  But weak export data capped further gains for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  February exports slid eight percent year-on-year to their \par \par \uc2  lowest levels in 32 months. \par \par \uc2  The government said the weak export performance would not \par \par \uc2  stop Thailand achieving economic targets this year, including \par \par \uc2  growth of more than three percent. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso shuttled in a narrow 51.125/80 range, with volume \par \par \uc2  roughly a fifth lighter than normal due to the upcoming Easter \par \par \uc2  break. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Manila said trade was quiet, with players \par \par \uc2  squaring off positions ahead of the vacation. \par \par \uc2      They said the peso was unfazed by volatility in the \par \par \uc2  dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2      The market will be closed from noon (0400GMT) on Wednesday \par \par \uc2  until Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0842 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     132.66       133.14         +0.36\par  Sing dlr      1.8425       1.8357         -0.37\par  Taiwan dlr    35.037       35.046         +0.03\par  Korean won   1329.30      1331.50         +0.16\pa