\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yen slide hurts north Asia  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2 , not peso, baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 03:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, March 26 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell \par \par \uc2  early on Tuesday, succumbing to the yen's negative influence. \par \par \uc2      However, there was a difference in the extent of their \par \par \uc2  losses in relation to the yen, with some faithfully following \par \par \uc2  the Japanese unit and others dragged along reluctantly. \par \par \uc2      North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Singapore dollar continued \par \par \uc2  to tag after the yen, which sagged on the market's assumption \par \par \uc2  of outflows from the economically frail Japan once the fiscal \par \par \uc2  year draws to a close this month. \par \par \uc2      In contrast, the peso and baht kept their yen-related \par \par \uc2  losses modest while the rupiah forged its own way higher. \par \par \uc2      The dollar hit a high of 133.46 yen before backing off to \par \par \uc2  trade around 133.06 yen on profit-taking. \par \par \uc2      Some said the yen could see more of a correction after \par \par \uc2  recent heavy gains. However, the dollar/yen's upward trend was \par \par \uc2  still intact. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said the mixed response of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  reflected the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's diminishing importance in the \par \par \uc2  region, barring a complete, and highly unlikely, meltdown of \par \par \uc2  the yen. \par \par \uc2  "What happens to the US economy and to the Chinese renminbi \par \par \uc2  are even more important for the rest of Asia than what happens \par \par \uc2  to the yen," Standard Chartered Bank said in a research note, \par \par \uc2  adding the United States was Asia's biggest customer and China \par \par \uc2  its biggest competitor. \par \par \uc2      "Asia can cope with a slightly weaker yen if the US is \par \par \uc2  strong and the Chinese do not devalue," it said. \par \par \uc2      Ahead for the market was Singapore manufacturing data for \par \par \uc2  February, due around 0445 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won fell past a two-month low of 1,331.5 to the dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and was trading around 1,333.3 -- a level last seen on January\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 24.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     While the weaker yen had some hand in driving the won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower, a sell-off of local equities by foreign investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par masterminded the won's fall. Foreign investors dumped 222\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion won worth of stocks on Monday, a third day of net\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par selling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Net sales of Korean shares by foreign investors has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par totalled 390 billion won in the past three days.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Nevertheless Korea continued to see increasing signs of an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par improving economy. Finance Minister Jin Nyum said earlier in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the day Moody's Investors Service was expected to raise the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's sovereign rating by two notches to "A" by February\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2003.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar was slightly down but was expected to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stay within its recent range around the level of 35 to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar thanks to equity-related inflows and month-end dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sales by exporters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said a softer yen and wariness over\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to keep its upside capped.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been active on both sides of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market in recent sessions keeping the Taiwan dollar within a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par narrow 34.95-35.05 range, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors were net buyers of T$4.02 billion worth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of local stocks on Monday, taking their net buying over the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par past five sessions to T$11.85 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht edged down to around 43.44 to the dollar, compared\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with late Monday's 43.38 on dollar demand from local corporates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and importers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said despite a weaker yen players were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reluctant to pull the baht too low after some U.S. names were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par spotted selling dollars around 43.45-43.50 range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said some equity-related inflows were also supporting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Offshore players had been selling dollars since last Friday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would keep its benchmark rates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher than those of the United States.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar was down as speculators bought\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars, betting the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be dragged down with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen into a weaker range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said talk that the yen was heading for 133-135\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range indicated the Sing dollar may have more downside. And\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par given recent inflation numbers, there was little hope the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities would resist a softer exchange rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore manages its exchange rate against a basket of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade-weighted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with the yen believed to be a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par significant component.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The consumer price index fell 0.6 percent in February\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the same month a year earlier and was up 0.3 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par versus January. Analysts said that indicated recent signals of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some life in the recession-hit economy were not strong enough.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah continued to gain thanks to optimism over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par returning capital inflows ahead of a key Paris Club creditors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par meeting next month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was around five-month highs, and dealers in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jakarta said it could test the psychologically key level of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 9,500 to the dollar - last seen on September 25.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Finance Minister Boedino told Reuters on Monday Indonesia\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would seek to reschedule less than $5.5 billion in debt against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations of some $6 billion. That comment helped boost\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment towards the rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite the optimism over Jakarta's debt rescheduling and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its attempts to tackle graft, the government's handling of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy was still seen as shambolic.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The finance ministry and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Monday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they were in dispute over the servicing of some $15 billion in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bonds, casting doubt on budget deficit figures for 2001 and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par beyond.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor was recently sentenced to three\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par years of jail for graft, but remains free and is still in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par control of the bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso opened a touch softer and dealers in Manila saw\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  drifting sideways in thin, pre-Easter trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was expected to remain in a narrow range and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par track movements in the dollar/yen, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said there would be no aggressive position taking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of the Easter holiday, with the cost of carry making long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar positions expensive and players reluctant to go short\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of the long weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Manila police have ordered tight security around churches\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after another explosive device was found near the capital on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday. Eight such devices were found last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market is closed from noon on Wednesday through Friday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the Easter holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0148 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     133.19       133.14         -0.04\par  Sing dlr      1.8405       1.8357         -0.26\par  Taiwan dlr    35.050       35.046         -0.01\par  Korean won   1333.30      1331.50         -0.14\par  Baht           43.36        43.38         +0.05\par  Peso           51.16        51.12         -0.07\par  Rupiah       9655.00      9695.00         +0.41\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     133.19       131.24         -1.46\par  Sing dlr      1.8405       1.8515         +0.60\par  Taiwan dlr    35.050       34.986         -0.18\par  Korean won   1333.30      1313.00         -1.52\par  Baht           43.36        44.16         +1.85\par  Peso           51.16        51.50         +0.67\par  Rupiah       9655.00     10350.00         +7.20\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020326dy3q004sm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\pi