\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  ease with yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 891 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 10:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, March 25 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  easier late Monday as the yen slipped to fresh multi-week lows. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen        slipped through 133 per dollar amid talk\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese investors had started to send funds abroad ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the new fiscal year starting on April 1.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah again managed to buck the trend,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hitting fresh five-month highs around 9,700, as Jakarta\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expressed optimism over rescheduling $5.5 billion of its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign debt owed to bilateral donors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some equity-related inflows and month-end dollar sales by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exporters helped cap the downside for the Taiwan dollar and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Philippine peso but the won fell to two-month lows on fears of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outflows as foreign investors continued to sell Korean stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After Wall Street's disappointing performance on Friday on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par worries over corporate earnings, markets would be looking at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par February durable goods and existing home sales data due later\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the day for confirmation that the U.S. recovery was on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par course.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan was also due to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speak before a reception in Washington at 2200 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah touched five-month highs beyond 9,750 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, buoyed by investment-related dollar inflows and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par optimism over Jakarta's upcoming Paris Club meeting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Dealers said the rupiah hit its highest levels since October\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with dollar sales spotted from local players, including the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit fresh highs after Finance Minister\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Boediono said creditor nations would agree to reschedule $5.5\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion debt maturing between April 2002 to December 2003 at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par April's Paris Club meeting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The first payment by U.S. investment house Farallon for a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 51 percent stake in Bank Central Asia , expected on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday, also aided sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won slipped to touch a low of 1,331.5, a level last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seen on January 25, as foreign investors sold local equities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the third consecutive session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign investors sold a net 222 billion won worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks on Monday, taking total net sales to 389 billion won for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the last three session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said part of those sales were settled\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Monday, resulting in outflow of dollars from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, hopes of investment-related inflows and month-end\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar sales by exporters capped the won's downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar edged to the weaker side of its recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range but equity-related inflows and fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  limited its downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said despite the inflows and local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks ending at a 17-month high, players pulled the Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar down on concerns over the bearish trajectory of the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was again spotted actively on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par both sides of the market which made players reluctant to push\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  too far either way.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said M2 money supply rose 4.44 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year on year in February, up from January's record low growth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 3.9 percent mainly due to a rise in demand for cash in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Lunar New Year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht held steady around late Friday's 43.35 per dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level aided by speculation over the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's comments on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary policy and on hopes of equity-related inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht touched a low of 43.44 early on, tracking the yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but dollar sales by offshore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par names capped the downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said some offshore players had been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par selling dollars since last Friday when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would keep its benchmark rates higher than those of the United\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par States.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso closed at the bottom end of its fairly tight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 51.120-51.155 range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said corporate buyers of dollars had been active as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the month draws to a close, with a shortened trading session\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this week for the Easter holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market will close early on Wednesday, and stay\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shut through Thursday and Friday for the Easter vacation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar weakened to near one-month lows in tandem\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the dollar/yen's movement north past 133.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slipped to a low of 1.8367 per dollar, its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lowest since February 28.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said they saw the dollar trying resistance at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par key psychological level 1.8400 after breaking through 1.8350.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR GMT 0912\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     133.14       132.33         -0.61\par  Sing dlr      1.8357       1.8294         -0.34\par  Taiwan dlr    35.046       35.036         -0.03\par  Korean won   1318.40      1328.40         +0.76\par  Baht           43.38        43.35         -0.07\par  Peso           51.11        51.08         -0.06\par  Rupiah       9695.00      9830.00         +1.39\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     133.14       131.24         -1.43\par  Sing dlr      1.8357       1.8515         +0.86\par  Taiwan dlr    35.046       34.986         -0.17\par  Korean won   1318.40      1277.00         -3.14\par  Baht           43.38        44.16         +1.80\par  Peso           51.11        51.50         +0.76\par  Rupiah       9695.00     10350.00         +6.76\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020325dy3p00jge\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
