\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Up Late On Yen; But Yen Vigor Unrivaled \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2 878 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 10:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were stronger late Thursday, as the dollar took a drubbing in international \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, particularly against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen vaulted through the psychologically important Y130 threshold against the dollar to trade at two-and-a-half month highs, after dollar sales by foreign investors triggered a slew of stop-loss orders. \par \par \uc2  At 0900 GMT (4:00 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y129.32, below Y130.77 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar had shed more than a full yen during the overnight session. \par \par \uc2  The yen also chalked up gains against its other Asian counterparts, as the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vigor was unrivaled. \par \par \uc2  "During periods when the yen strengthens sharply against the dollar, one tends to expect the strengthening of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar to lag," said David Simmonds, a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Salomon Smith Barney/Citibank. \par \par \uc2  With the market having largely priced in expectations of an economic recovery in Asia, excluding Japan, later in the year, participants who had gone long Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen in the last few months were now unwinding those positions; at the same time that they unloaded their short yen positions against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Markets have taken on board a strategy this year that Asian fundamentals are stronger than Japan's," Simmonds said, adding that this had led participants to build long positions in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "The whole world has seen this theme and played this theme out for a long time," Simmonds said. "It's time for the market to shake out their positions." \par \par \uc2  The yen's strength was evident in the yen/won. \par \par \uc2  The yen rose to 10.17 won, from around KRW9.9 just two days ago, even as the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened against the dollar Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Still, given South Korea's more promising economic fundamentals vis-a-vis Japan's, Simmonds said he "would look to reestablish won-longs against the yen" at current levels. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the won closed at KRW1,314.5, slightly stronger compared with KRW1,316.3 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The won was, however, off its intraday high of KRW1,309.0, as dollar demand from oil companies and short-covering in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by banks emerged, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market shrugged off the Bank of Korea's as-expected decision Thursday to keep its call rate target unchanged at 4% in March, as the economy shows signs of accelerated growth and inflationary pressures remain benign. The overnight call rate target has been maintained at 4% since late last year. \par \par \uc2  Late in the day, as the dollar collapsed below the key Y129 level, several Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended their gains. At 0940 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y128.95. \par \par \uc2  As Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue to receive a boost from the yen's gains and capital inflows in the region, some of the central banks - particularly in Taiwan, Singapore and Thailand - could become concerned over any excessive appreciation in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Since the anticipated economic recovery in the region has yet to take hold, it would be too early for the monetary authorities to allow their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen too much. \par \par \uc2  The yen lifted the New Taiwan dollar to a five-week closing high against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, although Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought an estimated US$300 million in the last few minutes of trading to curb the appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar closed at NT$34.989, down from NT$35.030 Wednesday. Dealings were valued at US$983 million, higher than US$602 million Wednesday. A dealer in Taipei said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounted for around half of Thursday's turnover. \par \par \uc2  As the baht climbed to a one-year high, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued with its recent dollar-purchases to check its strength, although not aggressively, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 43.275 baht, lower than THB43.515 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was at S$1.8208 against its U.S. counterpart, stronger compared with S$1.8263. \par \par \uc2  With the Singapore dollar currently trading near the stronger end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy band, there's been ongoing jitters about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  guides the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar within a trading band against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the city state's major trading partners and key competitors. In January, the MAS restored a tighter policy band. \par \par \uc2  "I don't expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy to change," said Simmonds at Salomon Smith Barney/Citibank. "The MAS wouldn't want to see the trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade through the strong end of the policy band." \par \par \uc2  Inspired by its regional peers, the Philippine peso cracked above the psychologically important PHP51.00 resistance level against the dollar for the first time in two-and-a-half months. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at PHP50.99, lower than PHP51.09 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was slightly firmer at 9,945 rupiah to the dollar, compared with IDR9,950 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4043; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020307dy37000k0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
