\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late, But Off Overnight High; Tracks Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 566 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 09:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was higher against its U.S. counterpart late Wednesday, tracking a stronger yen, but was off its overnight high when local banks bought U.S. dollars on behalf of corporate clients, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0845 GMT (3:45 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8263, down from S$1.8287 late Tuesday in Asia, but off its overnight low of S$1.8220 in New York. It traded between S$1.8250 and S$1.8285 in Asia Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said liquidation of long U.S. dollar positions pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a low of S$1.8220 the U.S. But it bounced off that level amid possible mild \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  during New York time, said a European bank dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened higher in Asia Wednesday and rose steadily to an intraday high of S$1.8285 as local banks bought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of corporate clients. \par \par \uc2  However, U.S. banks and investment houses sold it back down after the U.S. dollar fell below Y132 in the afternoon, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar could edge lower overnight, especially if it loses more ground to the yen, dealers said. It is expected to find support at S$1.8220, then S$1.8200, with resistance expected at S$1.8300. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were mixed late Wednesday after some bonds recovered from their early morning weakness, which had been due to an overnight fall in U.S. Treasurys, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  After the recent fall in prices, particularly in longer-term bonds, some investors were unable to resist picking up bargains, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  "The local market seemed to defy the U.S. Treasurys market. Our market proved to be quite resilient. Not only did they recover in the afternoon, but some even closed higher," a local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds was flat at 1.66% while the yield on five-year bonds was down two basis points at 3.08%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds slipped one basis point to 3.57% while the yield on 10-year bonds slipped one basis point to 3.80%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds was flat at 4.24%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, the most liquid seven-year swap\par offer closed flat at 3.68%. The 10-year swap offer ended unchanged at\par 3.96%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps widened to 185 basis points\par from 183 basis points late Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank money market, rates were mostly flat as liquidity\par remained flush in the system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Wednesday    Late Tuesday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.7500% 0.8750%   0.8750% 1.0000%\par 3-Month           0.8750% 1.0000%   0.8750% 1.0000%\par 1-Year            1.2500% 1.3750%   1.2500% 1.3750%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150;\par amit.prakash@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020306dy36000ii\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
