\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Higher, but rangebound. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,057 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2002\par 03:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Feb 26 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  firm on Tuesday, but stuck in their recent ranges as the \par \par \uc2  dollar/yen dithered. \par \par \uc2      Given the economic events slated for this week, trading in \par \par \uc2  the dollar/yen kept to the safe side. Players idled on the \par \par \uc2  sidelines as they waited for the Japanese government to \par \par \uc2  announce its deflation-fighting package on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan is also due to \par \par \uc2  appear before Congress for his biannual testimony on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      On Thursday, the Bank of Japan's monetary board is due to \par \par \uc2  meet. \par \par \uc2      With the dollar/yen acting docile, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have \par \par \uc2  been in somewhat of a bind in terms of finding a new direction. \par \par \uc2      "We still like the regionals versus the yen ... but other \par \par \uc2  than that, everyone is still waiting for the dollar/yen to \par \par \uc2  move," a senior dealer at a European bank in Hong Kong said. \par \par \uc2      Players were trying to dig for cues on the local front, but \par \par \uc2  even there, they were coming up short. Equity-related flows \par \par \uc2  have influenced the direction of the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but \par \par \uc2  not enough to push them out of their recent ranges. \par \par \uc2      As for data, Taiwan was set to issue its January M2 money \par \par \uc2  supply data. \par \par \uc2      Bangkok markets were closed for a one-day public holiday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won slipped amid continued nervousness over further\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possible equity sales by foreign investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors have been steadily selling local equities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the past seven sessions. However, players were hopeful that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wall Street's overnight gains and an early rise in the Korean\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Composite Stock Price Index could reverse that trend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, Singapore and Hong Kong dealers said there was also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some corporate demand that could keep the won on the backfoot.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They added there had been talk in the market that the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities were expressing more concerns over export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitiveness at private meetings with banks, making players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wary about pushing the won higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar stuck around the higher end of its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent range, close to the 1.83 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Since February 19, the Sing dollar has traded in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relatively narrow range of 1.8250-1.8340 largely due to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lack of interest and flows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They added unless the dollar/yen breaks out of its current\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range of 133-134, it was unlikely that the dollar/Sing was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par going to make any radical moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading activity is subdued as offshore players were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reluctant to take fresh positions aggressively in the absence\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the onshore market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Thai financial markets are closed for a religious holiday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and will reopen on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht was stuck in a tight 43.79-43.81 in early trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the forward market, baht funding costs were mostly steady,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the one-month rate quoted at 6/7 satang per dollar and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tom/next rate at 0.04/0.09 satang.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was held slightly down from late Monday levels\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 10,165 amid reluctance by interbank players to take fresh\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions on wariness over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar-selling\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par checking rates in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on Monday and some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers suspected dollar sales by state banks was on behalf of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the authorities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Focus in the market is on the sale of the Bank Central\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asia, which has recently hit snags after some of the investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bidding for the country's largest retail bank threatened to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pull out citing political reasons and a lack of transparency.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One foreign and several local companies separately have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said they were considering to pull out of the respective\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par consortium they were part of. In all four consortia are in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par race for up to 51 percent stake in the BCA.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts say Jakarta's failure to to sell the bank would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hit foreign investor sentiment and the rupiah further worsening\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the economic problems of the troubled country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar rose slightly, taking heart in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overnight gains on Wall Street, which lifted local stocks in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par early trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As with Korea, Taiwan's bourse has been suffering from net\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sales from foreign investors, which has worried the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, the market was hoping that the bourse's early gains\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could mean that foreign investors become net buyers of local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks again.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overall, the Taiwan dollar was not expected to move far\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par above or below the 35 level until there are clear signals as to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par where the recession-hit economy was headed. Indeed, the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was keeping its eye on key economic data due on Wednesday that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par include January industrial production and export orders.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso market opened slightly firmer at 51.330 against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 51.368 on Friday. The market is listless as players were still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reeling from a holiday on Monday, with no transaction done\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par until 0128 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to move in a recent 51.30-51.40\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as dollar demand for NDF settlements is offset by gains in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regionals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Apart from seasonal dollar demand for NDFs and hedging\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par purposes, dealers said the peso should be underpinned by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par improved sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts remain fairly positive on the ability of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government to stay close to its fiscal targets. They also see\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. involvement as a net positive in maintaining political\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stability.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0137 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     133.85       133.64         -0.16\par  Sing dlr      1.8308       1.8311         +0.02\par  Taiwan dlr    35.077       35.090         +0.04\par  Korean won   1323.70      1323.90         +0.02\par  Baht           43.80        43.80         +0.00\par  Peso           51.33        51.37         +0.07\par  Rupiah      10167.00     10165.00         -0.02\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japa