\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Dragged lower by yen, rupiah shines. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2002\par 09:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Feb 19 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were on \par \par \uc2  the defensive late on Tuesday because of the stumbling yen. \par \par \uc2      After U.S. President George W. Bush left Japan for Korea, \par \par \uc2  the market threw aside its recent decorum, punishing the yen \par \par \uc2  for the Japanese government's failure to come up with fresh \par \par \uc2  ways to tackle its many economic problems. \par \par \uc2  Only the Indonesian rupiah defied the regional downward \par \par \uc2  trend, climbing some 0.20 percent higher thanks to the trickle \par \par \uc2  of equity-related dollar inflows from foreign funds. \par \par \uc2  Otherwise, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  felt the gravitational pull \par \par \uc2  of the yen's fall past 133. But, as has been the trend since \par \par \uc2  late last year when the yen started on its decline to \par \par \uc2  three-year lows, losses in the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were modest. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht did have to suffer through a bit of verbal \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which said it would not let \par \par \uc2  the rate hurt exports. \par \par \uc2  "The market is really seeing this as a dollar/yen move. So \par \par \uc2  if the dollar/yen moves higher, why play it in the dollar/Sing \par \par \uc2  (dollar) or the dollar/baht? Just play it in the dollar/yen," \par \par \uc2  said the senior dealer at a local bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have already taken note of this phenomenon, saying \par \par \uc2  the yen, and in turn, Japan, no longer casts such a long shadow \par \par \uc2  over the region, especially as many countries here are expected \par \par \uc2  to benefit from the long-awaited U.S. economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah rose above the 10,200 level helped by \par \par \uc2  equity-related inflows and as some major corporates sold \par \par \uc2  dollars for their seasonal needs. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said given the small size and the \par \par \uc2  illiquid nature of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the rupiah rose even \par \par \uc2  though some state banks were spotted buying dollars which \par \par \uc2  sparked rumours the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market to beef up \par \par \uc2  its reserves. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said dollar/rupiah's failure to convincingly \par \par \uc2  breach the 10,250 level in the past several sessions would \par \par \uc2  further prompt interbank dealers to trim their dollar longs. \par \par \uc2  They said a test of the 10,000 level was possible in coming \par \par \uc2  days on the back of foreign inflows into the local stocks \par \par \uc2  market that has risen by about 19 percent year-to-date. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar followed the yen lower, flirting with \par \par \uc2  the 1.83 level on U.S. dollar short covering and U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  demand from funds. \par \par \uc2      But greenback offers from a U.S. name near 1.83 helped the \par \par \uc2  local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pare losses. \par \par \uc2      There had been talk earlier that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \par \par \uc2  have bought the U.S. dollar after one local bank was seen \par \par \uc2  bidding actively. \par \par \uc2      But some dealers dismissed such rumours, saying they saw no \par \par \uc2  need for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      "We don't think this is due to the MAS as SGD is currently \par \par \uc2  trading well within its bands against its trade-weighted \par \par \uc2  basket," said a UBS Warburg report. \par \par \uc2      "Instead, we expect players may be manipulating the market \par \par \uc2  at present to squeeze USD shorts and so we remain wary of a \par \par \uc2  pull back toward 1.8330," the report said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht gave up most of the gains it made in the past few\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sessions after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prompted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some players to cover short dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday the baht was stable and the bank would not let it hurt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exports. The market took the remark to mean the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would keep the baht soft to promote exports which is the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's major growth engine.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Moreover, some foreign banks bought back the U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because they believed the baht's recent appreciation was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overdone and that recent equity inflows might taper off soon,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said a dealer at a European bank in Thailand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Charts show the baht finally breaks out of its uptrend\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par channel dating back to January 23. However, a Fibonacci study\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par indicates 43.80 remains good support for the baht for now.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso slipped in line with the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par though it recovered from its day's lows of 51.33.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Manila said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was slightly upset by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade data that was issued earlier in the day. The National\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Statistics Office said the trade surplus fell 61.1 percent in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2001 to $2.6 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, the data did reveal a bit of good news. Imports\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fell in December 2001 on a year-on-year basis, but rose 5.1\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent month-on-month to $2.143 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Moreover, sentiment towards the peso remained chipper, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players hoping for more foreign funds inflows into the local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stock market as well as stronger economic growth this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won was weighed down to around 1,321 from late Monday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,316 level by fresh losses in the local stock market which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par raised the spectre of equity-related outflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign investors were net sellers, for the third\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par consecutive day, of local stocks worth 48 billion won on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said tapering off of foreign inflows in the stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market had caught several interbank and offshore players short\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of dollars. And covering of those positions could push the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/won towards 1,325-1,330 range in coming days.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Those concerns overshadowed data showing consumer outlook\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par improved in January for the fourth consecutive month. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par consumer confidence index rose to 106.7 from 100.9 in December,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par indicating higher household spending in the next six months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, some export-related dollar sales helped the won on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar ended the day lower on the weaker yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said some local corporates were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par spotted offering dollars, though most in the market were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fretting over the yen's weakened state. Moreover, the local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar was hurt by net foreign investors' sales of some T$897\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million in stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said Taiwan's very rich and very powerful \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was not seen in the market. The bank often \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on both\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sides of the market to keep the rate stable, now especially\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par important as the island's economy struggles to get back on its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par feet after being hit by its worst recession ever.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0839 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     133.65       132.67         -0.73\par  Sing dlr      1.8292       1.8274         -0.10\par  Taiwan dlr    35.095       35.085         -0.03\par  Korean won    1321.00      1316.60        +0.33\par  Baht           43.70        43.58         -0.27\par  Peso           51.28        51.23         -0.10\par  Rupiah      10195.00     10220.00         +0.25\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     133.65       131.24         -1.80\par  Sing dlr      1.8292       1.8515         +1.22\par  Taiwan dlr    35.095       34.986         -0.31\par  Korean won   1321.00      1313.00         -0.60\par  Baht           43.70        44.16         +1.05\par  Peso           51.28        51.50         +0.43\par  Rupiah      10195.00     10350.00         +1.52\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020219dy2j00hlj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
