\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yen weighs, U.S.-Japan summit disappoints. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2002\par 02:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Feb 19 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked the \par \par \uc2  yen lower in early trade on Tuesday as the market was \par \par \uc2  disappointed that no concrete steps were unveiled at the \par \par \uc2  meeting between President George W. Bush and Japanese Prime \par \par \uc2  Minister Junichiro Koizumi. \par \par \uc2      Trading is likely to be subdued, with financial markets in \par \par \uc2  the United States closed on Monday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2      The yen, followed closely by most emerging Asian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fell below the 133 level. Analysts expect the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move in a 130-135 range in the near term, and there \par \par \uc2  will be a search for official remark on any approach to these \par \par \uc2  extremes. \par \par \uc2  "The Bush-Koizumi meeting in a way is yen negative because \par \par \uc2  they did not say what the market had wanted to hear. That \par \par \uc2  should weigh on emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well, although the \par \par \uc2  downside is likely to be limited by recent capital inflows," \par \par \uc2  said a trader at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  On the data front, South Korea will publish its January \par \par \uc2  consumer outlook at 0300 GMT, and the Philippines will release \par \par \uc2  its trade balance data for December later in the day. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan will release fourth quarter current account balance \par \par \uc2  on Wednesday, and trade data on Thursday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar was easier on the back of U.S. dollar short\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par covering. There was talk of possible U.S. dollar buying on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday after one local bank was seen bidding aggressively.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But some dealers dismissed such rumours, saying they saw no\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par need for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -- the city\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par state's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -- to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at this point.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We don't think this is due to the MAS as the SGD is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par currently trading well within its bands against its trade-\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weighted basket," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at UBS Warburg, in his report.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Instead, we expect players may be manipulating the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at present to squeeze USD shorts and so we remain way of a pull\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par back towards 1.8330," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Another dealer said the Sing dollar weakness was also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par linked to demand for the U.S. dollar by funds and some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate players to invest in equities abroad.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won succumbed to the downward pressure of the weaker\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen, with falls on the local stock market also depressing its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mood.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overall, though, trading was subdued amid a dearth of fresh\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par leads. Analysts have noted that the onshore market may be long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on won, which meant there could be further downside for the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. President George Bush arrives in Seoul late on Tuesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from Japan for a visit, and is due to meet Korean President Kim\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dae-jung on Wednesday. The talks between the two leaders are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to centre on North Korea, which Bush dubbed as one of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the countries in an "axis of evil" along with Iraq and Iran.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Washington's rhetoric was seen as undermining Seoul's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "sunshine policy" of rapprochement with the North.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht retreated below the 43.60 per dollar level to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reflect the yen's weakness as exporters held back on selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers expect the baht to continue to be underpinned by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity inflows. The semi-state run Thailand Opportunity Fund\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said on Monday it planned to start investing an initial 3.6\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion baht in Thai stocks from this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The move is likely to attract more foreign investors into\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market where a number of blue chip stocks are still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par considered cheap, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Charts show the baht is well-supported at 43.80 which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par represents the dollar/baht's January 23-February 15 downmove.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah held steady within its recent range supported by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity-related inflows and trimming of long dollar positions by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interbank players.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Capping the upside for the rupiah were local corporates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying dollars at around 10,200 level for import and debt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par payment needs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank Indonesia said on Monday out of a total of $133\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion, the maturing foreign debt would total some $20 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in first-half 2002, adding pressure on the fragile rupiah, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outstanding debt would continue to shrink in the coming years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, dealers said market sentiment has improved amid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growing optimism over the government's privatisation programme,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the sale of a 30 percent stake in state-run Bank Central\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asia, Indonesia's largest retail bank, expected later in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar straggled along in familiar territory,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par falling slightly on the back of the weaker yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Daily charts showed the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been trading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par within a wider range since December 21, when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par let go of its usually dogged \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep a stable rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and allowed the Taiwan dollar to trade below the level of 35 to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Since then, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has fluctuated between 34.88-35.20\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appearing on both sides of the market to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par temper any volatility.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep up its presence\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the market, perhaps allowing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken given\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the uncertain prospects for the Taiwan economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Unlike its North Asian counterpart Korea, Taiwan has yet to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par show any firm signs of recovery. January exports fell by 1.4\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent year-on-year, damping hopes for a rebound.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso fell slightly, bruised by the yen's fall with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign banks buying the dollar/peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Manila said the market was also perturbed by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par news that the Philippine trade surplus fell to $503 million in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par December compared with $1.259 billion a year ago. The country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par full year trade surplus for 2001 was $2.6 billion versus $6.691\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion in 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, the peso's downside was expected to be limited\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because of subdued corporate dollar demand and generally upbeat\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment about the peso and the country's economic outlook for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers added the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was expected to trade within a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range of around 51.17-51.27, with some local oil companies\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par looking to pick up dollars on dips past 51.20.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0133 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     133.26       132.67         -0.44\par  Sing dlr      1.8289       1.8274         -0.08\par  Taiwan dlr    35.081       35.085         +0.01\par  Korean won   1319.30      1316.60         -0.20\par  Baht           43.60        43.58         -0.05\par  Peso           51.26        51.23         -0.06\par  Rupiah      10218.00     10220.00         +0.02\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     133.26       131.24         -1.52\par  Sing dlr      1.8289       1.8515         +1.24\par  Taiwan dlr    35.081       32.900         -6.22\par  Korean won   1306.60      1277.00         -2.27\par  Baht           43.60        44.16         +1.28\par  Peso           51.26        51.50         +0.47\par  Rupiah      10218.00     10350.00         +1.29\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020219dy2j0040k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
