\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Tracking yen in lacklustre holiday trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 710 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2002\par 02:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Feb 11 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  down with the yen early Monday, although holidays around \par \par \uc2  the region were expected to keep trading subdued and ranges \par \par \uc2  narrow. \par \par \uc2      Japanese financial markets were closed for Monday for a \par \par \uc2  local holiday while Korea, and Taiwan were shut for the Chinese \par \par \uc2  New Year. Most Asian markets will be closed on Tuesday and \par \par \uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      The yen was probing lows hit last week around the 135 level \par \par \uc2  but analysts expected rangebound trade in Asian time zone due \par \par \uc2  to the holiday mood and a lack of cues from the Group of Seven \par \par \uc2  finance leaders' meeting in Ottawa over the weekend. \par \par \uc2      The G7 finance ministers and central bankers sounded \par \par \uc2  hopeful that the global economic downturn would be short, but \par \par \uc2  made only the most tepid reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2      Markets had speculated that the world's industrialised \par \par \uc2  powers could discuss the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has tumbled \par \par \uc2  sharply to three-year lows against the dollar. \par \par \uc2      Japan being a major trading partner and export competitor, \par \par \uc2  the yen's sharp losses of more than 15 percent since last \par \par \uc2  September has made authorities around the region sensitive to \par \par \uc2  their own exchange rate competitiveness. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar edged down from its late Friday levels\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1.8310 with the market focused on the moves in the yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for direction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said activity in the market was mainly due to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pre-holiday interbank position squaring and trading interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was minimal. A range of 1.8330-1.8350 was expected for the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market would be closed from Tuesday to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday and will resume trade on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah touched a seven-week high of 10,230, a level\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par last seen on December 24, as interbank players trimmed their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par long dollar positions ahead of the Tuesday holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , after aggressive dollar purchases by state banks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par last week, had prompted players to square out of their long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Stop-loss dollar sales orders triggered along the way had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par also aided the rupiah, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, some local dollar demand was spotted around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10,225-10,230 which was expected to cap the rupiah's gains for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par now.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht held its ground above 44.00 in a subdued market as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players were not willing to take fresh positions ahead of Lunar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par New Year holidays.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Although Thai financial markets are open during Lunar New\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Year, a number of Chinese-Thai companies will be closed.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the baht was underpinned by dollar offers from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore names in Singapore and Hong Kong, and capital inflows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from a Japanese auto maker.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Going forward, dealers expect the baht to retain its firm\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tone, with charts showing 43.70 as its near-term resistance.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was down in line with other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and on local commercial demand for the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said with holidays around the region and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par absence of fresh local leads, most players would prefer to stay\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par out of the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They expected the peso to linger within a tight range\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around the 51.20 level for the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Although financial market in Philippines would be open\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par through the week, dealers said trade would remain subdued due\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to holidays in the region.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     134.79       133.66         -0.84\par  Sing dlr      1.8318       1.8309         -0.05\par  Taiwan dlr    35.080       35.029         -0.15\par  Korean won   1310.20      1320.20         +0.76\par  Baht           43.85        43.88         +0.07\par  Peso           51.28        51.22         -0.11\par  Rupiah      10233.00     10251.00         +0.18\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     134.79       131.24         -2.63\par  Sing dlr      1.8318       1.8515         +1.08\par  Taiwan dlr    35.080       34.986         -0.27\par  Korean won   1310.20      1313.00         +0.21\par  Baht           43.85        44.16         +0.71\par  Peso           51.28        51.50         +0.44\par  Rupiah      10233.00     10350.00         +1.14\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020211dy2b003ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
