\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-Asia c.banks cap  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  gains, but not for long. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 827 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2002\par 05:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 30 (Reuters) - From Seoul to Bangkok, Asian central banks are out to make sure their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not pushed too high by a positive turn in the region's economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  With the global economy stuttering back to life, Asian policymakers are anxious that strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  do not hamper their ability to compete in reviving export markets like Europe and the United States, analysts said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody wants to miss out when the U.S. economy starts moving again. You don't want to be uncompetitive when the global demand cycle picks up," said Simon Flint, Bank of America's senior strategist in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  But as soon as the dollar peaks against the yen and the global recovery becomes more entrenched, most central banks are likely to allow their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reflect their fundamental strength, the analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "These are \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for economies that have seen strong productivity gains, they have been gaining export market share over the last decade. They should be appreciating over time," said James Malcolm, J.P. Morgan Chase's strategist in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Given the region's exposure to global demand, analysts believe Asia, more than other emerging market zones, will benefit the most from an expected rebound led by the United States - its major export destination. \par \par \uc2  Recent data suggests most economies may have already hit a trough, while strong flows of money into Asian equities and moderating outflows from corporate debt repayments as interest rates fall are supporting most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Korean won -2 and the Thai baht have gained more than four percent from their April 2001 lows against the dollar of 1,365.30 and 45.85 respectively. The Singapore dollar is up by over one percent and the Philippine peso by over half a percent since the start of 2002. \par \par \uc2  CONSERVATIVE BIAS \par \par \uc2  Still, with the yen sickly and doubts lingering over the strength of the U.S. recovery, central banks in the region are keeping up their guard and many are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating too far. \par \par \uc2  "It is a conservative bias," Malcolm said. "We are in the very early stages of recovery, its tentative, a little bit too early to have a very strong view, so that sort of a cautious bias at least on the policymaker side is likely to continue for a little while." \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said on Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had entered the market to maintain the baht's export competitiveness. He said the bank bought dollars recently to help boost the country's foreign reserves. \par \par \uc2  Analysts believe central banks in Korea, Taiwan and \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , through actual or verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently, have also shown an explicit bias to keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped within narrow ranges. \par \par \uc2  "If you had \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  completely freely floating they would have been strengthening much sharply against the yen and the dollar right now. The reason why they are not is that central banks are out there picking up dollars," said Peter Redward, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  TRADE-WEIGHTED WEAKNESS \par \par \uc2  Flint said the performance of the yen tended to be the biggest determinant of exchange rate policy as Japan was most Asian countries' major trading partner and competitor. \par \par \uc2  Given a stronger overlap of North Asia's export portfolio with that of Japan, authorities in Korea and Taiwan would be more vigilant against yen weakness, he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore in a briefing to economists last month reportedly said volatility in the yen would impact its exchange rate management policy. \par \par \uc2  Singapore is the closest rival to North Asia's dominance in electronics exports. \par \par \uc2  "The low interest rate environment in a global recovery scenario suggests that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be used more to keep monetary conditions loose and strengthen the recovery and we see that policy as being positive," said Redward. \par \par \uc2  There are risks to such an active exchange rate policy. \par \par \uc2  "If you create continuous expectations of exchange rate depreciations than you can have an unsettling effect on your domestic banking system, you can cause capital flight and losses of deposits," Flint said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that was probably the reason most central banks had not forced their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to follow the yen in lockstep in its recent slide against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Malcolm said Bank of Korea was showing signs of breaking out of the old regime of mapping every yen move, when it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the yen/won cross rate slipping above 10 won. \par \par \uc2  "We've been breaking through that and we're going to continue to move out of that range for the rest of this year. It does signal that they don't want to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  super-weak to maintain a certain level of yen/won cross," he said. \par \par \uc2  The won last month touched a high of 9.90 against the yen, compared to a low of 11.24 in September. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020205dy2500845\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
