\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Yen cheers,though equity losses sting. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,113 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2002\par 02:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Feb 5 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose a tad \par \par \uc2  early on Tuesday, finding some solace in the steadier yen. \par \par \uc2      But they were held back by steep falls on Wall Street, \par \par \uc2  which dampened spirits on Asian bourses. The Dow Jones \par \par \uc2  Industrial Average lost 2.22 percent while the \par \par \uc2  technology-heavy Nasdaq slipped by 2.91 percent because \par \par \uc2  investors were growing more jittery about corporate accounting \par \par \uc2  practises. \par \par \uc2  Analysts, however, said most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were expected \par \par \uc2  to continue strengthening in the longer term because of the \par \par \uc2  economic recovery in the United States - the largest consumer \par \par \uc2  of Asian exports. \par \par \uc2  For now, though, dealers in Singapore said there was little \par \par \uc2  interest in many of the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which meant that \par \par \uc2  they could find themselves trapped in their recent ranges for \par \par \uc2  some time. Interest in trading was also falling off ahead of \par \par \uc2  the Lunar New Year next week. \par \par \uc2  "The Singapore dollar for instance has proven itself to be \par \par \uc2  very frustrating. Even if you have a range you can't really \par \par \uc2  play it because there's no liquidity. Something drastic has to \par \par \uc2  happen to move it," said a European bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  On the events calendar, the Philippines released inflation \par \par \uc2  data for January set to be followed later by Taiwan, while \par \par \uc2  Korea was expected to issue its January producer price index. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won edged up, tracking the yen's gains and as interbank \par \par \uc2  players sold dollars in anticipation of higher demand for the \par \par \uc2  won by local corporates to pay Chinese New Year bonuses to \par \par \uc2  their employees. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said recent losses in the stock market \par \par \uc2  were expected to cap the won's rise above the 1,305-1,310 \par \par \uc2  range. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Finance Minister Jin Nyum said Korea will \par \par \uc2  maintain a low interest policy in the first half of this year \par \par \uc2  as growth in exports and investment is not fast enough to spur \par \par \uc2  a full-fledged recovery. \par \par \uc2  Jin brushed off concerns that Korea's economy may show \par \par \uc2  signs of overheating, saying current economic and monetary \par \par \uc2  policies would be kept intact in the first half. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht lingered just above the 44 per dollar level aided \par \par \uc2  by equity-related inflows undetered by recent stock market \par \par \uc2  losses. Foreign investors have bought about 10 billion baht \par \par \uc2  worth of Thai stocks since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  However, the upside was capped by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that on Monday said it had bought dollars to \par \par \uc2  beef up foreign reserves and was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem \par \par \uc2  volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said local corporate dollar bids were \par \par \uc2  expected around 43.90 while offers were lined up within the \par \par \uc2  44.05-44.10 range. \par \par \uc2  Underlining the growing foreign investor interest in Thai \par \par \uc2  stocks, ING Barings in a recent research report said it has \par \par \uc2  upgraded Thailand to overweight from neutral saying it is the \par \par \uc2  third cheapest market in Asia. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso rose against the dollar following the regional \par \par \uc2  trend but was expected to maintain a narrow 51.00-51.15 range \par \par \uc2  due to the lack of fresh leads and corporate interest. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said improving sentiment on the economic \par \par \uc2  outlook and some equity-related inflows were expected to \par \par \uc2  support the peso. \par \par \uc2  Inflation for January came at 3.8 percent on the year, down \par \par \uc2  from 4.1 percent in December. The data would cement hopes of \par \par \uc2  further rate cuts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had recently said it \par \par \uc2  would continue to ease interest rates even after the U.S. ended \par \par \uc2  its easing cycle. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar drifted higher in its recent range of \par \par \uc2  around 1.8290-1.8400 per U.S. dollar, listlessly tagging after \par \par \uc2  the yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Sing dollar was likely to trade up to \par \par \uc2  1.8290, but was unlikely to break that level given its failure \par \par \uc2  to do so last week. They added its downside was likely limited \par \par \uc2  around 1.8340. \par \par \uc2  As with some of the other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the \par \par \uc2  Sing dollar has been plagued by a sheer lack of trading \par \par \uc2  interest, especially ahead of the Lunar New Year. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said while the market was happy to sell the dollar \par \par \uc2  on rallies given the view that Singapore - with its key \par \par \uc2  electronics sector - would stand to benefit from the global \par \par \uc2  economic recovery, many were also playing it safe by buying the \par \par \uc2  dollar back on dips. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar held onto its gains above the 35 level \par \par \uc2  thanks to exporters' U.S. dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually gets a boost ahead of the Lunar New \par \par \uc2  Year because local companies have to pay their employees \par \par \uc2  bonuses and to throw banquets for them. \par \par \uc2  However, the market was likely to remain well-behaved given \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's looming presence in the market. The bank has \par \par \uc2  been active on both sides of the market to deter the Taiwan \par \par \uc2  dollar from straying too far from the 35 level. \par \par \uc2      Taipei markets will be closed between February 11-14, and \par \par \uc2  will reopen on the 15th. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah was fenced in a fairly narrow range of around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10,310-10,320, with many players absent as Jakarta continued to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cope with the worst flooding seen in decades.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Market players have been opting to stay at home rather than\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par brave the floods, which have affected many parts of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesian capital. Jakarta dealers have said trading has been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lacklustre as a result.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the meantime, the government said its gross\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par international reserves were at $27.77 billion as of the fourth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week of January, the same figure as the week before. Before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rounding, there was a slight decrease of $3.3 million, which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the government owed to the repayment of foreign debts.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0108 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     132.12       133.26         +0.86\par  Sing dlr      1.8320       1.8335         +0.08\par  Taiwan dlr    34.950       34.998         +0.14\par  Korean won   1312.50      1317.80         -0.40\par  Baht           43.95        43.98         +0.07\par  Peso           51.16        51.22         +0.12\par  Rupiah      10310.00     10310.00         +0.00\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     132.12       131.24         -0.67\par  Sing dlr      1.8320       1.8515         +1.06\par  Taiwan dlr    34.950       34.986         +0.10\par  Korean won   1307.80      1313.00         +0.40\par  Baht           43.95        44.16         +0.48\par  Peso           51.16        51.50         +0.66\par  Rupiah      10310.00     10350.00         +0.39\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020205dy25007ja\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
