\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yen spoils upbeat global economic outlook. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,031 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2002\par 02:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Feb 1 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stumbled over \par \par \uc2  the yen early on Friday, though most resisted emulating the \par \par \uc2  yen's sharp losses as they have so far this year. \par \par \uc2      The dollar continued to hound the yen to three-year lows \par \par \uc2  after the market mulled over signs that the U.S. was indeed \par \par \uc2  recovering and decided to embrace optimism over the economy \par \par \uc2  whole-heartedly, especially as Japan struggled with political \par \par \uc2  and economic troubles. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill gave the dollar an \par \par \uc2  extra kick when he said he had no sympathy for U.S. \par \par \uc2  manufacturers fretting over the strong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Still, the dollar could face some resistance from Japanese \par \par \uc2  investors and companies seeking to repatriate ahead of the \par \par \uc2  fiscal year-end bookclosing in March. \par \par \uc2  Among the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the won was the most vulnerable \par \par \uc2  to waxing and waning of the yen's fortunes. However, gains on \par \par \uc2  Wall Street were likely to spillover to Asian bourses. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, many analysts have pointed out that regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should rise if the U.S. - the biggest consumer of \par \par \uc2  Asia's exports - does rebound. However, they have hit a major \par \par \uc2  snag in the form of the weaker yen. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won gapped lower to open at 1,324 compared with \par \par \uc2  Thursday's close of 1,314.4, upset with the yen's weakened \par \par \uc2  state. \par \par \uc2  However, rises in the local stock market and foreign fund \par \par \uc2  inflows quickly served to counteract the yen's negative \par \par \uc2  effects. \par \par \uc2  Talks between Hynix Semiconductor and Germany's Infineon \par \par \uc2  Technologies were also likely to provide a boost to the won. \par \par \uc2  While an Infineon Japan spokesman said the talks were not \par \par \uc2  necessarily about a tie-up, some sort of cooperative agreement \par \par \uc2  could be possible. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                              SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar drifted towards the weaker end of its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par familiar range in early trade as it shadowed an ailing yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers expected the Sing dollar to move between 1.8360 and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.8460 against the dollar, edging softer in intraday trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dollar buy orders from major banks were lining up around the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.8380 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  players who took short positions on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/Sing on Thursday were beginning to assume long dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But, capital inflows into the Singapore stock market, which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closed on a 10-month high on Thursday, should give the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a boost later in the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso tracked the regionals lower, opening at 51.30 to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar compared with 51.235 at the close on Thursday. At\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0125 GMT, the market turnover was $21 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But its downside was supported by improved sentiment after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par key economic data beat forecast. The country's GDP grew 3.4\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent on the year in 2001 against a 3.075 percent growth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forecast by economists polled by Reuters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Exporters and interbank players sold the U.S. dollar around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the morning low of 51.325 and dealers believed 51.350 should be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a good support for the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at this point.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht succumbed to the 44 level once again, with early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar bids on the back of the yen's falls driving it lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dealers described the buying as across-the-board,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but added it had lost some of its momentum around the 44.10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level as the yen regained some balance.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, while the baht was enjoying equity-related inflows,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dealers expected to trade towards the 44.30 level - last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seen on December 28 - as the yen continued to struggle.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There's no reason for a stronger baht. It's going to start\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hurting their exports," said a European bank dealer in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government said its current account surplus stood at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $1.022 billion at the end of December versus November's $556\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million surplus.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah held steady around 10,300 to the dollar in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lethargic early trade as flooding paralysed the islands of Java\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and Bali after three days of monsoons.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said corporate demand for dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par existed below the 10,300 level. They expect the rupiah to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weaken slightly against the dollar in intraday trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The bottom line is that the dollar/rupiah still needs to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par go up," a Singapore-based dealer at an American bank said,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par adding that other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should also reflect a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bullish dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar opened a touch easier at 35.032 against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Thursday close of 34.980 on the back of a weaker yen which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tracked closely because Japan and Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compete in a similar export market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, its losses are likely to be limited by capital\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows and seasonal dollar sales by exporters, especially\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of the Chinese New Year next month, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors were net buyers of T$695 million\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (US$19.86 million in local stocks on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I don't thing it (the Taiwan dollar) will stray from its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent range. It will be wedged between exporter dollar offers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the yen as well as fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said a dealer in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was rumoured to have bought around $80\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million during the last minute trading on Thursday to curb the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's appreciation.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0139 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     134.54       132.97         -1.17\par  Sing dlr      1.8376       1.8280         -0.52\par  Taiwan dlr    35.035       34.980         -0.16\par  Korean won   1323.70      1314.30         -0.71\par  Baht           44.08        43.98         -0.23\par  Peso           51.20        51.24         +0.07\par  Rupiah      10310.00     10300.00         -0.10\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     134.54       131.24         -2.45\par  Sing dlr      1.8376       1.8515         +0.76\par  Taiwan dlr    35.035       34.986         -0.14\par  Korean won   1304.40      1313.00         +0.66\par  Baht           44.08        44.16         +0.18\par  Peso           51.20        51.50         +0.59\par  Rupiah      10310.00     10350.00         +0.39\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020201dy21003pd\