\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Take heart from recovery hopes. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,077 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2002\par 10:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 31 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  retained their earlier gains on Thursday as market players took \par \par \uc2  the Federal Reserve's decision to hold interest rates steady to \par \par \uc2  mean the world economy had bottomed. \par \par \uc2      The Fed ended its year-long easing campaign, keeping the \par \par \uc2  benchmark fed funds rate at 1.75 percent but warned there is \par \par \uc2  still a risk of weakness in the economy. \par \par \uc2      The dollar failed to find much support from the Fed's \par \par \uc2  decision, partly because Japanese officials have toned down \par \par \uc2  their rhetoric on the yen. \par \par \uc2      "It is the very weakness of the local asset market that \par \par \uc2  appears to have caused Japanese policy makers to tone down \par \par \uc2  their rhetoric for fear of a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  coupled with \par \par \uc2  weakening equities and bonds causing investors to flee Japan en \par \par \uc2  masse," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS \par \par \uc2  Warburg. \par \par \uc2      "We continue to be short dollar/yen from 133.90 looking for \par \par \uc2  a return towards 130.00. We do note however that fundamentals \par \par \uc2  remain weak with banking shares and JGBs continuing to falter," \par \par \uc2  he said in a note. \par \par \uc2      The yen was hovering around 133.00 to the dollar. Charts \par \par \uc2  show the dollar/yen is trapped in a downtrend channel dating \par \par \uc2  back to January 28. \par \par \uc2      The Institute of International Finance forecast in its \par \par \uc2  latest report that private capital inflows into Asia should \par \par \uc2  pick up to $53.1 billion this year from around $44.4 billion \par \par \uc2  estimated for 2001. \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2      The Sing dollar was among the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  advancing against the U.S. dollar in a sluggish market as it \par \par \uc2  tracked a more buoyant yen and was helped by investment flowing \par \par \uc2  into the stock market . \par \par \uc2      Dealers said a midday break of 1.8300 prompted some \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players to cut long dollar positions. But corporates \par \par \uc2  eager to buy cheaper dollars pushed the U.S. dollar/Sing back \par \par \uc2  near that level. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) was rumoured to \par \par \uc2  be stepping in recently to slow the Sing dollar's appreciation, \par \par \uc2  which could hurt the export-driven recovery effort. \par \par \uc2       THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2      The baht was pushed higher by players betting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate on the back of a \par \par \uc2  steadier yen. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said there were no signs of \par \par \uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the baht touched a 10-day high of \par \par \uc2  43.87 per dollar, aided by equity-related and export inflows. \par \par \uc2      But local commercial demand for the dollar and wariness \par \par \uc2  over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  made most players \par \par \uc2  reluctant to push the baht higher. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  upgraded its growth projection saying the \par \par \uc2  economy will grow 2-3 percent in 2002, against an October \par \par \uc2  prediction of 1-3 percent. The economy grew an estimated 1.5 \par \par \uc2  percent in 2001. \par \par \uc2      INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2      The rupiah barely budged from its range around 10,300 \par \par \uc2  level, with trading activity subdued as floods paralysed \par \par \uc2  transport and communications in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2      However, dealers in Singapore said the bias was for a \par \par \uc2  modestly stronger rupiah given a lack of commercial demand and \par \par \uc2  an improved economic outlook with lower interest rates. \par \par \uc2      The benchmark one-month SBI rate eased to 16.93 percent in \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's auction, from 17.09 percent the previous week. \par \par \uc2   KOREAN WON \par \par \uc2      The won ended the day slightly lower with the shaky yen \par \par \uc2  overshadowing foreign net purchases of 15 billion won worth of \par \par \uc2  local stocks. \par \par \uc2      Earlier in the day, the won was in an upbeat mood thanks to \par \par \uc2  growing relief over signs that the U.S. economy was indeed on \par \par \uc2  the mend and the infectious cheer in the stock market. \par \par \uc2      But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fortunes began to sour, with \par \par \uc2  profit-taking driving the local stock market lower and the yen \par \par \uc2  taking a turn for the worse. \par \par \uc2      Singapore dealers added that genuine dollar demand from \par \par \uc2  importers also emerged around the 1,305 level. Charts also \par \par \uc2  showed the dollar/won had been on the verge of being overbought \par \par \uc2  with a 14-day relative strength index reading of around 35 on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      "It's obvious -- this is not a good level to sell at," said \par \par \uc2  a Singapore dealer at a European bank, noting that some players \par \par \uc2  had taken long-dollar positions ahead of the dollar's sharp 1.6 \par \par \uc2  percent correction from January 23 to its present levels. Data \par \par \uc2  released earlier showed headline inflation rising in January by \par \par \uc2  2.6 percent year-on-year, which may signal the end of the Bank \par \par \uc2  of Korea's rate-cutting cycle. \par \par \uc2      TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2      The Taiwan dollar was virtually flat from Wednesday's \par \par \uc2  34.985 close, caught between the battling influences of the \par \par \uc2  unsteady yen and gains in local stocks. \par \par \uc2      Trading was sluggish in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the range was a \par \par \uc2  tight 34.94-34.98. Singapore dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \par \par \uc2  curbing the Taiwan dollar's gains in its regular attempt to \par \par \uc2  keep the exchange rate along the straight and narrow. \par \par \uc2      PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2      The Philippine peso closed at 51.235 against the dollar, \par \par \uc2  compared with 51.220 on Wednesday after spending the day in a \par \par \uc2  tight range between 51.21 and 51.26. \par \par \uc2      Trading was brisk, with $110 million changing hands. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Manila and Singapore said the peso shrugged off \par \par \uc2  news the country's GDP grew 3.4 percent in the fourth quarter, \par \par \uc2  beating market and government expectations. \par \par \uc2      "The positive news has already been priced into the peso," \par \par \uc2  a Singapore-based dealer at an American bank said. \par \par \uc2      They said all the action was onshore, with corporates \par \par \uc2  buying dollars at the cheaper range to pay off debts. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  084