\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mixed up between Fed and yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,190 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2002\par 02:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 31 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were torn \par \par \uc2  early on Thursday between the Federal Reserve's affirmation \par \par \uc2  that the U.S. economy was picking up and a stagnating yen. \par \par \uc2      The Federal Open Market Committee left interest rates \par \par \uc2  steady at the end of its two-day meeting. \par \par \uc2      While the decision to leave rates alone was widely \par \par \uc2  expected, U.S. stock markets were relieved to see the Fed \par \par \uc2  joining the ranks of those who believe the U.S. economy is on \par \par \uc2  the road to recovery. \par \par \uc2  "What it means is that the Fed has helped lay the \par \par \uc2  groundwork for the U.S. recovery with its previous cuts...that \par \par \uc2  could lead to some spillover buying of Asian stocks, which \par \par \uc2  would give some of the regionals some support," said Thio Chin \par \par \uc2  Loo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      "But given how the yen and euro are struggling, the \par \par \uc2  dollar/Sing could reassert itself," she added. \par \par \uc2      The Fed's move to suspend its aggressive rate-cutting spree \par \par \uc2  gave the dollar a leg-up against the other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The yen gave up some of its 0.64 percent gains on Wednesday \par \par \uc2  in early Asian trade, slipping beyond the 133 level. \par \par \uc2      The yen's fragility continued to dampen Asia's outlook, \par \par \uc2  which would have been brighter given the expected rebound in \par \par \uc2  the U.S., its largest export market. The Institute of \par \par \uc2  International Finance warned on Wednesday in a report that the \par \par \uc2  weaker yen threatened growth and capital flows into Asia. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won rose for the sixth day in a row as giddy spirits in \par \par \uc2  the local stock market dominated the mood in the market. \par \par \uc2  Korean shares were up one percent, taking heart \par \par \uc2  along with their U.S. counterparts the Fed's decision to sit \par \par \uc2  tight on rates amid signs that the U.S. economy was improving. \par \par \uc2  Exporters' dollar sales at month-end also gave the won a \par \par \uc2  boost, as did a report in a local newspaper that Kumho \par \par \uc2  Industrial Co. was likely to announce the sale of \par \par \uc2  its tire \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a consortium led by U.S. private equity \par \par \uc2  fund, the Carlyle Group. \par \par \uc2  However, charts showed the dollar/won veering into \par \par \uc2  overbought territory with a 14-day relative strength index \par \par \uc2  reading of around 35 on Wednesday. That could bring some \par \par \uc2  support for the dollar in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Korea reported January inflation crept up 2.6 percent \par \par \uc2  versus a year ago and 0.6 percent from the previous month, in \par \par \uc2  line with expectations. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar bobbed around the middle of its recent \par \par \uc2  1.8300-1.8370 range in early trade as it looked for new \par \par \uc2  direction. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Fed's announcement had little effect on \par \par \uc2  the Sing dollar because the market had already factored in the \par \par \uc2  decision. They expected it to trade between 1.8320-1.8370. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar market continued to track the movements in \par \par \uc2  the dollar/yen. Still, the domestic dollar's upside was capped \par \par \uc2  by talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy \par \par \uc2  dollars at 1.83 to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating. A \par \par \uc2  strong Sing dollar would make exports, which account for about \par \par \uc2  70 percent of Singapore's GDP, less competitive. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said charts showed the dollar would be \par \par \uc2  well-supported around 1.8270, which it managed to avoid \par \par \uc2  breaking from December 6-December 14.. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht edged higher above the 44 per dollar level on \par \par \uc2  equity-related inflows and was further aided by the steadier \par \par \uc2  tone in the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But dealers in Singapore said most players still fear the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might start buying dollars around these levels to \par \par \uc2  cap the baht's rise. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said on Wednesday that \par \par \uc2  the budget deficit for fiscal year starting in October would be \par \par \uc2  cut to 175 billion baht from 200 billion baht this year. \par \par \uc2  He said Thailand could not rely solely on fiscal spending \par \par \uc2  to fuel economic recovery and more monetary measures would be \par \par \uc2  unveiled by the Bank of Thailand to kick-start growth. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had twice cut its benchmark 14-day repo \par \par \uc2  rate by a total of 50 basis points to 2.00 percent. \par \par \uc2      The bank is due to release its monthly economic indicators \par \par \uc2  for December and its quarterly report on inflation later in the \par \par \uc2  day. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah held on its range around 10,300 level with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading activity subdued after heavy rains and floods paralysed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par transport and communications in Jakarta.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said the rupiah is expected to trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par within 10,250-1,350 range for now but a lack of commercial\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand could push it higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The benchmark one-month SBI interest rate eased to 16.93\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in Wednesday's auction, from 17.09 percent in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par previous week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso opened lower against the dollar while\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market waited for two key figures from the government.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Manila dealers said the market was waiting for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Philippines' fourth quarter 2001 GDP due at 0200 GMT. Some said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par an annual rise of 3.0-3.7 percent would be bullish for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par peso, and a number below that range would prompt the peso to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fall.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Reuters poll of 10 economists suggested the country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fourth quarter GDP was likely to have expanded 3.06 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from the previous year. The government target is 3.3 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Players also waited for the Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decision on interest rates. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said earlier in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the day it would still consider a rate cut despite the Fed's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par move to hold rates steady.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar rose thanks to rises in the local stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market and expectations of more exporters' dollar sales.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, the market was well-aware that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was likely to curb the Taiwan dollar's gains, especially in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par light of the still wobbly yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  usually feels upward pressure ahead of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Lunar New Year because local companies need the Taiwan dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to pay out bonuses to their employees. Analysts said the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was even more likely to step into the market to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ensure a stable exchange rate.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0139 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     132.75       132.71         -0.03\par  Sing dlr      1.8320       1.8318         -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    34.960       34.985         +0.07\par  Korean won   1306.40      1311.00         +0.35\par  Baht           43.95        43.99         +0.09\par  Peso           51.24        51.22         -0.04\par  Rupiah      10325.00     10305.00         -0.19\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Lat