\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Yen cheers despite stock losses. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,085 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2002\par 09:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 30 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  notched \par \par \uc2  higher late on Wednesday with the yen's gains providing \par \par \uc2  encouragement despite falls on the U.S. equity markets. \par \par \uc2      Trading was relatively subdued ahead of the U.S. Federal \par \par \uc2  Open Market Committee's rate announcement expected later in the \par \par \uc2  day. The market isn't expecting a rate cut, but was hoping for \par \par \uc2  a good prognosis on the U.S. economy from the Fed. \par \par \uc2  The market also remained largely focused on the yen, which \par \par \uc2  shot past the 133 level on a report in the Wall Street Journal \par \par \uc2  that U.S. auto giant General Motors was complaining to the Bush \par \par \uc2  administration about attempts to weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  The Korea won saw the most volatile trade, opening lower at \par \par \uc2  1,319 before the yen's strength managed to pull it back towards \par \par \uc2  1,311, flat from Tuesday's close. The won has gained some 1.8 \par \par \uc2  percent in a week, making it the region's leader in recent \par \par \uc2  sessions. \par \par \uc2  The other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  paled in comparison, with many of the \par \par \uc2  Southeast Asian regionals merely trading in the higher end of \par \par \uc2  their recent ranges. But analysts said they expected that to \par \par \uc2  change in the long term because the U.S. recovery is expected \par \par \uc2  to show more signs of health. \par \par \uc2  "The other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  really haven't taken off like the \par \par \uc2  yen. But that should change because we're expecting more good \par \par \uc2  U.S. data, which should be welcome news for the regionals," \par \par \uc2  said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg in \par \par \uc2  Singapore. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  Despite a sell-off in local stocks on Wednesday, the won \par \par \uc2  managed to track the yen higher. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also boosted \par \par \uc2  by capital inflows into the local bond market. \par \par \uc2  The won closed at 1310.90 to the dollar against 1318.50 at \par \par \uc2  the open and 1313.60 at the close on Tuesday. Foreigners \par \par \uc2  emerged as net sellers of Korean stocks, sending the benchmark \par \par \uc2  KOSPI index slipping 3.18 percent to close at 749.45. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained around 1.80 percent in a week, \par \par \uc2  which is considered a sharp move in Asia's context, and dealers \par \par \uc2  said it should be top heavy going forward. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar rose alongside the yen, but the local \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was top heavy at around 1.8320 amid talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have recently stepped in to slow its appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Despite being rangebound in the past few sessions, the Sing \par \par \uc2  dollar has gained more than one percent since the end of last \par \par \uc2  year, making it the best performing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  year-to-date. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say the next key level is 1.8300 where hefty \par \par \uc2  stop-loss U.S. dollar selling orders are lining up. Charts show \par \par \uc2  that a break above that level will take the Sing dollar out of \par \par \uc2  its recent consolidative phase, indicating further upside \par \par \uc2  ahead. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht edged above the 44 level aided by a steadier \par \par \uc2  regional tone and portfolio-related inflows. \par \par \uc2      But fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \par \par \uc2  commercial demand for the dollar capped its upside. \par \par \uc2      The market has been rife with talk that the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Thailand was seeking to buy dollars to increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  reserves and keep the baht's competitive edge. \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  dealers said they believed the bank had repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  above the 44 level. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Thailand will raise this week its 2002 economic growth forecast \par \par \uc2  to 2-3 percent from 1-3 percent, saying the upbeat forecast was \par \par \uc2  based on the improving global economic outlook and the Thai \par \par \uc2  economy's better performance in the last quarter of 2001. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah held steady around 10,300, off its early \par \par \uc2  three-week high of 10,250 where local corporates were spotted \par \par \uc2  bidding for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said overall trading interest and \par \par \uc2  volumes were low as most of Jakarta was inundated by floods \par \par \uc2  after heavy monsoon rains that paralysed air, road and rail \par \par \uc2  transport. \par \par \uc2  The IMF issued a statement after its board approved the \par \par \uc2  latest $341 million instalment under the nation's $4.5 billion \par \par \uc2  loan programme, urging Indonesia to renew efforts to reform its \par \par \uc2  economy and take the needed steps to boost investor confidence \par \par \uc2  and reduce poverty. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso closed lower at 51.22 after meandering \par \par \uc2  in a familiar 51.17-51.25 range in the absence of clear \par \par \uc2  direction. \par \par \uc2  Trading was brisk with $136 million changing hands. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said most of the market action came from \par \par \uc2  corporates buying the greenback below the 51.20 level to pay \par \par \uc2  off dollar debts. The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumoured to \par \par \uc2  be also buying dollars at similar levels to pay their bills. \par \par \uc2  Marginal gains in the Philippine stock market on Wednesday \par \par \uc2  supported the peso, one of the most stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \par \par \uc2  region. The main Manila index closed 0.21 percent higher at \par \par \uc2  1,301.11. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said gross domestic product data for the fourth \par \par \uc2  quarter of 2001 due on Thursday should offer the dollar/peso \par \par \uc2  market something new to chew on. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar rose above the 35 level in line with the \par \par \uc2  yen and won. \par \par \uc2  But its rise was much more tempered given the market's \par \par \uc2  wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  has been on both sides of the market on a regular basis to \par \par \uc2  maintain a stable rate. \par \par \uc2      And dealers expected it to be even more keen to keep the \par \par \uc2  rate steady ahead of the Lunar New Year holidays. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0833 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     132.71       133.09         +0.29\par  Sing dlr      1.8318       1.8325         +0.04\par  Taiwan dlr    34.985       35.001         +0.05\par  Korean won   1311.00      1313.60         +0.15\par  Baht           43.99        44.01         +0.05\par  Peso           51.22        51.17         -0.10\par  Rupiah      10305.00     10315.00         +0.10\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     132.71       131.24         -1.11\par  Sing dlr      1.8318       1.8515         +1.08\par  Taiwan dlr    34.985       34.986         +0.00\par  Korean won   1303.60      1313.00         +0.72\par  Baht           43.99        44.16         +0.39\par  Peso           51.22        51.50         +0.56\par  Rupiah      10305.00     10350.00         +0.44\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020130dy1u00han\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
