\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Up Late; Some Central Banks Check Gains \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2 887 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2002\par 10:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  basked in the glow of the yen's rebound late Tuesday, although dealers believe the central banks in Taiwan, \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Thailand had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the strength of their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market watchers said. \par \par \uc2  In recent sessions, portfolio inflows had mitigated the pain on the New Taiwan dollar, Singapore dollar and Thai baht from the yen's slide to new 39-month lows versus the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the euro's weakness, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Given the appreciation of these Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against their major trading counterparts, the region's central banks are probably concerned about the strength of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a trade-weighted basis, they added. The authorities would need to maintain the price competitiveness of their exports. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was stronger at S$1.8325 against its U.S. counterpart, compared with S$1.8363 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore had been bidding for U.S. dollars since Monday kept the unit buoyed above S$1.8300, even as the yen threatened to approach the Y133 psychological resistance level to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Any further strength could push the Singapore dollar into more expensive area against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its trading partners," BNP Paribas said in a report. "This would run against the authority's current bias of maintaining a neutral \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar against its basket." \par \par \uc2  "We expect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue if portfolio-led \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar demand continues to push up the value of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the bank added. \par \par \uc2  At 0854 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at Y133.20, below Y133.50 in New York late Monday. The dollar was at Y133.86 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  In the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the dollar failed to stay below 44 baht, amid talk that the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying dollars sporadically via its agent banks in Bangkok and Singapore since Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have bought dollars when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded between THB43.990 and THB44.050, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The amount should be substantial," said a dealer at an Asian bank in Singapore. "They came in a few times and they're still there." \par \par \uc2  In fact, dealers believe that the Bank of Thailand has been curbing the strength of the baht almost daily in the last two weeks, in an apparent bid to maintain the price competitiveness of the country's exports. \par \par \uc2  "We think that there has been a shift in policy thinking at the BOT from a focus on "stability" - through managing interest rate differentials and exchange rates (through the latter half of 2001) - to more conventional counter-cyclical 'growth-oriented' measures," Bank of America said in a research note. \par \par \uc2  "We expect the authorities to consciously guide the baht lower against its nominal effective basket, to boost exports," the bank said, adding that the dollar will likely be well supported around THB43.900 to THB43.950. \par \par \uc2  In Taiwan, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reportedly bought U.S. dollars around NT$34.980, offsetting the pressure from the exporter U.S. dollar sales and the yen's rise, Taipei-based dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ended at NT$35.001, marginally lower than NT$35.015 Monday. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won closed at a two-week high, receiving an additional boost from dollar demand by foreign investors needing to settle their recent purchases of local shares, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The won also gained from the unwinding of long dollar positions by foreign funds - triggered by the dollar's fall below the psychologically important KRW1,320 level - and jitters about the yen, with "dollar/yen hanging precariously above Y133," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  "Offshore players are coming in and selling dollar/won for speculative reasons as well," noted Mansoor Mohi-uddin, a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg. \par \par \uc2  Remarks by international ratings agency Fitch that there is room for an upgrade in South Korea's sovereign ratings also boosted sentiment toward the won. \par \par \uc2  "It helped sentiment - definitely," said Mohi-uddin. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at 1,313.6 won, down 0.6% from KRW1,321.3 Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah received a fillip from the International Monetary Fund's approval of a loan installment of $341 million for the country and its agreement to extend a $4.5-billion loan facility by a year to the end of 2003. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah also received another dose of good news - that a Standard Chartered Plc. (U.STA)-led consortium appeared to be the front runner in bidding for a stake in nationalized PT Bank Central Asia (P.PCA). \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to 10,295 rupiah to the dollar from IDR10,390 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine Dealing System, the dollar closed at 51.165 pesos, down from PHP51.240 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Financial markets are awaiting the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision on interest rates at the end of its two-day policy-setting meeting, which begins later Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Markets have priced in expectations that the Fed will hold its overnight target rate steady at 1.75%, which would end a year-long streak of aggressive easing. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4043; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020129dy1t000ig\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
