\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Yen drives regionals lower. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,099 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2002\par 03:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 9 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell under \par \par \uc2  the sickly yen's spell early on Wednesday, though the degree of \par \par \uc2  their losses has yet to match the yen's. \par \par \uc2      Compared with the yen's 0.29 percent decline from Monday's \par \par \uc2  levels in late Asian trade, the Singapore dollar has only ceded \par \par \uc2  0.11 percent and the Thai baht 0.18 percent. \par \par \uc2      Analysts say the chief reasons for the slightly more \par \par \uc2  subdued reaction from regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the yen this time \par \par \uc2  around are capital inflows, primarily into North Asia, and the \par \par \uc2  fact that most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have corrected substantially \par \par \uc2  since the Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  That said, they emphasise that the yen still wields huge \par \par \uc2  influence over regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it plays a \par \par \uc2  significant part in their trade-weighted baskets. Analysts \par \par \uc2  reckon the yen holds an 11-15 percent weighting in the \par \par \uc2  trade-weighted basket for the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  With little other fresh leads, the market was likely to \par \par \uc2  remain riveted on the yen's movements, and to whether Japan's \par \par \uc2  neighbours may express alarm. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  received a drubbing \par \par \uc2  late on Monday after comments from senior Japanese officials \par \par \uc2  that the market interpreted as giving a green light for a \par \par \uc2  weaker yen. \par \par \uc2  Faced with an economy that has slipped into recession \par \par \uc2  again, Japan's government seems to be taking the option of \par \par \uc2  trying to export its way out of trouble, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was wrestling with the 1.8500 level, \par \par \uc2  and found itself being defeated by the wobbly yen. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said the Singapore dollar was able to \par \par \uc2  avoid its early morning lows of around 1.8525 because some \par \par \uc2  players were still trying to unload long dollar positions from \par \par \uc2  last week. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also been able to avoid more severe losses \par \par \uc2  because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's decision last \par \par \uc2  week to narrow its trading band for the trade-weighted Sing \par \par \uc2  dollar. Analysts said they view that move as an indication of \par \par \uc2  renewed confidence in the city-state's economy and less \par \par \uc2  tolerance for exchange rate volatility. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won followed the shaky yen in its downward path, \par \par \uc2  gapping lower to 1,315.5 from Tuesday's close of 1,309.5. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to outperform the yen, with the \par \par \uc2  yen/won cross-rate at levels not seen since July \par \par \uc2  1999 and well below what many analysts had believed was the \par \par \uc2  government's threshold because of concerns over export \par \par \uc2  competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  The cross-rate's fall has prompted analysts to take the \par \par \uc2  view the government may be becoming more tolerant of a stronger \par \par \uc2  won against the yen because of capital inflows and a brighter \par \par \uc2  outlook for the Korean economy. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  official from the Finance Ministry told \par \par \uc2  Reuters on Tuesday that while the government is monitoring the \par \par \uc2  won closely, it does not have a target for the yen/won rate and \par \par \uc2  respects market consensus. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar edged lower with the regional trend and \par \par \uc2  on talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken \par \par \uc2  further in line with the yen's recent losses. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar touched a low of 35.16 per dollar early \par \par \uc2  on, compared with 35.038 at the close of onshore trade on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said some support was expected from \par \par \uc2  equity-related inflows but overall the market would keep its \par \par \uc2  focus on moves in the yen. \par \par \uc2      A weaker yen raises competitiveness concerns as Taiwan \par \par \uc2  competes with Japan in several export markets. \par \par \uc2      Foreign investors were net buyers of T$5.9 billion of local \par \par \uc2  shares on Tuesday, taking net purchases in the past seven \par \par \uc2  sessions to T$33 billion. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah lingered around 10,430, wedged in between rising\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar demand from local corporates and fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said suspected dollar sales by the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state banks on Monday had sparked rumours\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would not allow the rupiah to slip beyond\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10,500 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, local corporates have kept the dollar supported\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with strong bids at around 10,400, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht found a toehold below the 44 level, tracking the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen and the regionals lower. Dealers cited talk of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  buying the U.S. dollar regularly recently to meet its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign debt requirement.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I heard the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has bought regularly recently,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around $20-30 million each time. I don't think the objective is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to keep the baht weak but to meet its dollar debt requirement,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said a dealer in Bangkok.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Otherwise, the baht should be well-supported around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 44.15-44.20 where dollar selling orders are lining up, said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bangkok and Singapore dealers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar gains are likely to be dented also by rising\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht funding costs. In the offshore market, the one-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forward rate rose to 10/15 satang per dollar from around 8/10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par satang late on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso was down tracking a weaker yen and other regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Manila said the Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rumoured to be selling dollars in early trading to prevent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par volatility in the exchange rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They also said the intraday range for the dollar/peso was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to be about 51.60 to 51.75, with further possible\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hits a high of 135 against the yen, which would prompt the bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to further weaken the peso to maintain export competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Local corporate dollar demand has yet to emerge in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Volume on the Philippine Dealing System was relatively thin\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at around $23 million.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0229 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     132.70       132.59         -0.08\par  Sing dlr      1.8501       1.8490         -0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    35.100       35.038         -0.18\par  Korean won   1299.50      1309.50         +0.77\par  Baht           44.13        44.04         -0.19\par  Peso           51.67        51.68         +0.02\par  Rupiah      10425.00     10420.00         -0.05\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     132.70       131.24         -1.10\par  Sing dlr      1.8501       1.8515         +0.08\par  Taiwan dlr    35.100       34.986         -0.32\par  Korean won   1299.50      1313.00         +1.04\par  Baht           44.13        44.16         +0.08\par  Peso           51.67        51.50         -0.33\par  Rupiah      10425.00     10350.00         -0.72\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020109dy19005eo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
