\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Sing, Taiwan dollars wilt, eyes on central banks. \b0\par\par\uc2 979 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2001\par 11:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Dec 27 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  shuddered as \par \par \uc2  the yen fell through key levels against the dollar on \par \par \uc2  Thursday, sparking fears central banks in the region may step \par \par \uc2  in to curb the pace of decline. \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar sank to a new 11-year low while the \par \par \uc2  Taiwan dollar slipped to fresh 15-year troughs as importers and \par \par \uc2  corporates scrambled to hedge their future dollar requirements \par \par \uc2  amid talk the yen could hit 135 level in days. \par \par \uc2      The yen slipped to a three-year low of 131.75 after \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials said its weakness was justified by \par \par \uc2  fundamentals, with more pressure coming from players seeking \par \par \uc2  settlements as Thursday was the last trading day for the year. \par \par \uc2      But dealers expected the yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \uc2  regain some lost ground in the near future. \par \par \uc2      "Given the speed with which the dollar/yen has \par \par \uc2  moved....there is a possibility of a sharp retracement," said \par \par \uc2  Peter Redward, Deutsche Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist in \par \par \uc2  Singapore. \par \par \uc2      A weaker yen stirs up concerns across the region with \par \par \uc2  Korea, Taiwan and Singapore seen more vulnerable due to the \par \par \uc2  similarity of their exports and markets with those of Japan. \par \par \uc2      However, analysts said most central banks in the region \par \par \uc2  might see weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as less stimulating for exports and \par \par \uc2  more damaging for the real economy. Therefore, any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  is likely for the sake of financial stability. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was lower, although it managed to come off \par \par \uc2  its fresh 11-year lows on option-related purchases and fears of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had earlier fallen to 1.8530 - its \par \par \uc2  worst level since June 30, 1990 when it hit 1,8540 - due to a \par \par \uc2  weaker yen and the country's bleak economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some banks were buying the Sing dollar to stop \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling to 1.8600 where their options would \par \par \uc2  be triggered. Apart from fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \par \par \uc2  option-linked buying, there is little else to support for the \par \par \uc2  local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Recent economic data painted a gloomy picture, with its \par \par \uc2  non-oil exports shrinking 21.1 percent on the year in November \par \par \uc2  and its manufacturing output contracting 13.60 percent in the \par \par \uc2  same month. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar ended at 15-year lows against the dollar, \par \par \uc2  weighed down by the yen and other regionals. It finished at \par \par \uc2  35.127, the lowest close since 35.140 reached on January 21, \par \par \uc2  1987, according to data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the market on \par \par \uc2  Thursday by announcing it would cut key interest rates by \par \par \uc2  another 0.125 percentage points. \par \par \uc2  Market participants had earlier speculated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep the borrowing costs unchanged to support the \par \par \uc2  local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the backdrop of a weaker yen. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won tracked the yen down to a low of 1,331.0, the \par \par \uc2  lowest level since on April 16 when it hit a low of 1,334.0. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said the yen's decline and talk of \par \par \uc2  further downside has sent importers and corporates seeking to \par \par \uc2  cover their dollar requirements. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile exporters, who had sold dollars earlier for their \par \par \uc2  year-end requirements, were holding back to wait for more \par \par \uc2  attractive levels. \par \par \uc2  But the won's losses were trimmed by market wariness of \par \par \uc2  potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after recent comments by government \par \par \uc2  officials against excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah eased to the wrong side of the 10,300, pushing a \par \par \uc2  three-week low of 10,350, as interbank players marked down the \par \par \uc2  local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the backdrop of weaker regionals. \par \par \uc2  But dealers in Jakarta said commercial demand for the \par \par \uc2  dollar from local corporates and importers tapered off ahead of \par \par \uc2  the year-end, which helped limit the rupiah's downside. \par \par \uc2      Bank Indonesia was not been in the market, but dealers do \par \par \uc2  not rule out the possibility if the rupiah falls further. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht sank to its one-month lows of 44.24 after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weaker yen sparked short covering in the U.S. dollar among\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interbank players, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But charts show the baht should be well-supported around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 44.25 which represents the 50 percent retracement of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar's October 25-December 13 downmove.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar's further gains should also be restrained by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher baht funding costs offshore, with the one-month rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par firming up to 16/18 satang per dollar from 12/28 satang\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earlier.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso closed lower at 51.49 against Wednesday's close of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 51.32 after companies and exporters snapped up the U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to hedge for their future dollar requirements.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Market turnover picked up, with $98.55 million traded\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compared with $56.30 million on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the macro front, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Rafael\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Buenaventura said on Thursday he expected annual inflation rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to come in between 3.9 to 4.3 percent, which some analysts said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par should provide room for further rate cuts.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 