\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yen hurts, Sing dlr near 11-1/2-yr low. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,003 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2001\par 04:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Dec 27 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were dragged \par \par \uc2  lower by the yen in early trade on Thursday, with the Singapore \par \par \uc2  dollar sliding towards its lowest level since mid-1990. \par \par \uc2      The Sing dollar fell to 1.8530 to the U.S. dollar during \par \par \uc2  Asian trading, a whisker away from the 1.8540 level hit on June \par \par \uc2  30, 1990. But it bounced back later on fears of potential \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yen, which is tracked closely by most emerging Asian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dropped to a fresh three-year low of 131.40 to the \par \par \uc2  dollar due to speculation Japan wants a weaker yen to get \par \par \uc2  itself out of its economic mess. \par \par \uc2  The market seemed to ignore comments by a senior minister \par \par \uc2  that it was desirable for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates to move in a \par \par \uc2  stable manner. \par \par \uc2  A sharp weakening of the yen can arguably result in a loss \par \par \uc2  of export competitiveness for other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \par \par \uc2  could spark competitive devaluation across the region. It would \par \par \uc2  also diminish demand from Japan for Asian goods. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said roughly 11 percent of exports from Asian go \par \par \uc2  to Japan, far less than 15 years ago but still a significant \par \par \uc2  portion. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in the region, Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold a \par \par \uc2  quarterly monetary board meeting later in the day. The market \par \par \uc2  is betting the board will keep its rates steady to support the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar managed to clamber off its lows, but the \par \par \uc2  downside risk against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained due to the \par \par \uc2  weak yen and Singapore's gloomy economic outlook, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said interbank players were in the market to cover \par \par \uc2  short U.S. dollar positions, but fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  held \par \par \uc2  them back from pushing the Sing dollar too far too fast. \par \par \uc2  "Our synthesised basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggests there might \par \par \uc2  be some form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (if the Sing fell) below 1.8480. I \par \par \uc2  don't think the U.S. dollar will go much further from here," \par \par \uc2  said a senior dealer at a U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said the Sing dollar was also supported by \par \par \uc2  option-linked buying as some banks were trying to stop the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling to 1.8600 where their options will be \par \par \uc2  triggered. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht fell to a one-month low of around 44.12 on the \par \par \uc2  back of the sliding yen. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since December 13 \par \par \uc2  reversed its upward trend against the U.S. dollar which dated \par \par \uc2  back to October 25. \par \par \uc2  But dealers expected the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be kept within \par \par \uc2  its recent range as most players had already squared their \par \par \uc2  positions for this year. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs in the offshore market were mostly \par \par \uc2  steady, with the one-month rate quoted at 12/28 satang per \par \par \uc2  dollar and the one-year rate at 100/250 satang. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won fell as low as 1,323, a level last seen on April \par \par \uc2  30, as the weakening yen prompted players to hedge their future \par \par \uc2  dollar requirements. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could provide some support to the won, but overall \par \par \uc2  the sentiment was in favour of the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Kim Yong-duk, deputy minister of the Finance Ministry's \par \par \uc2  International Affairs division, said on Wednesday that \par \par \uc2  authorities were concerned about the yen's steep fall and could \par \par \uc2  take action if necessary to stabilise the won. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar edged lower following the weaker tone of \par \par \uc2  the yen and the won. \par \par \uc2  Analysts believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not cut its key \par \par \uc2  rates when it holds its quarterly meeting later in the day to \par \par \uc2  review monetary policy on concerns cheaper borrowing costs may \par \par \uc2  further hurt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar fell to a low of 35.20 last week, its \par \par \uc2  weakest since July 11 when it set a 2001 low of 35.30. It \par \par \uc2  touched a session low of 35.173 early on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said players were reluctant to take \par \par \uc2  aggressive positions and would be closely watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate decision expected to be announced at a press \par \par \uc2  conference due at 0900 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Charts also showed the U.S. dollar was massively \par \par \uc2  overbought, with the 14-day relative strength index reading \par \par \uc2  99.169. This highlights the risk of a downward correction of \par \par \uc2  the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was down from late Wednesday levels as interbank \par \par \uc2  players beefed up their long dollar positions given the weak \par \par \uc2  regional bias. \par \par \uc2  But a lack of commercial demand for the dollar and a \par \par \uc2  trickle of inflows from overseas workers and exporters helped \par \par \uc2  limit the peso's losses. Turnover was thin, with only $27.50 \par \par \uc2  million traded so far, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah slipped to the weak side of the 10,200 level, \par \par \uc2  weighed down by rising dollar demand by interbank players \par \par \uc2  worried about the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Dollar sales by exporters for year-end requirements and \par \par \uc2  some equity-related inflows were expected to limit the losses. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Jakarta said players were reluctant to take \par \par \uc2  fresh positions in a lacklustre market thinned by holidays. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     131.22       130.66         -0.43\par  Sing dlr      1.8482       1.8434         -0.26\par  Taiwan dlr    35.143       35.096         -0.13\par  Korean won   1308.00      1298.20         -0.75\par  Baht           44.09        44.04         -0.11\par  Peso           51.35        51.30         -0.09\par  Rupiah      10227.00     10180.00         -0.46\par  Ringgit       3.7995 