\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Dn Late, Revisits 11-Yr Low On Yen Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 685 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2001\par 10:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was down sharply against its U.S. counterpart Friday, after briefly revisiting its previous 11-year low, as the yen plunged to its weakest point in more than three years, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0930 GMT (4:30 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8374, up from S$1.8354 late Thursday. It traded between S$1.8360 and S$1.8435. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar rose sharply in early Asian trading, underpinned by its strong overnight performance against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar rose further against the local dollar as stop-loss buying was triggered above the S$1.8400 mark, and as it popped through the Y129 mark against its Japanese counterpart. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  briefly touched S$1.8435 - the previous 11-year high against the Singapore dollar which it reached last month - in line with its broader gains against the yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. dollar pulled back slightly as commercial sell orders emerged in the afternoon session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Liquidity was thin and trading was muted as market participants wound down their dealings early ahead of the Christmas holidays. \par \par \uc2  Despite the U.S. dollar's sharp rise, dealers said they saw no indication of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to iron out excess volatility in the market. \par \par \uc2  "I think because the move has been slow, we haven't seen any sign of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It's been very gradual and has largely been in line with the other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a senior European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The MAS uses the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than interest rates, as its primary monetary-policy tool in seeking to maintain brisk growth and low inflation. The Singapore dollar is guided within a trading band against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the country's major trading partners. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is expected to retreat further as market participants in Europe and the U.S. are expected to take profit ahead of the weekend, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Support for the U.S. dollar is expected at S$1.8350, with resistance at S$1.8450. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were mostly lower late Friday, as sentiment was hurt by the crisis in Argentina, volatile U.S. Treasurys overnight and higher domestic interbank rates, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Rates moved higher as liquidity in the system tightened ahead of the Christmas holiday season and on unconfirmed talk that rail operator SMRT Corp. needed funds to make payments on its bond issue to the Land Transport Authority, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds was up three basis points at 2.01% while the yield on five-year bonds was flat at 3.36%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds rose two basis points to 3.60% while the yield on 10-year bonds gained one basis point to 3.91%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds was up five basis points at 4.29%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web Site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, the most liquid seven-year swap\par offer closed nine basis points higher at 3.82% while the 10-year swap\par offer closed five basis points higher at 4.10%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps widened slightly to 160\par basis points from 159 basis points late Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank money market, rates were mostly mixed amid the\par tighter liquidity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Friday       Late Thursday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.3750% 0.5000%   0.6875% 0.8125%\par 3-Month           1.1250% 1.2500%   1.0000% 1.1250%\par 1-Year            1.4375% 1.5625%   1.4375% 1.5625%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011221dxcl000jz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
