\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mostly happily treading water. \b0\par\par\uc2 958 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2001\par 09:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Dec 5 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  sat on \par \par \uc2  their hands late on Wednesday, happy to stay in their current \par \par \uc2  ranges while the dollar/yen treaded water. \par \par \uc2      Investors in Korea and the Philippines were starting to \par \par \uc2  turn their attention to their central banks, both of which have \par \par \uc2  meetings on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      Philippine inflation data issued earlier in the day pointed \par \par \uc2  the way towards more rate cuts. On the other hand, the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Korea was expected to keep its rate steady at four percent \par \par \uc2  despite the IMF's recent recommendation of another rate cut. \par \par \uc2  But for the most part, activity in the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  market was subdued with the Christmas holiday season \par \par \uc2  approaching. \par \par \uc2  Players were also lying low on the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, \par \par \uc2  though the dollar was well supported against the yen in light \par \par \uc2  of more dismal data from Japan. \par \par \uc2      The market was looking out for the U.S. non-manufacturing \par \par \uc2  NAPM index due later in the day. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won gathered some more gains thanks to stock inflows,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but still kept to its recent range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors' equity-related flows have been the chief\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par driver behind the won's direction for weeks, with the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shrugging off most economic news. They bought a net 202 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par won of local stocks on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Despite the heartened sentiment in Korea, the government\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said it was too early to claim an economic recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Nevertheless, a recent Reuters poll showed 10 economists\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unanimously expecting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to hold its key\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overnight call rate steady at four percent because of recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par encouraging signs for the economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar bobbed around its recent levels, caught\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between equity inflows and fears over the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said activity was thin with players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par conscious the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was watching the market and ready to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par step in to keep the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in check.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been in the market on an almost daily\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par basis to maintain an exchange rate that is at once competitive\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and stable. Analysts say the huge jump in its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  coffers of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around $5 billion to $121 billion reflects the level of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that has been conducted.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar moved slightly higher in its recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.8310-1.8400 range after players decided to unwind their long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar positions when the greenback failed to break 1.8370.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been hostage to the major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par particularly the yen. With the dollar unable to make much\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par headway against the yen, dealers say the market has not been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par able to find the momentum to push the market either way.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht dawdled in paper-thin offshore trading, with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par onshore market closed for a public holiday. It will reopen on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Charts show the dollar/baht is still trapped in a downtrend\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par channel dating back to October 25, indicating the baht is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to retain its strength in the near term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The pair's immediate resistance is seen at 44.25 which is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 38.2 retracement of the dollar's October 25-November 30\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par downmove.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso traded in a 51.955-51.980 range in a quiet market,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with around $89 million transacted. Dealers in Manila said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market was driven mostly by corporate dollar requirements and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seasonal inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market has largely priced in the possibility that the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will cut interest rates by 25 basis points or cut\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par liquidity reserve requirements, or both, at its policy meeting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Philippine Socio-economic Planning Secretary Dante\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canlas said on Wednesday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could cut benchmark\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates by up to 50 basis points.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par His remark followed lower-than-expected inflation numbers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Consumer prices in the Philippines grew 4.4 percent on the year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in November - their slowest pace so far this year. A Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par poll of 10 economists gave an average forecast of 4.73 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was caught in a tight range around the 10,480\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level with dollar inflows from exporters matching demand from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local corporates in thin trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Jakarta said interbank players were also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reluctant to take aggressive positions due to the low volumes\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and ahead of the holiday season.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chief Economics Minister Dorodjatun Kuntjoro-Jakti said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government aims to push annual economic growth to 6-7 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in coming years, adding that poverty and unemployment would be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hard to cut if GDP growth remained at 3-5 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He said public consumption was expected to remain the major\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par driver for economic growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indonesia's statistics bureau said last month GDP growth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for 2001 would be at least 3.47 percent. The government also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forecast in the 2002 budget economic growth to swell to four\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent from 3.5 percent this year.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0821 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.03       123.59         -0.35\par  Sing dlr      1.8341       1.8331         -0.05\par  Taiwan dlr    34.460       34.461         +0.00\par  Korean won   1269.50      1272.60         +0.24\par  Baht           43.96        43.95         -0.02\par  Peso           51.95        52.01         +0.12\par  Rupiah      10468.00     10430.00         -0.36\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     124.03       114.45         -7.72\par  Sing dlr      1.8341       1.7365         -5.32\par  Taiwan dlr    34.460       32.900         -4.53\par  Korean won   1269.50      1277.00         +0.59\par  Baht           43.96        43.70         -0.59\par  Peso           51.95        50.75         -2.31\par  Rupiah      10468.00      9470.00         -9.53\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011205dxc500m2j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100