\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Soft but helped by yen's rebound. \b0\par\par\uc2 910 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2001\par 10:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Dec 4 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  lying low late on Tuesday but the yen's resilience to \par \par \uc2  another downgrade of Japan's sovereign debt helped limit their \par \par \uc2  downside. \par \par \uc2      The yen held steady in early European trade, off its early \par \par \uc2  lows and showing little lasting impact from a cut in Japan's \par \par \uc2  yen-denominated debt rating to Aa3 from Aa2 by Moody's \par \par \uc2  Investors Service. \par \par \uc2      The yen's rebound from overnight lows helped the Singapore \par \par \uc2  dollar bounce off its session low and capped losses in the won \par \par \uc2  and the Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2      Slowing equity-related foreign inflows, however, kept the \par \par \uc2  won and the baht under pressure while fresh data from the \par \par \uc2  Philippines and Singapore reinforced the negative view on \par \par \uc2  regional economies. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said traders of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be \par \par \uc2  watching for U.S. economic data including the November \par \par \uc2  non-manufacturing NAPM index on Wednesday, weekly jobless \par \par \uc2  claims on Thursday and November jobs on Friday. \par \par \uc2      Most Asian economies need a U.S. rebound before they can \par \par \uc2  recover because of the large share of exports in their gross \par \par \uc2  domestic product, particularly to the United States. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won eased a touch because of local banks buying\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  to pad their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  coffers, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also scared off further gains by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korean authorities, who threatened to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if necessary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A Bank of Korea official told Reuters the bank would step\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in to temper the market if necessary, denying a local newspaper\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par report that quoted an unidentified official as saying the bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would remain out of the market as long as the won stayed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between 1,250-1,300.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, most analysts were of the view that the Bank of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korea was taking an easier view than Taiwan on its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise, allowing the won to appreciate some three percent since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par October 4 as equity-related inflows poured in.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors were net buyers of some 35.1 billion won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of local stocks on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the macro front, the market was starting to turn its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attention to the Bank of Korea's monthly rate-setting meeting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Thursday. A recent Reuters poll showed 10 economists\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unanimously expecting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to hold its overnight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par call rate steady at four percent because of evidence that the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy was on the mend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Still, the IMF said Korea had further room to cut interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates to help spur economic recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar kept close to its recent levels around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 34.46, despite the opposing forces of a weaker yen and gains on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the local stock market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     For weeks, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been keeping the exchange\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate stable to maintain export competitiveness while keeping\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local confidence high. The Taiwan dollar has stuck to a tight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range of 34.4-34.6 since late September.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the huge jump in Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  coffers to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $121 billion was due to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's near daily\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot market.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar bounced off a low of 1.84 as the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar failed to make headway against the yen much beyond the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 124 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said as the yen held out against the dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players booked profits from the Singapore dollar's recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, sentiment was weak on data that showed the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par manufacturing sector shrank for the 10th straight month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore's Purchasing Managers Index for November fell to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 45.9 percent from 47.1 percent in October due to a drop in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par order intakes as domestic demand weakened.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said year-end corporate demand for dollars,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par traditionally seen in December and early January, was expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to cap any significant gains in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept the rupiah within a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tight range, but local corporates were seeking dollars on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par renewed doubts about the government's ability to meet its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fiscal deficit target.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Finance Minister Boediono proposed widening the 2001 budget\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deficit target, a move seen contradictory to recent remarks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par indicating the deficit would be well below the existing target.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT The baht edged below the 44-per-dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level as corporate and interbank traders covered their dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par requirements ahead of a holiday on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Bangkok said the softer yen and other regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  further encouraged players to cover their short\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Financial markets in Thailand will be closed on Wednesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to celebrate King Bhumibol Adulyadej's birthday. They will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reopen on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Talk of more commercial banks cutting their interest rates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after Siam Commercial Bank cut its interest rates by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 25 basis points on Monday also raised uncertainty about baht\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par liquidity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economists say there is room for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par further cut interest rates if it wants to, given the country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tame inflation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand's headline inflation fell to 1.0 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year-on-year in November, its lowest level since February 2000,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par thanks to fast falling oil prices and sluggish domestic demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso slipped below 52 per dollar but found support from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows of remittances from overseas workers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Exports fell 13.5 percent on the year in October but came\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in better than a 15 percent contraction officials had expected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     That raised some cautious hopes that the decline in exports\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was near a bottom. However, analysts said it was too early to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par judge that and the slower fall could just be a blip.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011204dxc400spi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
