\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Helped by yen, hurt by U.S. data. \b0\par\par\uc2 962 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2001\par 03:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 28 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stuck to the \par \par \uc2  safety of recent ranges on Wednesday, unsure whether to cheer \par \par \uc2  the firmer yen or mourn the fall in U.S. consumer confidence. \par \par \uc2      The dollar retreated against the yen and euro after the \par \par \uc2  Conference Board said its index of consumer confidence fell to \par \par \uc2  an unexpected 82.2 in November from 85.3 in October - the \par \par \uc2  fifth straight month of decline. \par \par \uc2  Investors who were jubilant over the prospect of a U.S. \par \par \uc2  recovery in the second half of next year were taken aback by \par \par \uc2  the figure and held off dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  While that was good news for the yen and yen-sensitive \par \par \uc2  regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the fall in U.S. consumer confidence could \par \par \uc2  unnerve markets in Korea and Taiwan, two economies heavily \par \par \uc2  dependent on U.S. exports. \par \par \uc2  Rising hopes for a U.S. recovery and its spillover effect \par \par \uc2  in the region have inspired the recent rally in Asian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar finally mustered some strength thanks \par \par \uc2  to the firmer yen. \par \par \uc2  Since the beginning of the week, the Sing dollar has \par \par \uc2  notably lagged behind the other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , primarily \par \par \uc2  because of its shackles to the yen. However, with the yen \par \par \uc2  safely above 124, the Sing dollar was poised to win back ground \par \par \uc2  against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market could be looking to test 1.83 if \par \par \uc2  the dollar/yen dips further. They added it was still slightly \par \par \uc2  long on the greenback, which could spur further unwinding of \par \par \uc2  long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won opened flat on Wednesday as investors took pause \par \par \uc2  from the recent strong rise both in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock \par \par \uc2  market. Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also dampened \par \par \uc2  sentiment. \par \par \uc2  The won opened at 1,265.2 to the dollar against the \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's close of 1,265.3. The KOSPI came off 1.46 \par \par \uc2  percent, with foreign investors selling a net 37.3 billion won \par \par \uc2  worth of local stocks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect further gains for the won in the near-term \par \par \uc2  following what they believe would be a brief consolidation \par \par \uc2  because dollar demand for foreign debt repayment has dwindled \par \par \uc2  while more capital inflows into local stocks are expected. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was weighed by news of hostage taking and violence \par \par \uc2  in the southern city of Zamboanga which raised concerns over \par \par \uc2  the country's political and security stability. \par \par \uc2      Corporate players continued to buy dollars to settle their \par \par \uc2  contracts in the non-deliverable forward market. \par \par \uc2      Muslim gunmen freed 21 hostages early on Wednesday out of \par \par \uc2  more than 80 they seized following pitched battles with \par \par \uc2  Philippine troops. \par \par \uc2      But losses are likely to be trimmed by remittances from \par \par \uc2  overseas Filipino workers ahead of the Christmas holiday. \par \par \uc2      There are also continued expectations in the market that \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will further lower overnight rates before \par \par \uc2  Christmas provided inflation remains subdued. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht rose to 44.00 overnight but failed to break the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par key psychological level due to fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and dollar bargain hunting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers said they had not heard of any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par during London and New York trading. Foreign names from\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained major buyers of the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht has risen steadily since October 25 and is still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trapped in the dollar's downtrend channel, indicating further\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains are possible.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The one-month forward rate was quoted at 6/8 satang per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar in the offshore market and 2/2.5 satang onshore. The gap\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between offshore and onshore rates was caused by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's regulations which restrict the amount of baht flowing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par into overseas markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah shuffled around just below 10,400, relieved by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par diminishing local corporate dollar demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had little to cheer about. The government\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par posted on Tuesday a 16.5 trillion rupiah budget deficit for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first 10 months of the year. While analysts say it might not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par get worse, they added it was no cause for celebration as the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par target was hit because of the reduction of much-needed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par development spending.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government is scrambling to plug its budget deficit, an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par issue which has been a sore point between Jakarta and its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par donors and lenders who have been frustrated by the slow pace of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reforms and privatisation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar rose from its closing level on Tuesday of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 34.468, though the market was slightly confused by which lead\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to follow.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the positive side, the yen was firmer. But the yen's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par firmness was due to a dip in U.S. consumer confidence, which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has negative implications for Taiwan's exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A gain in the cabinet-level Council of Economic Planning\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and Development's index of leading indicators rose in October\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was another plus point.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said another factor was market perception that the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unlikely to allow the Taiwan dollar to venture\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par far, especially ahead of key parliamentary elections.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.92       124.13         +0.17\par  Sing dlr      1.8335       1.8332         -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr    34.438       34.468         +0.09\par  Korean won   1255.00      1262.50         +0.60\par  Baht           44.10        44.06         -0.09\par  Peso           52.02        52.04         +0.04\par  Rupiah      10430.00     10415.00         -0.14\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Japan yen     123.92       114.45         -7.64\par  Sing dlr      1.8335       1.7365         -5.29\par  Taiwan dlr    34.438       32.900         -4.47\par  Korean won   1255.00      1277.00         +1.75\par  Baht           44.10        43.70         -0.91\par  Peso           52.02        50.75         -2.44\par  Rupiah      10430.00      9470.00         -9.20\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011128dxbs000qb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
