\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Up Late On Fears Of MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2001\par 09:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was stronger against its U.S. counterpart late Tuesday, having pulled back from the previous day's 11-year low, as market players remain fearful of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0836 GMT (3:36 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8381, down from S$1.8427 late Monday when it hit an 11-year low of S$1.8430. It traded in a range between S$1.8370 and S$1.8415. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened lower against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia, after moderate profit-taking by U.S. investment houses out of London overnight, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was then confined to a tight S$1.8395-S$1.8410 range for much of the day as market participants remained wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the MAS and were unable to establish clear U.S. dollar direction against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  So far, there's been no indication that the MAS will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to combat excessive volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Obviously, after yesterday's sharp rise, there will be some consolidation. Maybe it (U.S. dollar) will go back to around S$1.8370 for about one or two days before it shoots up again," a Japanese bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  A Bank of America report said the U.S. dollar was in a consolidation phase against the local dollar, lacking any fresh trading direction. \par \par \uc2  "Interestingly though, there has again been no indication of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest at these levels, which suggests the latter might not necessarily be uncomfortable with further Singapore dollar weakness," the report said. \par \par \uc2  However, the U.S. dollar is expected to resume its rise in overnight trading in London and New York, as the outlook for the U.S. dollar takes on a more positive tone on hopes the fighting in Afghanistan may be close to an end, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is expected to face initial resistance at S$1.8450 and S$1.8500 thereafter, with support at S$1.8370. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were mostly higher as overnight gains in U.S. Treasurys and bargain-hunting helped to lift prices from their recent lows, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds was down 20 basis points at 1.48% while the yield on five-year bonds was down 14 basis points at 2.71%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds was down 17 basis points at 2.99%, while the yield on 10-year bonds was down 12 basis points at 3.42%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds was down 10 basis points at 3.77%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swaps were also mostly lower in\par line with local bond yields.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The most liquid seven-year swap offer closed down 13 basis points at\par 3.40% while the 10-year swap offer also closed down 13 basis points at\par 3.70%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between the two- and 10-year swaps widened to 147 basis\par points from 145 basis points late Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank money market, rates were mostly steady amid ample\par liquidity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Tuesday      Late Monday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.6875% 0.7500%   0.6250% 0.7500%\par 3-Month           1.0625% 1.1875%   1.0625% 1.1875%\par 1-Year            1.3750% 1.5000%   1.3750% 1.5000%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011120dxbk000hp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
