\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP:Singapore Dlr Weakens To 11-Yr Low,Testing MAS Band \b0\par\par\uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2001\par 12:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The U.S. dollar rose to an 11-year high against the Singapore dollar Monday just days after the government unveiled the latest in a series of grim economic indicators and said the near-term outlook is likely to remain dim. \par \par \uc2  In frenetic afternoon trading, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke through key resistance at S$1.8398 and pushed all the way up to S$1.8432, last traded in June 1990. Many analysts said the trend toward a rising dollar is likely to continue, with next resistance pegged at S$1.8440 and then again at S$1.8500. \par \par \uc2  Around 1030 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.8432. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar's decline is the result of concerns about deteriorating economic conditions here combined with uncertainty over monetary policy. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore revised its monetary stance in July to a position calling for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tread water against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , easing the bias from a policy that previously called for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen gradually. \par \par \uc2  Last month, the MAS said it's widening the policy band to allow for more flexibility in managing the exchange rate, though the new band continues to be centered on zero percent appriciation of the Singapore dollar against the basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its major trading partners. \par \par \uc2  "We have already entered a time of greater volatility in dollar/Sing," said Jimmy Koh, head of treasury research at Singapore's UOB Group. "The market is still trying to discover the MAS' threshold of tolerance." \par \par \uc2  The apparent lack of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday gave credence to market talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be comfortable with a weaker local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially if the yen and the euro continue to weaken. \par \par \uc2  The MAS declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, some of the U.S.-dollar buying Monday was a result of the U.S. dollar's strength against the yen, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the Singapore dollar often tracks and one of the key components of the basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is measured against. \par \par \uc2  The dollar pushed up above Y123 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Many observers believe the MAS hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since announcing, on Oct. 10, its decision to widen the undisclosed band in which it guides the trade-weighted Singapore dollar. At the time, market observers interpreted this move as a sign of tacit approval for a weaker Singapore dollar, which would help support exporters at a time when the city-state is grappling with the worst recession in its 36-year history. \par \par \uc2  In any case, with the MAS having widened its policy band, market participants are more willing to test the limits of the band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  This is especially true as long as economic data continue to suggest the economy's recession is deepening. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's Ministry of Trade & Industry Friday released detailed third-quarter economic data that confirmed an economic contraction of 5.6%. Ministry officials also said they see no chances of a recovery anytime soon. \par \par \uc2  "Hopes of a recovery by the end of this year have evaporated" following the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks on the U.S., the ministry said. \par \par \uc2  Leading indicators point to further weakness. According to Singapore's trade and industry ministry, its composite leading indicator, which tracks economic activity three quarters ahead, declined 2.8% in the third quarter over the second quarter. The figure was, however, better than the 5.3% decline registered in the second quarter. \par \par \uc2  Business expectations surveys are also dismal. "Both manufacturing and services firms foresee worsening business prospects in the next six months," the ministry said. \par \par \uc2  Under the current economic environment, a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be a plus, says Irene Cheung, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro Bank in Singapore who expects the U.S. dollar to rise to S$1.85 by the year's end. \par \par \uc2  -By Hasan Jafri and Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; \par \par \uc2  65/4154-151; hasan.jafri@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011119dxbj000p3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
