\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Late; Off Fresh 11-Year Low Vs US Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 718 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2001\par 09:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was sharply weaker late Monday, after hitting fresh 11-year lows against the U.S. dollar following a decline by the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0820 GMT (3:20 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8427, up from S$1.8361 late Friday. It traded between S$1.8355 and S$1.8430. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened lower against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia in very thin trading as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped on profit-taking by U.S. investment houses late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar also showed little reaction to Prime Minister Goh Chok Tong's naming of his new Cabinet, including the new Finance Minister, over the weekend. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Prime Minister, and Chairman of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, Lee Hsien Loong, was named Finance Minister in place of Richard Hu. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar then rose on buying by a large local bank and U.S. investment houses in line with its broader gains against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  ""They've been looking for dips to buy (U.S. dollars) and they started from S$1.8320. I think the U.S. dollar was looking very attractive just now," said a European bank dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar reached its new 11-year high despite fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  above the key S$1.8398 mark, the previous 11-year high, to smooth out excessive volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The last time the U.S. dollar reached that level against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was believed to have sold U.S. dollars aggressively in the market to prevent the Singapore dollar from falling too sharply. \par \par \uc2  However, after the MAS widened its policy band last month, market participants are more willing to test the limits of the band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is expected to rise further against its Asian counterparts, including the Singapore dollar, in overnight trading sessions on a more bullish outlook for the U.S. dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is expected to face initial resistance at S$1.8440, and next resistance at S$1.8500, with support at S$1.8320. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were mostly higher late Monday, as bargain-hunting pulled prices up from their early morning lows, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bonds prices had tumbled earlier tracking falls in U.S. Treasurys late Friday and as planned corporate bond issues continue to cause concerns about oversupply, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  Singapore commuter rail operator SMRT Corp. is the latest company to seek financing through the debt market, having just priced its S$500 million issue earlier. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds was down six basis points at 1.66% while the yield on five-year bonds was flat at 2.86%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds was down two basis points at 3.17% while the yield on 10-year bonds was down one basis point at 3.55%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds was down two basis points at 3.87%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest-rate swaps market, swaps were also mostly lower in\par line with local bond yields.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The most liquid seven-year swap offer closed down three basis points\par at 3.40% while the 10-year swap offer closed down three basis points at\par 3.70%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps was steady at 145 basis\par points from late Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank money market, rates were mostly steady although the\par overnight rate rose slightly in spite of ample liquidity.\par                   Late Monday       Late Friday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.6250% 0.7500%   0.1250% 0.2500%\par 3-Month           1.0625% 1.1875%   1.0625% 1.1875%\par 1-Year            1.3750% 1.5000%   1.3750% 1.5000%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011119dxbj000hv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
