\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Singapore dollar falls past 1.84/dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2001\par 11:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 19 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar slid past 1.84 to the U.S. dollar on Monday to an 11-year low on the back of a weaker yen, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  This was the lowest level since June 31, 1990 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit 1.8540. At 1008 GMT the Sing dollar was trading at around 1.8430 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , recently widened the trading band for the Sing dollar in a move the market saw as a tacit acceptance of A weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign banks scrambled to buy back the U.S. dollar to cover short positions after the stop near 1.84 was triggered. \par \par \uc2  But they highlighted the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell too far too fast because it is out of line with movements of other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We've got lots of dollar buying orders from bank clients but I'm not sure exactly what the orders are linked to. My guess is that people are covering short positions due to a much weaker yen," said a senior dealer at a regional bank. \par \par \uc2  "But I will be very cautious at this point because the Sing dollar is falling at a much faster pace compared with its regional peers," he said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar hit a three-week high against the yen on Monday because of increasing worries about Japan's banking sector. \par \par \uc2  Dollar bulls were also reassured by progress in the U.S.-led military campaign in Afghanistan, although last week's growing optimism over the U.S. economy was dampened somewhat by grim industrial output figures released on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar tracks the yen closely because the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes up a big chunk of Singapore's trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  FUNDING VEHICLES \par \par \uc2  Dealers say losses in the Singapore dollar are due partly to the fact that it is being used as a funding vehicle for some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the won. \par \par \uc2  JP Morgan suggested last week that clients go long of 1-month won/Sing dollar, saying the trade would earn 278 basis points if the dollar/won hits its target of 1,280 to the dollar and the U.S. dollar/Sing dollar hits 1.8350. \par \par \uc2  The rising won ended at 1,284.4 per dollar on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say the Singapore dollar is also used to fund U.S. dollar holdings due to a market view that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  might drop further because of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weak economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  BOND \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? \par \par \uc2  There was also talk that the Sing dollar's declines might have been influenced partly by rumoured government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local bond market to bring interest rates lower. \par \par \uc2  Market sources said the MAS might have been in the market to buy the five-year bond following the sell-off of the government bond on Friday, which was caused by moves in the U.S. Treasuries. \par \par \uc2  "It might have been indirectly linked to that although the impact should be very mild," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  "The MAS might have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stave off volatility. But the move doesn't seem to have much of the impact on the money market which has been rather steady," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011119dxbj00l0b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
