\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Korea shines, others flicker. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Jennifer Chen \par \uc2 1,062 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2001\par 10:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 19 (Reuters) - Korean assets commanded \par \par \uc2  centre-stage on Monday with some analysts voicing increasing \par \par \uc2  optimism over the country's financial markets. \par \par \uc2      Key Asian markets rallied despite a lacklustre Wall Street \par \par \uc2  on Friday on hopes for a U.S. recovery by the second half of \par \par \uc2  next year. The optimism helped boost the dollar's against most \par \par \uc2  regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar took a hit and a further reminder of \par \par \uc2  consolidation in banking came with job cuts at Merrill Lynch in \par \par \uc2  Asia. \par \par \uc2      Shares in Seoul closed up 2.55 percent with airline and \par \par \uc2  insurance counters leading the charge. Foreign investors, who \par \par \uc2  have been snapping up local stocks in recent weeks, were also \par \par \uc2  spotted buying stock market futures as well, providing more \par \par \uc2  cheer to the market. \par \par \uc2      The Korean won moved a bit more cautiously, anxious about \par \par \uc2  the weaker yen. Still, analysts have noted a steady uptrend for \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since October 4, when it touched a low of around \par \par \uc2  1,316 to the dollar. At 0902 GMT, it was quoted around 1,284. \par \par \uc2      The influence of foreign investment in Korean stocks, more \par \par \uc2  than worries about the yen, has held sway over the won. \par \par \uc2       Moreover, with Korean interest rates at four percent and \par \par \uc2  U.S. interest rates at two percent, the rate of return on the \par \par \uc2  won was attractive, traders said. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the market was wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the 1,280 level, where they were last \par \par \uc2  suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to head off the won's rise. Given \par \par \uc2  still gloomy global economic conditions, some analysts say the \par \par \uc2  authorities want to maintain the country's export \par \par \uc2  competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  But thanks to the resilience of Korea's domestic economy \par \par \uc2  combined with the equity-related inflows, others see the won \par \par \uc2  rising further. \par \par \uc2  "First of all you still have a very strong current account \par \par \uc2  surplus that is going to get even stronger because of the lower \par \par \uc2  oil prices. \par \par \uc2  "On top of that, after September 11, you had about $2.4 \par \par \uc2  billion that left the country ... all coming back, and probably \par \par \uc2  more will come back," Dominique Dwor-Frecaut, director of Asia \par \par \uc2  Research at Barclays Capital in Singapore, told Reuters \par \par \uc2  Television. \par \par \uc2      She said the won could hit 1,250 to the dollar, but did not \par \par \uc2  give a time frame. \par \par \uc2      Stock markets in Tokyo, Hong Kong and Taiwan also gained \par \par \uc2  ground thanks to rising hopes over the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE DOLLAR SUFFERS \par \par \uc2      However, cheer that the U.S. economy would rebound next \par \par \uc2  year hobbled the other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar suffered the day's worst losses, \par \par \uc2  falling past the 1.84 level on the back of the weaker yen. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not seen levels past 1.84 since June 30, \par \par \uc2  1990, when it hit 1.8540, Reuters data show. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said a major U.S. bank was spotted actively buying \par \par \uc2  the dollar throughout the day. Others added the Sing dollar's \par \par \uc2  fall was caused when the authorities came into the government \par \par \uc2  securities market to buy bonds, keeping interest rates low. \par \par \uc2  Daily charts show the Sing dollar has been on a sharp \par \par \uc2  downtrend since September 17, shedding nearly six percent to \par \par \uc2  its current levels. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been undermined by the \par \par \uc2  city-state's grim economic outlook, which many believed spurred \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore to widen its neutral policy \par \par \uc2  band for the trade-weighted Singapore dollar recently. \par \par \uc2  The authorities use the trade-weighted Singapore dollar as \par \par \uc2  their main monetary policy tool because of the open nature of \par \par \uc2  the economy. Analysts say nearly 70 percent of the country's \par \par \uc2  gross domestic product comes from exports. \par \par \uc2  Confirming the dismal forecasts, government officials have \par \par \uc2  said repeatedly that the economy is unlikely to recover until \par \par \uc2  the second half of next year. \par \par \uc2  MERRILL LYNCH LAYS OFF STAFF \par \par \uc2  Singapore was not the only one in Asia feeling the pinch \par \par \uc2  from the global economic downturn. \par \par \uc2  U.S. investment banking giant Merrill Lynch has cut about \par \par \uc2  25 investment banking staff in Asia and will move its Asia \par \par \uc2  Pacific chief operating officer Ausaf Abbas to Japan following \par \par \uc2  the departure of two senior executives there, sources familiar \par \par \uc2  with the situation told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, Merrill's New York office said around 2,600 \par \par \uc2  employees, or nearly four percent of its workforce, had \par \par \uc2  accepted buyout packages. \par \par \uc2  Merrill is the latest U.S. brokerage house to have reduced \par \par \uc2  its staff in Asia. Salomon Smith Barney was expected to begin \par \par \uc2  cutting staff in its global investment banking division on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday, a person in the company's Hong Kong office said on \par \par \uc2  Friday. \par \par \uc2  Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.09       122.09         -0.81\par  Sing dlr      1.8424       1.8353         -0.39\par  Taiwan dlr    34.495       34.500         +0.01\par  Korean won   1284.00      1282.00         -0.16\par  Baht           44.43        44.42         -0.02\par  Peso           52.13        51.92         -0.40\par  Rupiah      10565.00     10600.00         +0.33\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Japan yen     123.09       114.45         -7.02\par  Sing dlr      1.8424       1.7365         -5.75\par  Taiwan dlr    34.495       32.900         -4.62\par  Korean won   1284.00      1277.00         -0.55\par  Baht           44.43        43.70         -1.64\par  Peso           52.13        50.75         -2.65\par  Rupiah      10565.00      9470.00        -10.36\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ASIAN STOCK MARKETS  0839 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Market       Current      Prev Close     Pct Move\par  Tokyo       10727.94     10649.09         +0.74\par  Hong Kong   11360.26     11287.37         +0.65\par  Singapore    1452.81      1422.17         +2.15\pa