\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Pare gains, dlr recovers from NY crash. \b0\par\par\uc2 977 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2001\par 03:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 13 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  pared gains \par \par \uc2  in early trade on Tuesday as the U.S. dollar, which had been \par \par \uc2  roiled by the crash of a passenger plane in New York, regained \par \par \uc2  some lost ground after it became clear the crash was likely an \par \par \uc2  accident. \par \par \uc2      The dollar/yen, closely tracked by the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  had been sold down to its one-month low of 119.73 before it \par \par \uc2  crawled back above 120 during Asian trading as the incident \par \par \uc2  rekindled the horror of the September 11 attacks . \par \par \uc2      The American Airlines passenger jet, which was leaving New \par \par \uc2  York for Santo Domingo in the Dominican Republic, nose-dived \par \par \uc2  into residential homes in Queens shortly after takeoff from New \par \par \uc2  York's Kennedy Airport, killing up to 268 people. \par \par \uc2      There was no immediate indication of the crash's cause. \par \par \uc2      Otherwise, the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lacked a clear \par \par \uc2  direction, with players looking to local leads for trading \par \par \uc2  ideas. \par \par \uc2      The Indonesian rupiah was clouded by fears of fresh \par \par \uc2  violence in the eastern province of Irian Jaya following the \par \par \uc2  weekend killing of a rebel leader there. \par \par \uc2      The Thai baht defied the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , drawing support from strong capital inflows \par \par \uc2  linked to a new share issue and stop-loss dollar sales. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah sank past 10,700 in early trade as jittery\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate players continued to snap up the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par debt repayment due to fears of violence in Irian Jaya.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A leading human rights group in Indonesia demanded an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inquiry, saying the death of a prominent Papua separatist\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par leader Theys Eluay was a well-orchestrated assasination.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The concerns overshadowed optimism on fresh fund\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par disbursement from the International Monetary Fund (IMF).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Finance Minister Boediono said on Monday he was optimistic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the IMF would disburse a new US$400 million loan to the country\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar was locked in a narrow range, with players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par busy squaring positions ahead of a public and market holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Financial markets in Singapore will be close on Wednesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for a national holiday and will reopen on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said some American names were buying back U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars after they oversold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  overnight in response\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to the New York crash.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market awaits October trade statistics due on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Most players are keeping a low profile and carry only small\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions on books as annual book closing nears.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht retained its firm tone despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par active dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as foreign investors poured\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in cash to buy shares of state-owned energy company the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Petroleum Authority of Thailand which will launch its IPO later\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Bangkok said the Bank of Thailand has been in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market to curb the baht's rapid appreciation since Monday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from 44.45.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the dollar/baht is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unlikely to rise above 44.55 in the near-term as the level\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par represents the 38.2 percent retracement of the pair's October\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 25-November 13 downmove.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won drifted lower, disheartened by foreign investor's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par selling of local stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said early losses in the local stocks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and heavy selling by foreign equity investors prompted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players to cover their short dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market was already cautious to the won's recent gains\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par following suspected dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last Friday after it hit a high of 1,280.2, level not seen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since November 4.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign investors were net sellers of 6.3 billion won worth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of local stocks early Tuesday. They bought a net 11 billion won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par worth of local stocks on Monday, the eighth straight session\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign investors had been net buyers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar held steady early on, but dealers in\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expected Monday's dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and net selling of local stocks by foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors to weigh down the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign investors were net sellers of 760.6 million Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars worth of local shares on Monday, after selling a net\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 332.9 million on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent sessions had repeatedly\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on either side to keep the Taiwan dollar from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par straying far from the 34.50 level to protect its export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economists forecast third-quarter gross domestic product\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (GDP) to shrink by an average of 4.27 percent on the year. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government is due to issue the figures on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso edged lower on a lack of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that dashed hopes of a steady rise in remittances from overseas\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par workers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday as the peso\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slipped to a low of 52.10 would keep players from pushing the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par peso too much too fast.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, dealers said local corporates fearing the peso may\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slide lower were looking to buy dollars around the 52 level.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0136 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.87       120.53         -0.28\par  Sing dlr      1.8261       1.8255         -0.03\par  Taiwan dlr    34.514       34.501         -0.04\par  Korean won   1273.00      1284.50         +0.90\par  Baht           44.35        44.37         +0.05\par  Peso           52.03        52.09         +0.12\par  Rupiah      10770.00     10650.00         -1.11\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.87       114.45         -5.31\par  Sing dlr      1.8261       1.7365         