\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Holding ground, eye yen, c.banks. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,104 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2001\par 03:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 12 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held \par \par \uc2  their ground early Monday backed by a steady yen and on \par \par \uc2  expectations of subdued trade because of a holiday in the \par \par \uc2  United States. \par \par \uc2      Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities were expected \par \par \uc2  to cap the yen's gains, but analysts said market was short of \par \par \uc2  yen especially against the euro , limiting its downside. \par \par \uc2      With Wall Street's moderate gains on Friday, foreign \par \par \uc2  investors may continue to purchase equities in Korea and \par \par \uc2  Taiwan, supporting the Korean won and Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2      But suspected dollar buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea on \par \par \uc2  Friday, to protect the won's export competitiveness, could \par \par \uc2  limit further gains. Similar \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to keep Taiwan dollar's gains in check. \par \par \uc2      Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  see the Singapore dollar likely \par \par \uc2  to stay pressured from the Asian Development Bank's report \par \par \uc2  saying Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to keep the exchange rate \par \par \uc2  weak. \par \par \uc2      The Thai baht was expected to follow the lead of the \par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar, while the Indonesian rupiah and Philippine \par \par \uc2  peso would focus on their domestic economic and political woes. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won was slightly lower as players covered their short\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar positions after Friday's suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the market was caught by surprise\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as a state-run bank bought dollars halting the appreciation of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the won, which hit a high of 1,280.2 on Friday, not seen since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par November 4 when it rose to a high of 1,278.5.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won's rise has been backed by equity-related inflows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with foreign investors purchasing a net 206 billion won worth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of local shares on Friday alone. It was the seventh straight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par session foreign investors had been net buyers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The inflows and a steadier yen were expected to keep the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par won's downside limited, the dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar steadied itself around 1.8250 against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.8270 late on Friday, with the market unsure which direction\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would take.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     To the market's consolation, volatility in the dollar/Sing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has dropped, with charts showing the 10-day close to volatility\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par settling to levels of around four compared to seven in late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par September.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nevertheless, sentiment was still fragile because of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par city-state's struggling economy. On Friday, the Sing dollar was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bruised by an Asian Development Bank report that suggested the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities may have to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  given\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the grievous state of the economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Underlining how badly the economy was doing, a local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par newspaper reported over the weekend that Singapore's National\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wages Council may recommend severe wage cuts for the second\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par time in its 29-year history.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said a major local bank had been spotted steadily\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying dollars last Friday, and its activity was driving the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market's direction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah held onto last week's gains, though the bid/ask\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par spread was unusually wide, indicating a reluctance to trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Players were still wary of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par following last week's relatively huge \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities after the rupiah stumbled to 11,000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, dealers in Jakarta see the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the only\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supplier of dollars. With little prospect of dollar inflows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from foreign investment, the rupiah's ambitions were likely to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be frustrated.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Daily charts showed the rupiah is likely to encounter\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resistance around 9,900, which represents the 38.2 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fibonacci retracement of the dollar/rupiah's rise from August\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 14-November 6.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar was expected to be supported by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity-linked inflows with further boost to sentiment likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from the World Trade Organisations's approval of the island's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par entry.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts believe the WTO's approval on Sunday, a day after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it welcomed China into the trade body, would increase economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par integration with the mainland which considers Taiwan a renegade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par province.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China, despite chilly political relations, has been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan's major destination of exports and investment in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par past several years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that pulled the Taiwan dollar back to 34.50 from a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high of 34.455 should keep players cautious from seeking any\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par significants gains on the back of inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With no fresh local leads, the baht was expected to keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its focus on the Singapore dollar and moves in the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said tight baht liquidity and fears of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might keep the baht shy of the 44.50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level, but with the market short of dollars, gains for the baht\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would be limited.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Charts showed the dollar oversold with a reading of 25.90\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the 14-day relative strength index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     One-month baht forwards were at 3/13 satang per dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compared to 6/10 on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was bobbing around the 52 level, torn between the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's poor fundamentals and hopes for dollar remittances.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said the peso could get a hand from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar remittances from overseas Filipino workers ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Christmas.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, some analysts say remittances for this year might\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slow given the global economic downturn and the likelihood that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par many overseas workers may have lost their jobs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Other analysts say the connection between a stronger peso\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and dollar remittances was tenuous.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was still suffering downward pressure from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic economic woes. A local newspaper reported on Monday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that the budget deficit - one of the biggest concerns for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government - may climb to 161 billion pesos by year-end, above\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the target of 145 billion pesos because of the government's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par failure to improve tax collection.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0123 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.40       120.46         +0.05\par  Sing dlr      1.8225       1.8270         +0.25\par  Taiwan dlr    34.484       34.500         +0.05\par  Korean won   1273.00      1275.00         +0.16\par  Baht           44.42        44.46         +0.10\par  Peso           51.90        51.88         -0.04\par  Rupiah      10500.00     10375.00         -1.19\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.8000         +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.40       114.45         -4.94\par  Sing dlr      1.8225       1.7365         -4.72\par  Taiwan dlr    34.484       32.900         -4.59\par  Korean won   1273.00      1277.00         +0.31\par  Baht           44.42        43.70         -1.61\par  Peso           51.90        50.75         -2.22\par  Rupiah      10500.00      9470.00         -9.81\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.8000         +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011112dxbc003k2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
