\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Sing dollar loses out as most others gain. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,229 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2001\par 10:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 9 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained \par \par \uc2  more ground on the dollar late on Friday, largely thanks to a \par \par \uc2  stable yen. \par \par \uc2      Only the Singapore dollar was the spoiler, stumbling past \par \par \uc2  the 1.82 level when local banks were spotted buying the \par \par \uc2  greenback on behalf of their corporate clients. \par \par \uc2      Some dealers also cited the Asian Development Bank's report \par \par \uc2  on Singapore that included a suggestion that the authorities \par \par \uc2  may have to weaken the Sing dollar, which it said had remained \par \par \uc2  persistently strong. \par \par \uc2  Overall, though, the ADB's growth forecasts did little to \par \par \uc2  damp the cheer in other regional markets where domestic factors \par \par \uc2  played a large role. \par \par \uc2  While rate cuts boosted hopes of a recovery in Taiwan, the \par \par \uc2  Bank of Korea's decision to keep its overnight call rate steady \par \par \uc2  fueled optimism in the won market that things weren't as bad as \par \par \uc2  they seem. \par \par \uc2  In Bangkok, the market was hopeful of dollar inflows ahead \par \par \uc2  of a share listing by the state oil firm PTT Plc. Even the \par \par \uc2  usually ailing rupiah found consolation as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  stepped in to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its behalf. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar bucked the regional uptrend, falling \par \par \uc2  past the 1.82 level while local banks bid for the greenback. \par \par \uc2  Dealers, however, said there was nothing unusual about the \par \par \uc2  dollar buying, and the banks were likely covering their short \par \par \uc2  dollar positions ahead of the weekend. Thin liquidity in the \par \par \uc2  market also exaggerated the moves. \par \par \uc2  Some in the market cited the ADB's report that recommended \par \par \uc2  that the authorities should weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further given \par \par \uc2  the massive decline in exports. Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  of Singapore's neutral policy stance on the trade-weighted Sing \par \par \uc2  dollar, and its recent move to widen the bands on the \par \par \uc2  trade-weighted Sing dollar, the ADB said it still saw the Sing \par \par \uc2  dollar appreciate in terms of its real exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won enjoyed further gains, knowing that a stable won \par \par \uc2  and foreign investors' net purchases of local stocks were there \par \par \uc2  to help it along. \par \par \uc2  Still, its rise was held in check by dollar buying from a \par \par \uc2  state-run bank late in the day, which many believed was on \par \par \uc2  behalf of the authorities. Given Korea's export dependency, \par \par \uc2  analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is keen on keeping the exchange \par \par \uc2  rate competitive, yet stable. \par \par \uc2  After deciding to keep rates steady, the bank said on \par \par \uc2  Thursday the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was likely to remain stable, \par \par \uc2  though it did warn of downside risks in Korea's growth \par \par \uc2  forecast. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, the Finance Minister, Jin Nyum, said the government \par \par \uc2  would lower its growth target for 2002 to four percent from \par \par \uc2  five percent. He also added the government would raise its 2002 \par \par \uc2  budget by five trillion won. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar failed to hold onto its earlier gains \par \par \uc2  with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  making sure it did not stray too far from \par \par \uc2  the 34.50 level. \par \par \uc2  Still, it did manage to end at a four-month high of 34.50 \par \par \uc2  despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Taiwan dollar has \par \par \uc2  been stuck in increasingly narrow ranges for the past several \par \par \uc2  months. \par \par \uc2  Dollar-selling on the non-deliverable forward market drove \par \par \uc2  the local dollar higher on the spot market, though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  waded in to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say given Taiwan's poor economic prospects, the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is intent on keeping the rate stable to maintain \par \par \uc2  export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso held a narrow range around the 51.75 per dollar as \par \par \uc2  remittances from overseas workers outstripped demand for the \par \par \uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  But players were reluctant to push the peso too much either \par \par \uc2  way on talk of dollar bids lined up at around 51.60 level, \par \par \uc2  dealers in Manila said. \par \par \uc2  Doubts that the seasonal remittances, received annually \par \par \uc2  ahead of Christmas, would be lower than previous years also \par \par \uc2  held back most players from taking short dollar positions. \par \par \uc2      But on the downside dealers believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \par \par \uc2  defend the peso at around 51.80 level. \par \par \uc2      The ADB expected GDP to grow at 2.7 percent in 2001, down \par \par \uc2  from an April forecast of 3.1 percent because of a \par \par \uc2  steeper-than-expected global slowdown. The government has a \par \par \uc2  target of 3.3 percent for 2001. \par \par \uc2      The ADB said growth in 2002 was expected at 3.0 percent, \par \par \uc2  down from a prediction in April of 4.2 percent. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht was stuck in a tight range around 44.50 supported\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by expected buying of Petroleum Authority of Thailand's stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offering by foreign equity investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PTT is expected to raise up to 32 billion baht (US$719)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from its IPO by offering up to 920 million shares to the public\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at 31-35 each during November 15-21.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said local corporate demand for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar capped the baht's upside, while easing baht funding cost\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the offshore forward market also slowdown dollar sales by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore players.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The one-month forward rate was steady at 6/10 satang per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar compared with 10/15 earlier this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the economic front, the government Thailand said it was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par putting together a major package of measures, including tax\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par incentives, to lure foreign investors and encourage\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par multinational companies to set up regional headquarters in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thai Deputy Prime Minister Somkid Jatusripitak told Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the package would be ready in the next couple of months and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could be announced as early as January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah firmed up to touch a session high of 10,340 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par repeated dollar sales by state-run banks which dealers in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jakarta believed was on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They estimated the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Bank Indonesia, through\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the state banks may have sold up to $20 million with total\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par turnover reaching slightly above $100 million near the close of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was further supported by stop-loss dollar sales\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par triggered at around 10,400. But local corporates were seen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying dollars around 10,350 capping further gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But overall most corporates were on the sidelines expecting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more donor aid commitments, after Thursday's $3.73 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pledged by the Consultative Group on Indonesia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par An International Monetary Fund mission is in Jakarta while\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the talks with the Paris Club of donor nations are due next\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia's bank restructuring agency said it was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par optimistic the sale of 51 percent stake of the country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par largest retail bank, Bank Central Asia, would go through by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par end of 2001 as planned.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.29       120.74         +0.37\par  Sing dlr      1.8254       1.8166         -0.48\par  Taiwan dlr    34.500       34.510         +0.03\par  Korean won   1275.00      1287.40         +0.97\par  Baht           44.48        44.47         -0.02\par  Peso           51.88        51.75         -0.25\par  Rupiah      10405.00     10445.00         +0.38\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Japan yen     120.29       114.45         -4.85\par  Sing dlr      1.8254       1.7365         -4.87\par  Taiwan dlr    34.500       32.900         -4.64\par  Korean won   1275.00      1277.00         +0.16\par  Baht           44.48        43.70         -1.75\par  Peso           51.88        50.75         -2.18\par  Rupiah      10405.00      9470.00         -8.99\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011109dxb900i7l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
