\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED-Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Up on firmer yen, Manila cuts rates. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2001\par 01:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      In Singapore datelined story with headline ...Emerging \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -Up on firmer yen; Seoul, Manila cut rates...please read in \par \par \uc2  the headline...Emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -Up on firmer yen, Manila cuts \par \par \uc2  rates...(Removing erroneous reference in headline to rate cut \par \par \uc2  in Seoul). A corrected repetition follows. \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 8 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were higher \par \par \uc2  in late trade on Thursday, riding on the yen's coat-tails as \par \par \uc2  the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated on the back of option-related \par \par \uc2  selling. \par \par \uc2  But the yen's gains were limited by fresh concerns over \par \par \uc2  Japan's banking system after shares in Asahi Bank and \par \par \uc2  Daiwa Bank - due to merge to form the country's fifth \par \par \uc2  largest banking group - plunged to new lows for the year, \par \par \uc2  sparking rumours the merger was failing. \par \par \uc2      Asahi later issued a statement saying the merger was still \par \par \uc2  on the cards. \par \par \uc2      Elsewhere, the Philippines' \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut overnight \par \par \uc2  interest rates by half a percentage point on Thursday, \par \par \uc2  exceeding market expectations of 25 basis points. \par \par \uc2      Governor Rafael Buenaventura said further cuts were likely \par \par \uc2  before the end of the year as inflation was likely to stay tame \par \par \uc2  and the U.S. Federal Reserve was likely to make more cuts. \par \par \uc2      The Bank of Korea, on the other hand, kept its key interest \par \par \uc2  rate target steady in November at a meeting on Thursday, but \par \par \uc2  economists speculated its next easing could be as early as \par \par \uc2  December. \par \par \uc2  It last cut rates by 50 basis points in late September. \par \par \uc2  Despite its patchy reforms, Indonesia managed to convince \par \par \uc2  donors to loosen their purse strings and pledge a fresh fund of \par \par \uc2  more than $3.5 billion for next year. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah held steady at around 10,500, in muted response \par \par \uc2  to a pledge of a fresh injection of $3.14 billion and $586 \par \par \uc2  million by international donors because the news was largely \par \par \uc2  priced in. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said with an International Monetary Fund \par \par \uc2  mission still in the capital and debt negotiations with the \par \par \uc2  Paris Club of donor nations due next week, players would tend \par \par \uc2  to refrain from taking fresh positions. \par \par \uc2  The Consultative Group on Indonesia approved the aid \par \par \uc2  package but underscoring growing wariness over the government's \par \par \uc2  foot-dragging on economic reforms, the World Bank said $1.3 \par \par \uc2  billion was conditional on a major boost in policy \par \par \uc2  implementation. \par \par \uc2  The chief dealer of a U.S. bank in Jakarta said the two-day \par \par \uc2  meeting in which Jakarta was repeatedly criticised by the \par \par \uc2  donors for failing to make progress on reforms would keep \par \par \uc2  overall sentiment glum. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said local corporate demand for the dollar was \par \par \uc2  still strong within a 10,450-10,500 range, but an upward breach \par \par \uc2  of 10,450 could push the rupiah up to levels around \par \par \uc2  10,250-10,300. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar failed to break free from its shackles, \par \par \uc2  and closed below 34.50 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to keep \par \par \uc2  it in line. \par \par \uc2  It spent much of the session above that level, hitting \par \par \uc2  34.42 for the first time since September 19 as hopes rose for \par \par \uc2  the island's maligned economy. \par \par \uc2  The market rallied around the Taiwan dollar after trade \par \par \uc2  data, which still recorded falls, came in better than expected \par \par \uc2  late on Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also got an unexpected boost \par \par \uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 25 basis point cut in key rates. \par \par \uc2  Usually, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be hurt by interest rate cuts \par \par \uc2  because of fears of capital outflows due to lower rates of \par \par \uc2  return. \par \par \uc2  However, because growth has been the main concern in Taiwan \par \par \uc2  and other parts of the region, the market was hoping the rate \par \par \uc2  cut would help spur the economy. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said players had expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the U.S. dollar's behalf around 34.50, \par \par \uc2  which it has done in recent sessions. However, when the bank \par \par \uc2  failed to do so in early trade, the market quickly began \par \par \uc2  unwinding its long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  They added the bank later bought the greenback around \par \par \uc2  34.42, and then more aggressively towards the end of the day. \par \par \uc2  The bank has been keeping the rate stable in order to hold on \par \par \uc2  to export competitiveness and keep domestic confidence intact. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar failed to hold onto its earlier gains \par \par \uc2  with the market covering its short U.S. dollar positions after \par \par \uc2  a major local bank was spotted buying. \par \par \uc2  Otherwise, dealers said trading was unremarkable, and there \par \par \uc2  was little talk attached to the dollar buying by the local bank \par \par \uc2  for now. \par \par \uc2  Stop-loss dollar buy orders were triggered when the \par \par \uc2  greenback rose above 1.8130 after languishing around levels of \par \par \uc2  1.8120 in early Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  The local dollar found some consolation in Singapore \par \par \uc2  Telecommunications' announcement that it would issue $1.5 \par \par \uc2  billion in bonds, though the details of the issue are not \par \par \uc2  known. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won rose to an eight-week high after the Bank of Korea \par \par \uc2  announced it was keeping rates steady and expressed guarded \par \par \uc2  optimism about the economy. \par \par \uc2  The bank's Governor Chon Chol-hwan said he expected two \par \par \uc2  percent growth in the economy in the fourth quarter on the \par \par \uc2  year, and noted recent signs of improvement in the Korean \par \par \uc2  economy. \par \par \uc2  Still, he warned there were still near-term risks to \par \par \uc2  growth, and many analysts stuck by their predictions that the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cut rates by at least 25 basis points in the \par \par \uc2  short term. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, the won's mood was buoyant, and continued \par \par \uc2  strong buying of local stocks by foreign investors also lifted \par \par \uc2  its spirits. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso rose on the back of remittances from overseas \par \par \uc2  workers to touch a session high of 51.74 where dollar bids from \par \par \uc2  importers and corporates capped further gains. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed key overnight interest rates by \par \par \uc2  half a percentage point, taking the borrowing rate to 8.25 \par \par \uc2  percent and the lending rate to 10.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura further cuts were possible \par \par \uc2  before the end of the year as inflationary pressure was \par \par \uc2  subsiding. He added that annual inflation was likely to be \par \par \uc2  below five percent in both November and December, falling from \par \par \uc2  a 12-month low of 5.4 percent in October. \par \par \uc2  With the rate cut already factored in, the peso showed \par \par \uc2  little response. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was also \par \par \uc2  re-introducing a tiering scheme for overnight borrowing to \par \par \uc2  encourage banks to seek returns in government paper. \par \par \uc2  The scheme was withdrawn in August because of fears the \par \par \uc2  funds were being used to speculate against the peso. Seasonal \par \par \uc2  inflow of remittances ahead of Christmas has raised \par \par \uc2  expectations of the peso holding steady for sometime. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0910 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.66       121.01         +0.29\par  Sing dlr      1.8175       1.8171         -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr    34.510       34.520         +0.03\par  Korean won   1287.40      1292.30         +0.38\par  Baht           44.46        44.62         +0.36\par  Peso           51.73        51.88         +0.29\par  Rupiah      10440.00     10625.00         +1.77\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 