\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Dn Late; GDP Gives US Dlr Respite \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2001\par 11:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  wobbled in thin trading late Thursday, as the U.S. dollar found some respite from a smaller-than-expected contraction in the U.S. economy in the third quarter, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. economy shrank at an annualized rate of 0.4% during the July-September period; economists had forecast a contraction of 1%. It was the first time since 1993 that the U.S. has experienced a quarterly economic contraction. \par \par \uc2  Anxieties ahead of the announcement of key U.S. economic data had restrained U.S. dollar bulls earlier this week, providing a floor to the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The slightly better-than-expected data revived the market's appetite for U.S. dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Trading volume in Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was thin, as activity started to show signs of slowing ahead of the year end, said a dealer a European bank. \par \par \uc2  As the honeymoon for Indonesian President Megawati Sukarnoputri came to an end, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  briefly floundered past 10,600 rupiah per U.S. dollar earlier in the day, its weakest level since the leader took office on July 23. \par \par \uc2  Just over 100 days into her rule, Megawati admitted Thursday in her address to the People's Consultative Assembly - the country's highest legislative body - that her government has achieved little since it was formed. \par \par \uc2  She also said the government's ability to repay its debt "has come close to a dangerous point." \par \par \uc2  But she didn't offer any concrete solutions, analysts noted. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah had soared by as much as 30% in the immediate weeks after Megawati came to power. Megawati formed a market-friendly cabinet, appointing a slew of technocrats to key ministerial positions, as she signaled her resolve to press ahead with economic reforms. \par \par \uc2  "Megawati's progress report was surprisingly negative," said Bank of America in a note to clients. \par \par \uc2  Still, a Jakarta-based dealer at a large European bank said the rupiah has priced-in the market's frustrations over her government's slow progress. \par \par \uc2  At 0940 GMT (4:40 a.m. EST), the rupiah had regained some of its footing to trade at IDR10,545, after sliding to as low as IDR10,640 earlier. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold some U.S. dollars to stave off the pressure on the rupiah, "but it was not much - $10 million tops," said a Jakarta-based dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  He added that the U.S. dollar was going through a downward correction, with interbank participants "very long" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and customers showing little interest in buying U.S. dollars above IDR10,600. \par \par \uc2  Although market participants expect the U.S. dollar to trend higher toward IDR11,000 in the near term, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely first extend its downward correction to IDR10,400-IDR10,450, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's fall added to the pressure on the Singapore dollar, which already hurting from the market's renewed appetite for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers also blamed the Singapore dollar's weakness on market talk that Singapore Telecommunications Ltd. may have bought U.S. dollars to pay for its US$601 million purchase of a 22.3% stake in Indonesia's Telkomsel from Dutch telecommunications company Royal KPN. \par \par \uc2  Around 1000 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8272, higher than S$1.8166 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Wednesday to curb the appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , helping set the firmer tone for the U.S. dollar Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Pressured by the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slump, the Thai unit weakened to 44.705 baht per U.S. dollar, compared with THB44.685 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In Seoul, U.S. dollar demand by offshore participants sparked short-covering in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , weighing on the South Korean won, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar finished at 1,298.0 won, up from KRW1,296.10 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar closed steady amid lackluster trading, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slowing down in its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ended at NT$34.529, little changed from Wednesday's close of NT$34.525. \par \par \uc2  Philippine markets were closed Thursday for a long religious holiday, and will re-open Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4043; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011101dxb1000kr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
