\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Steady Late Vs US Dlr But Remains Pressured \b0\par\par\uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2001\par 11:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was steady against the U.S. dollar late Friday, but remained pressured by poor economic data and broad U.S. dollar strength. \par \par \uc2  At 0800 GMT (4:00 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8273, little changed from S$1.8274 late Thursday in Asia. It traded in a S$1.8238-S$1.8285 range Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar opened around S$1.8238 per U.S. dollar in Asia, down from its overnight high of S$1.8175 in New York. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar's gains overnight was due to the U.S. dollar's blip lower on position adjustments, dealers said. Sentiment for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains fragile, they added. \par \par \uc2  Data published Friday showed Singapore's industrial output dived 22.3% on year in September, worsening from a 21.1% contraction in August. \par \par \uc2  Although the figure was slightly better than analysts' expectations generally, some players sold the Singapore dollar on the data. \par \par \uc2  The sharp fall in industrial production drew further attention to the country's exposure to the global slowdown, particularly the slackening in demand for electronics, a key export for Singapore, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. investment houses and local banks were selling the Singapore dollar, they added. \par \par \uc2  However, the Singapore dollar's losses against the U.S. dollar were limited by pre-weekend consolidation and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted caution in the market as the Singapore dollar slipped to S$1.8285 against the U.S. dollar, amid rumors the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  near the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intraday low, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, dealers said sentiment toward the U.S. dollar remains strong, and it is likely to drift higher against the Singapore dollar overnight and early next week. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar is expected to be supported at S$1.8300 against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and resisted at S$1.8200, according to dealers. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were mostly higher, tracking U.S. Treasurys' gains overnight, and as local interbank rates stay pressured, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds was seven basis points lower at 1.67% as the newest issue of bonds, maturing February 2004, started trading, dealers said. The February 2004 bonds were auctioned at an average yield of 1.74% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The yield on five-year bonds was down eight basis points at 2.55%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds was down six basis points at 2.83% while the yield on 10-year bonds was down five basis points at 3.17%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds was two basis points lower at 3.63%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web Site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swaps were mostly lower tracking\par local bond yields.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The most liquid seven-year swap offer closed down five basis points at\par 2.96% while the 10-year swap offer also closed five basis points lower\par at 3.26%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps widened to 142 basis points\par from 140 basis points late Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank money market, rates were mostly lower due to ample\par liquidity, although the overnight rate stayed flat.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Friday       Late Thursday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.1250% 0.2500%   0.1250% 0.2500%\par 3-Month           0.9375% 1.0625%   1.0000% 1.1250%\par 1-Year            1.1875% 1.3125%   1.5000% 1.6250%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011026dxaq000mc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
