\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Steady Late Vs US Dlr But Remains Pressured \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2001\par 11:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was steady against the U.S. dollar late Friday, but remained pressured by poor economic data and broad U.S. dollar strength. \par \par \uc2  At 0800 GMT (4:00 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8273, little changed from S$1.8274 late Thursday in Asia. It traded in a S$1.8238-S$1.8285 range Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar opened around S$1.8238 per U.S. dollar in Asia, down from its overnight high of S$1.8175 in New York. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar's gains overnight was due to the U.S. dollar's blip lower on position adjustments, dealers said. Sentiment for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains fragile, they added. \par \par \uc2  Data published Friday showed Singapore's industrial output dived 22.3% on year in September, worsening from a 21.1% contraction in August. \par \par \uc2  Although the figure was slightly better than analysts' expectations generally, some players sold the Singapore dollar on the data. \par \par \uc2  The sharp fall in industrial production drew further attention to the country's exposure to the global slowdown, particularly the slackening in demand for electronics, a key export for Singapore, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. investment houses and local banks were selling the Singapore dollar, they added. \par \par \uc2  However, the Singapore dollar's losses against the U.S. dollar were limited by pre-weekend consolidation and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted caution in the market as the Singapore dollar slipped to S$1.8285 against the U.S. dollar, amid rumors the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  near the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intraday low, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, dealers said sentiment toward the U.S. dollar remains strong, and it is likely to drift higher against the Singapore dollar overnight and early next week. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar is expected to be supported at S$1.8300 against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and resisted at S$1.8200, according to dealers. \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011026dxaq000m3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
