\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Bow to the dollar, but cautious. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2001\par 04:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 23 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  struggled \par \par \uc2  against a firmer dollar early on Tuesday in cautious trading \par \par \uc2  due to concerns over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks, coupled \par \par \uc2  with uncertainties over the anthrax scare and the war in \par \par \uc2  Afghanistan. \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar was off but not far from its \par \par \uc2  three-month low of 1.8290 per U.S. dollar touched overnight. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said weighing down the Singapore dollar were \par \par \uc2  factors including speculation over local corporates' overseas \par \par \uc2  investment needs, pessimism over the economic outlook and the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new-found tolerance with a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, such tolerance was not expected by central banks \par \par \uc2  in Indonesia, the Philippines, and Taiwan and as such trading \par \par \uc2  interest was likely to be limited and ranges narrow in the \par \par \uc2  rupiah, peso and the Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  Wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is no less in Thailand, \par \par \uc2  but markets there will be closed Tuesday for the Chulalongkorn \par \par \uc2  Day. \par \par \uc2  Uncertainty surrounding the impact on the dollar from a \par \par \uc2  widening anthrax scare in the United States and the war in \par \par \uc2  Afghanistan, now in its third week, would also deter players \par \par \uc2  from seeking too much weakness in most regionals. \par \par \uc2  The frail yen, hit by gloomy industrial production data \par \par \uc2  seen as a proxy for the gross domestic product, would hurt \par \par \uc2  sentiment in the North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the won and Taiwan \par \par \uc2  dollar might find some support in the Wall Street's rally \par \par \uc2  overnight. \par \par \uc2  In early Tokyo trading, the dollar held firm and was just \par \par \uc2  shy of its overnight highs against the yen, levels last seen in \par \par \uc2  mid-August. The euro was also off overnight lows but was \par \par \uc2  seen struggling due to growing pessimism over the German \par \par \uc2  economy. \par \par \uc2  Six leading economic institutions on Monday slashed their \par \par \uc2  2001 growth forecasts for Germany saying the euro zone's \par \par \uc2  largest economy was on the verge of recession. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan will release September jobless rate at 0300 GMT and \par \par \uc2  Singapore and Hong Kong will issue September consumer prices \par \par \uc2  data. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Volatility marked the Singapore dollar's early trade as \par \par \uc2  funds speculating on its downside struggled against \par \par \uc2  profit-takers in dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said with the dollar strengthening against both the \par \par \uc2  yen and the euro, the Singapore dollar was expected to stay \par \par \uc2  under selling pressure and could test the 1.8300 psychological \par \par \uc2  barrier. \par \par \uc2  The yen and euro are among the major components of the \par \par \uc2  trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore to manage the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said a significantly weaker inflation number would \par \par \uc2  further raise expectations of a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The consumer \par \par \uc2  price index in August rose 0.7 percent on the year, against 1.3 \par \par \uc2  percent in July. \par \par \uc2  Trading range for the day was expected to be 1.8250-1.8300. \par \par \uc2  Charts showed the dollar in overbought territory with a reading \par \par \uc2  of 79.44 on the 14-day relative strength index. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  With local markets closed the baht held onto its recent \par \par \uc2  range of 44.65-44.80 in light offshore trade, impervious to the \par \par \uc2  weaker Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said offshore players had shown little \par \par \uc2  interest in the baht after the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  implemented \par \par \uc2  stricter reporting rules on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions. Their view was \par \par \uc2  that the bank could slap on more severe restrictions on trade. \par \par \uc2      And while the onshore market was still fairly liquid, \par \par \uc2  dealers said little speculative activity had been going on. \par \par \uc2      That said, dealers in Bangkok noted the baht had been \par \par \uc2  unable to strengthen much because many in the market were \par \par \uc2  anxious about the Thai economy's prospects. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar remained true to its sedentary ways of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the past month or so, with volumes in the market shrinking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par steadily.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Despite the island's struggling economy, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stabilised thanks to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's determination to keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it in line. Faced with a bank that boasts $115 billion in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reserves, many players have decided to sit on the sidelines for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the time being.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, the government was expected to issue more poor\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic data later in the day. The statistics bureau will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par announce September's unemployment rate at 0300 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso slipped to 51.80, though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  quickly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stepped into the market to prevent the peso from falling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Turnover on the Philippine Dealing System has been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dwindling with players becoming increasingly frustrated by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lack of flows and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's dogged attempts to keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the peso from slipping past 51.80.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With the Christmas season approaching, dealers in Manila\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were expecting an increase in dollar remittances from overseas\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par workers, which should boost the peso. However, the market was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still perturbed by the Philippines' economic prospects.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government conceded over the weekend that it might not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be able to sell its 10 percent stake in power firm Meralco by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the end of the year as planned. Analysts say this could make it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par difficult for the government to reach its privatisation target\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this year, which could widen the already large budget deficit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won softened in early trade with the market focusing on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen's weakness but a firm opening at the local stock market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was expected to cap the downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said with the yen looking vulnerable\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to more downside and with little hopes of a quick recovery in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic growth and exports the won was likely to probe weaker\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par levels in coming days.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par An analyst at a U.S. bank said with the won now trading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par below the 1,300-level, a test of 1,310 was possible on further\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weakness of the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To cushion the impact of the downturn, Seoul will unveil a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supplementary budget of $1.4 billion which comes on top of five\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trillion won worth of extra spending already in the pipeline.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was weighed down by local corporate demand for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars around the 10,000-level but fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept the downside limited.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was expected to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par step into the market to defend the 10,200-level. But a breach\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of what has now become a psychological support level could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par spark a steep fall of the rupiah, they added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar was on the edge of the overbought territory with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a reading of 70.68 on the 14-day relative strength index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Worries about domestic political stability amid growing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par anti-American sentiment against U.S. military action in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Afghanistan would also keep the players cautious.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0149 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.44       121.62         -0.67\par  Sing dlr      1.8263       1.8257         -0.03\par  Taiwan dlr    34.549       34.543         -0.02\par  Korean won   1298.00      1303.50         +0.42\par  Baht           44.76        44.74         -0.04\par  Peso           51.75        51.76         +0.02\par  Rupiah      10110.00     10100.00         -0.10\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     122.44       114.45         -6.53\par  Sing dlr      1.8263       1.7365         -4.92\par  Taiwan dlr    34.549       32.900         -4.77\par  Korean won   1298.00      1277.00         -1.62\par  Baht           44.76        43.70         -2.37\par  Peso           51.75        50.75         -1.93\par  Rupiah      10110.00      9470.00         -6.33\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.8000         +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011023dxan00339\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
