\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Better off being ignored. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,139 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2001\par 11:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 15 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept \par \par \uc2  modest gains late on Monday, though their composure was more \par \par \uc2  due to dimming trading interest rather than any change to the \par \par \uc2  region's economic health. \par \par \uc2      With uncertainty abounding in geopolitics as well as in the \par \par \uc2  global economy, more and more players have been favouring the \par \par \uc2  sidelines, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      Besides, investors were hardly likely to plunge into the \par \par \uc2  regional markets given how quiet the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were. The \par \par \uc2  dollar barely budged from 121.00 yen the entire session as \par \par \uc2  concerns over anthrax reports in the United States were \par \par \uc2  balanced by wariness over possible Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Low volumes plagued the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, which spent the \par \par \uc2  day swinging in a range of 1.8140-1.8225, ending near the low \par \par \uc2  end as some dealers took profits on recent hefty gains. \par \par \uc2      The market is eyeing Wednesday's release of non-oil \par \par \uc2  domestic exports for September which are expected to make grim \par \par \uc2  reading given how badly hit Singapore has been by the \par \par \uc2  electronics slowdown and the attacks on the U.S. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar managed to crawl back to the right\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par side 1.8200, taking heart from abating U.S. dollar bids.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said a local bank that had been a big Sing$ seller\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par last week, so playing a leading role in its dive to 10-week\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lows, had been quiet today. The let-upo in selling prompted a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par general round of profit-taking on long U.S. dollar positions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and saw the Sing$ edge to $1.8150.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Trading was choppy throughout the session, with thin\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par volumes aggravating the price movements. Many players decided\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to hug the sidelines until fresh trading cues emerged.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Unfortunately, there was little to boast about in the Sing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar's prospects with more bad economic news expected later\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this week. September non-oil domestic export numbers (NODX) are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par due on Wednesday, and a recent Reuters poll showed economists\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on average expect NODX to fall by 14.6 percent in 2001.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dismal economic outlook has already prompted the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to widen its preferred trading band for the Sing$,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a move which traders took as tacit acceptance of a weaker\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht clawed back more ground as the market continued to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unwind long dollar positions after being caught short on baht\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the baht failed to break a key resistance level of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 44.55 as players pessimistic about the country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic outlook were keen to buy dollar on dips.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bangkok dealers also attributed Friday's gains to one-off\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par maturing options and said the baht's fundamentals all pointed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par downwards for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They added the market was getting increasingly edgy over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Bank of Thailand's refusal to lower interest rates. While\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower rates could hurt the baht, dealers and analysts believe\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it is a necessary move to help boost Thailand's faltering\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy because it would help corporates refinance bad loans.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The BOT, however, continued to disappoint their hopes,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par steadfastly refusing to lower its benchmark 14-day repo rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that was hiked by 100 basis points in July. It said earlier in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the day a visiting IMF delegation agreed with its rate policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso edged slightly higher in line with other regionals\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher amid paper-thin trading volumes as most players kept\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par away from the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said wariness over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which doggedly defended the 51.80 level last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week, has prompted most corporates and importers to stay out\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and avoid getting caught on the wrong foot.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, Finance Secretary Jose Camacho accepted it was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par difficult to prop up the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He said it might be difficult for the peso to stabilise at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 50 to the dollar by year-end because low \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows and the global tension following strikes on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Afghanistan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo has said she hoped the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par peso would stabilise at 50 to the dollar by the end of the year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after touching a six-month low of 54.70 in July.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Charts showed the dollar/peso overbought with 14-day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relative strength index reading at 76.86, indicating more room\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the dollar to correct downwards.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah idled in a narrow range around 10,000 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, with the local markets closed for a religious holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said there was no major activity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reported in the offshore spot market or in the Singapore-based\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-deliverable forward market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Rupiah's one-month NDF was quoted by a broker at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10,110.0/10,210.0 and three-month at 10,400.0/10,500.0.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said rupiah's upside would remain capped by worries\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about domestic political stability, with more street protests\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reported on Monday following sporadic incidents of harassment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and assault on foreigners and tourists over the weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A steady stream of foreign equity-linked flows lifted the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par won, which closed a touch higher against the dollar to 1,296.9\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against 1,299.3 on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foregin investors were net buyers of 16 billion won worth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of stocks on Monday, after buying a whopping 500 billion won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par worth last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, dealers said the won's upside was capped by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par profit-taking from players nervous about events in Afghanistan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the United States.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar chalked up miniscule gains to close at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 34.549 from Friday's 34.550.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As with the won, the Taiwan dollar was boosted by steady\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign investment in the local stock market, despite a two\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent drop in the TAIEX on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept the Taiwan dollar in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par check. Given the dismal state of Taiwan's export-dependent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been actively buying U.S. dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the market to keep the island's competitive edge.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0848 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \hi