\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mostly firmer as dollar fumbles. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,081 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2001\par 04:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 15 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  clambered onto firmer ground early on Monday after the dollar \par \par \uc2  suffered another blow to its confidence from poor economic data \par \par \uc2  and fears of more anthrax cases. \par \par \uc2      The exception was the Singapore dollar which softened again \par \par \uc2  despite being massively oversold following last week's slump to \par \par \uc2  10-week lows. \par \par \uc2      The respite elsewhere could also be cut short since Asia's \par \par \uc2  fortunes are largely tied to the fate of the U.S. economy. Data \par \par \uc2  reported on Friday showed U.S. retail sales fell by 2.4 percent \par \par \uc2  in September, which does not bode well for an economy fueled by \par \par \uc2  consumer spending. \par \par \uc2      And stores in the United States may have a tougher time \par \par \uc2  luring back consumers amid fears of biological warfare after an \par \par \uc2  anthrax case was reported in New York. \par \par \uc2      Toughening the odds for the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen \par \par \uc2   was not providing much support. Though the dollar \par \par \uc2  wobbled against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it held its ground against \par \par \uc2  the yen thanks to wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Japan. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lost a battle to hold above $S1.8200 despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure for a U.S. dollar correction, with manuy in the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suspecting the local authorities want to see the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for economic reasons.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Charts do show the dollar/Sing at its most oversold levels\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since early July, with a 14-day relative strength index reading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of around 91.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said a major local bank that had been bidding\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par aggressively for U.S. dollars was starting to sell back some of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par those dollars. Analysts also warned higher local interest rates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par or a stronger rupiah could also support the Sing dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the prognosis for the Sing dollar was still poor as the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy braces for a few more quarters of recession. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government warned last week that the city-state's economy could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remain in recession during the first half of next year. It also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lowered it full-year 2001 gross domestic product forecast to a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par three percent contraction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In response to the bleak economic outlook, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore said it was widening its policy band for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which the market took as tacit acceptance of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the U.S. dollar was well-supported around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.81, with many in the market posied to buy the U.S. unit on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dips.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was expected to follow other regionals higher but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a lack of dollar inflows and economic worries were likely to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par keep the rise limited.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said the peso's upside was expected to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be capped at around 51.65-51.70. On the downside the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may step in again at around 51.80, the level it is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suspected to have repeatedly defended last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Charts showed the dollar/peso overbought with 14-day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relative strength index reading at 77.31, indicating room for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par profit-taking in the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Secretary of Finance Jose Camacho after two days of talks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with Wall Street bankers, bond investors and ratings agencies\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said on Friday the government is standing by its 2001 target of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3.3 percent gross domestic product growth despite the economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shocks heaped upon it by the U.S. downturn.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht was steady at 44.70 wedged in between onshore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par commercial demand for the dollar and trimming of long dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions amid uncertainty about the local government's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said offshore players were reluctant\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to take any aggressive dollar/baht positions, despite repeated\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par denials by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of any plan to cut its key interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also said it would announce within the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par next two weeks whether it would go ahead with plans to issue\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 320 billion baht of bonds in October-December, to rollover debt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par taken up by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from bailed out and troubled\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah trotted just above the 10,000 per dollar level,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with its upside capped on concerns about domestic political\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stability.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     State media and tour operators said tourists and foreigners\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are being harassed, and in the first of such incidents two\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par German tourists were punched and kicked after being mistaken\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for Americans.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But players were reluctant to push the rupiah too low on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in support of the rupiah\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par just beyond the 10,000 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week confirmed it had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. The bank also said it would prefer to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support the rupiah through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , rather than by hiking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic interest rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won rose another notch against the dollar as the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cheered the prospect of more foreign net purchases of local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors bought a net 500 billion won worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korean shares last week, helping the won close at its best\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level since September 20 on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's gains could be limited if the Seoul\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bourse takes Wall Street's losses on Friday to heart. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par benchmark Korean Composite Stock Price Index slipped 0.47\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in early trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar crept higher to 34.546 against Friday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close of 34.55, but the market remained wary of possible\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to restrain the local dollar's gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     With the economy badly hit by the global electronics\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slowdown, the authorities have been keeping the Taiwan dollar's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise in check. Net purchases of local stocks from foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors have buoyed the local dollar recently.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0155 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.06       121.41         +0.29\par  Sing dlr      1.8212       1.8203         -0.05\par  Taiwan dlr    34.540       34.550         +0.03\par  Korean won   1289.00      1292.00         +0.23\par  Baht           44.67        44.71         +0.09\par  Peso           51.76        51.80         +0.08\par  Rupiah       9960.00      9950.00         -0.10\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     121.06       114.45         -5.46\par  Sing dlr      1.8212       1.7365         -4.65\par  Taiwan dlr    34.540       32.900         -4.75\par  Korean won   1289.00      1277.00         -0.93\par  Baht           44.67        43.70         -2.17\par  Peso           51.76        50.75         -1.95\par  Rupiah       9960.00      9470.00         -4.92\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011015dxaf003jt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
