\par\par \b \uc2  Emerg  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sin$ gets sinking feeling as MAS stands aside. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2001\par 04:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 11 (Reuters) - The wobbly Singapore dollar \par \par \uc2  sank to its fresh 10-week lows in early trade on Thursday on \par \par \uc2  lingering concerns over the country's troubled economy \par \par \uc2  following dismal third quarter GDP data. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell a cent overnight to its lowest levels \par \par \uc2  since July 26 without any signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      On Wednesday the Monetary Austhority of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened \par \par \uc2  its preferred trading band for the trade-weighted Sing$, which \par \par \uc2  dealers took as tacit acceptance of further weakness as a \par \par \uc2  monetary policy stimulus. \par \par \uc2  Other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were rangebound as players kept \par \par \uc2  low profile ahead of fresh leads from central banks in Japan \par \par \uc2  and Korea, and key economic data from the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan kicked off its two-day meeting on \par \par \uc2  Thursday, with analysts expecting it to maintain its official \par \par \uc2  daily target for excess funds in the money market and leave its \par \par \uc2  symbolic discount rate unchanged at 0.10 percent. \par \par \uc2  In Korea, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy makers met this morning but \par \par \uc2  elected to keep rates unchanged, disappointing market hopes for \par \par \uc2  another easing. \par \par \uc2  Market participants also await Friday's double dose of \par \par \uc2  major data from the U.S. - consumer confidence and retail \par \par \uc2  sales. \par \par \uc2  They largely shrugged off the IMF's forecast on Wednesday \par \par \uc2  that Japan would slip into recession this year, Europe would \par \par \uc2  grow modestly and the U.S. should recover in first half of next \par \par \uc2  year, saying the view was fully priced in. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar got a brief reprieve after players, \par \par \uc2  especially one local name which had snapped up the U.S. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently, unwound long U.S. dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  But once that was done, the market quickly took to selling \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again sending it to $1.8190 and bringing losses in \par \par \uc2  the last month to five percent. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still pretty bullish on the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Having said that, I do expect some profit taking to continue \par \par \uc2  because the market has got ahead of itself in the past few \par \par \uc2  days," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  "After a brief dollar correction, the Sing dollar is likely \par \par \uc2  to head further south. It might fall to 1.8190 soon and still \par \par \uc2  be consistent with the new MAS' policy band. Our year-end \par \par \uc2  target is 1.8300," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The market is focusing on a government's stimulus package \par \par \uc2  expected on Friday. Most analysts reckoned the package would \par \par \uc2  worth at least S$10 billion. \par \par \uc2      Singapore unveiled a S$2.2 billion stimulus package in \par \par \uc2  July. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won opened a touch firmer, drawing support from gains\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in local stocks and a steadier yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Bank of Korea's decision to keep rates unchanged\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par disappointed some. Seven out of 10 respondents to a recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters poll expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to lower its target for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the short-term call rate by 25 basis points to an all time low\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 3.75 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But rate cut hopes were dampened when a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par official said on Wednesday that the debt market had been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overreacting to U.S.-led raids on Afghanistan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar was expected to stay underpinned by a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity-related inflows and a steadier yen when local markets\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par open for trade after a national holiday on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said foreign investors would continue\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to settle their purchases of 9.43 billion Taiwan dollar worth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of local shares they had bought over a four-session buying\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par streak.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was expected to cap any\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par significant upside for the Taiwan dollar. The grim economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outlook would also keep players cautious.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso edged down in light interbank trade but dealers in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Manila said a lack of dollar demand from importers and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporates was expected to push it higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said wariness over suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Wednesday had sent most importers and corporates to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sidelines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Charts also showed the dollar heavily overbought with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 14-day relative strength index reading at 80.67 indicating a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par downward correction of the dollar/peso was due.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The upside was however seen limited with dollar purchases\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to emerge around 51.60-51.65 range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Meanwhile, Finance Secretary Jose Camacho said on Wednesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that he is considering a bond issue guaranteed by the World\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank as part of a plan to raise $1.4 billion in financing for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2002.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The new option is among several including an issue in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dollar. Philippines has already announced plans to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par issue around $414.6 million in private placement of yen bonds\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par or a shibosai issue.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was expected to stay supported around the 10,000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level amid wariness over dollar sales by state names.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said concerns have also eased over the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par protest rallies by Islamic radicals against the U.S.-led\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strikes on Afghanistan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But an unclear political and economic outlook, most players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would prefer to buy dollars at dips, they said. Dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected a trading range of 9,900-10,100 for the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht edged lower taking cue from the Singapore dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and as dollar sales from exporters abated.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said talk of strong dollar bids at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 44.70 has also prompted players to beef up their long dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Capping the downside, exporters are expected to be back in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market at around 44.85 per dollar level, while Wednesday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the baht would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par also keep players wary of pulling the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  too low.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0130 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.22       120.49         +0.22\par  Sing dlr      1.8155       1.8060         -0.52\par  Taiwan dlr    34.559       34.555         -0.01\par  Korean won   1298.00      1308.70         +0.82\par  Baht           44.77        44.70         -0.16\par  Peso           51.79        51.79         +0.00\par  Rupiah       9950.00     10030.00         +0.80\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.22       114.45         -4.80\par  Sing dlr      1.8155       1.7365         -4.35\par  Taiwan dlr    34.559      