\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Singapore GDP delivers blow to Sing$. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Jennifer Chen \par \uc2 1,062 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2001\par 11:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 10 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar teetered \par \par \uc2  close to 1.81 to the U.S. dollar on Wednesday after the \par \par \uc2  government issued a dire outlook for the city-state's economy. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffered another blow when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore later announced it was widening its \par \par \uc2  policy band for the trade-weighted Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2      Though the MAS added it would stick to its neutral policy \par \par \uc2  stance, the market took the step as tacit approval for a weaker \par \par \uc2  Sing dollar. Finance Minister Richard Hu reinforced that notion \par \par \uc2  when he said a wider band reduced the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Unlike most Asian countries, \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses the \par \par \uc2  trade-weighted exchange rate as its primary monetary policy \par \par \uc2  tool rather than interest rates, since its economy is so open. \par \par \uc2  Around 70 percent of Singapore's GDP is derived from exports. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar        skidded to fresh 10-week lows of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1.8088 before profit-takers rescued it. The market had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been bracing for the news as aggressive dollar bids from a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local bank spurred talk that the data was going to be worse\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than expected, forcing the MAS to tolerate a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the Sing dollar's prospects were not bright.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore's Ministry of Trade and Industry said its flash\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par estimate showed third-quarter gross domestic product shrank by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 5.6 percent on the year and by an annualised 9.9 percent on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Those figures could be revised downwards as they only\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reflect the first two months of the quarter, before the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par September 11 attacks in the United States.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     To make matters worse, the government said it had revised\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its full-year GDP forecast to a 3.0 percent contraction, from a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par previous target of 0.5-1.5 percent growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Moreover, it said the 2002 outlook was "highly uncertain,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the first half could see another contraction. That would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mean six straight quarters of contraction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     WHAT'S IN STORE FOR THE SING DOLLAR?\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     After the MAS's announcement, analysts debated the merits\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the move.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     One camp of analysts argued that the MAS did its best in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par finding a middle way between loosening and maintaining its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par policy bias, which it only recently changed in July.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The risk, they say, was that investors would demand a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher rate of return from Singaporean assets if the exchange\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate weakened substantially.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     This camp also argues that Singapore's exports will not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par necessarily benefit from a weaker exchange rate as global\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand remained sluggish. A weaker Sing dollar, they say, would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par only translate into cheaper exports rather than more sales.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The other camp, however, says the MAS was not being\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par flexible enough given size of the economic downturn.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "They should have gone ahead and announced a depreciation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par policy as well, rather than sticking to a zero percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appreciation," said Rajeev Malik, an economist at JP Morgan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chase.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The magnitude of the slump and the intense disinflationary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bias probably supports that."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     While analysts bickered over the wisdom of the MAS's move,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they also scrambled to adjust their estimates of the Sing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar's policy band and their dollar/Sing targets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The MAS does not reveal the exact composition of its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade-weighted basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , nor its policy bands.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Peter Redward, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore, estimated that a widening would tack on another half\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percentage point to the band. His current estimate for the band\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par is plus or minus three percent, which would have 1.8250 to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollar as the bottom of the band, and 1.79 in the middle.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In terms of what this means for the bilateral exchange\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate for the dollar, a lot of it hinges on what happens to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah, the yen and all the other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that have a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par material weighting in the trade basket," Manu Bhaskaran, Chief\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Strategist at SG Securities in Singapore, told Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "My best guess is that given that the yen is likely to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weaken, we're probably looking at anything between 1.85 and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.90 even if the yen weakens a lot."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par STOCKS EDGY\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore shares recovered some of their losses after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GDP report's initial shock, with the benchmark Straits Times\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Index only down 0.67 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere in the region, other key bourses slipped as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors struggled with the lingering unease over the impact\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and length of the U.S.-led military strikes in Afghanistan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo stocks dipped below the key 10,000 level for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the first time this week as investors fretted over the grievous\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par state of Japanese banks. Shares in Seoul and Hong Kong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  also dipped following falls in U.S. technology stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Markets in Taipei were closed for a public holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0849 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change o