\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Late; Many Holding Dollar Longs \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 1,048 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2001\par 12:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed late Wednesday, with dollar bulls experiencing a resurrection as the region's grim fundamentals return to the forefront of investors' concerns, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Anxieties over the aftermath of the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks in the U.S. had weighed on the dollar last month. But as panic in the market subsided, the dollar has gradually regained its footing. \par \par \uc2  The weaker yen exerted some pressure on the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0930 GMT (4:30 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y120.82, slightly up from Y120.81 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y120.35 late Tuesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  But with many in the market already sitting on long dollar positions and as the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the region's central banks loomed, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  languished in rangebound trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar and the Thai baht were weaker, while the Indonesian rupiah, the Philippine peso and the New Taiwan dollar were slightly stronger. \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed a muted reaction to the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision Tuesday to cut the target for its benchmark federal-funds interest rate to 2.5% from 3%. \par \par \uc2  The rate cut was within expectations and isn't likely to provide an antidote to Asia's woes, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Instead, a rebound in the region's exports would be needed to jump-start Asia's economies, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The way most of us have read the Fed's rate decision and the fiscal spending that's coming in the U.S. is that as far as the downturn is concerned it's becoming more real," said Philip Wee, a market strategist at Singapore's DBS Bank. \par \par \uc2  "Countries that have weathered the downturn so far have to reexamine their prospects, especially Thailand, Indonesia and the Philippines," he added. \par \par \uc2  Including its emergency rate cut just before the U.S. stock markets reopened Sept. 17, the Fed has slashed rates a full percentage point since the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks, and by a whopping four percentage points since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  Even though the Dow Jones Industrial Average jumped 1.3% Tuesday as the Fed left the door open to further rate cuts in the aftermath of the attacks, Asian stock markets displayed a lukewarm response. \par \par \uc2  "That's not a good confidence booster for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar felt the brunt of the yen's weakness and on U.S. dollar demand by U.S. investment houses, which sent it reeling to its lowest level in almost two months, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar climbed to as high as S$1.7818, its highest level since Aug. 7. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar, however, retreated below S$1.7800 late in the day as sales of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by local banks fueled speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to temper the sharp decline in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent sessions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Late Wednesday, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7788, still higher\par than S$1.7774 the previous day.\par - - 03/10/01 10-04G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, some dealers were skeptical on whether the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par of Singapore had defended the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , given that the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  still appeared stable against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of its major\par trading partners.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The weakness of the Singapore dollar and the yen weighed on the Thai\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which was at 44.760 baht a dollar, compared with THB44.690\par late Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht could succumb to further pressure as the Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par continued to resist the market's calls for it to lower interest rates,\par market watchers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thai Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said Wednesday there was no\par immediate need to lower the country's interest rates to mirror the\par latest policy easing in the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Six months ago, they could do that because the outlook for the\par economy wasn't that bad, but now, it's bad," said Wee at DBS Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Suspected dollar sales by Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  helped push the\par U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to below the IDR10,000 level late in the day, dealers\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But corporate demand for dollars kept the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  buoyed above\par IDR9,900, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Late in the day, the dollar was at IDR9,915, lower than IDR10,015 late\par Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Protests against possible U.S. military retaliation on Afghanistan for\par the terrorist attacks in New York and Washington have sparked security\par concerns and fears that this could drive foreign investors away.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market observers are also worried that President Megawati's pledge to\par support the U.S. in its war against terrorism might hurt her fragile\par alliance with Muslim political parties.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market prices back the political risk premium whenever they see\par the leadership being questioned," said Wee at DBS Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the Philippine Dealing System, the peso ended slightly higher as\par dealers believed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had supported the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by selling\par as much as $50 million to various banks at around PHP51.600.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Participants were wary of taking any major positions ahead of the\par Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision on its overnight rates at its weekly\par board meeting Thursday. Although the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is under intense\par pressure to lower rates, it finds it difficult to do so given\par inflationary pressures.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar closed at PHP51.575, down from PHP51.600 Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The New Taiwan dollar resisted getting dragged by the tottering yen,\par as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought and sold an estimated US$60 million to stave\par off any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar closed at NT$34.569, little changed compared with\par NT$34.574 Tuesday, in dealings valued at a relatively thin US$260\par million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Every \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's game now is to temper the dollar's upside, but I\par don't think they will fight the trend," said Wee at DBS Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korean markets were closed Wednesday for a holiday and will\par reopen Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4043;\par netty.ismail@dowjones.com\par -0- 03/10/01 11-27G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011003dxa3000k6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
