\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Lower Late; Tracks Weaker Yen, Regionals \b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2001\par 11:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar fell to its lowest level since Aug. 7 on Wednesday, tracking weakness in the yen and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as banks bought U.S. dollars on concerns over Asia's economic fundamentals, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0910 GMT (5:10 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7784, up from S$1.7780 late Monday in Asia. It traded between S$1.7775 and S$1.7818. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened little changed in Asia, but rose above S$1.7800 by midmorning in line with its rise to an intraday high of Y121. \par \par \uc2  Buying led by U.S. investment houses pushed the U.S. dollar to an intraday peak of S$1.7818, its highest level since Aug. 7. \par \par \uc2  However, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped below S$1.7800 in late afternoon trade on selling by local banks. This was interpreted by some market participants as probable \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The selling wasn't very big, but the speculation is that it could have been to smoothen things," a dealer at a U.S. brokerage said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market largely ignored the 50 basis point cut in the U.S. Federal Funds rate by the Federal Open Market Committee, as it had already been priced in. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the U.S. dollar to trade between S$1.7780 and S$1.7820 overnight. \par \par \uc2  Singapore government bond prices surrendered early gains to end unchanged Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Bonds opened higher following the Fed rate cut, but retreated in the afternoon on profit-taking, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The 50 point cut was expected and had been priced in, so it was natural for some profit-taking to happen," a dealer at a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  The yields on two- and five-year bonds ended flat at 1.89% and 2.89%, respectively. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yields on seven-, 10- and 15-year bonds also ended flat at 3.14%, 3.38% and 3.73%, respectively. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swaps were mostly lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The most liquid seven-year swap offer closed 1.5 basis points lower at\par 3.235%, and the 10-year swap offer closed at 3.465% compared with at\par 3.48% Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps widened slightly to 113.5\par basis points from 112.5 basis points late Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank money market, rates were mostly lower, due to ample\par liquidity in the system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Wednesday    Late Tuesday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.3750% 0.5000%   0.1250% 0.3750%\par 3-Month           1.6250% 1.7500%   1.6250% 1.7500%\par 1-Year            1.8750% 2.0000%   2.0000% 2.1250%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (65) 415-4152;\par amit.prakashdowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011003dxa3000io\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*