\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Calm now, but rough waters ahead. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,126 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2001\par 03:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 3 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  clung onto \par \par \uc2  dry ground early on Wednesday with the market taking a moment \par \par \uc2  to consolidate after recent losses. \par \par \uc2      Little reaction as yet to the Federal Reserve's widely \par \par \uc2  expected 50 basis point rate cut on Tuesday, which took its \par \par \uc2  funds rate to 2.50 percent - the lowest level in nearly 40 \par \par \uc2  years. \par \par \uc2  After announcing the ninth cut so far this year, the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was poised to act again to help cushion \par \par \uc2  the economy in the aftermath of the attacks in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The dollar bounced against the yen immediately after the \par \par \uc2  cut, touching a high of 121.14 in overnight trade. \par \par \uc2  Profit-takers, however, later trooped out to drag it down. \par \par \uc2  Still, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially in Southeast Asia, \par \par \uc2  were quivering in fear of future falls given Asia's \par \par \uc2  vulnerability to a weaker yen as well as a damaged U.S. \par \par \uc2  economy. \par \par \uc2  Given these fears, central banks in Southeast Asia may \par \par \uc2  think twice before following the Fed's rate cut. Central banks \par \par \uc2  in North Asia, however, are widely expected to mimic the Fed's \par \par \uc2  move. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong has already eased by 50 basis points and analysts \par \par \uc2  reckon South Korea, Taiwan and Malaysia may follow at some \par \par \uc2  point. \par \par \uc2  Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are also wrestling with domestic \par \par \uc2  concerns, with the Indonesian rupiah struggling to stay above \par \par \uc2  the 10,000 level amid anxiety that anti-American protests could \par \par \uc2  drive away badly needed foreign investment. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was trapped at 10,000 as the market despaired \par \par \uc2  over recent anti-American protests possibly driving away \par \par \uc2  foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia has seen several small, but vocal anti-American \par \par \uc2  rallies held by fringe Muslim radical groups. While few \par \par \uc2  foreigners are actually leaving Indonesia, there is a growing \par \par \uc2  fear that a U.S. strike against the Taliban could produce a \par \par \uc2  backlash in Indonesia, the world's most populous Muslim \par \par \uc2  country. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Jakarta said Bank Indonesia tried to cushion the \par \par \uc2  rupiah's falls on Tuesday, but only with limited success. \par \par \uc2      However, charts showed the dollar/rupiah was heavily \par \par \uc2  overbought, with a 14-day relative strength index reading of \par \par \uc2  83. If corporate dollar demand is less than expected, the \par \par \uc2  rupiah could enjoy a technical bounce. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar remained soft against the U.S. dollar, with \par \par \uc2  corporate players and local banks continuing to add to long \par \par \uc2  dollar positions against the backdrop of a weak yen and the \par \par \uc2  situation in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2      But the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  drew some support from dollar profit \par \par \uc2  taking above 1.7780. \par \par \uc2      Charts show the U.S. dollar is slightly overbought, with a \par \par \uc2  reading of 74.3 on the 14-day relative strength index (RSI). \par \par \uc2  The overbought line is 70. This indicates the upside for the \par \par \uc2  dollar could be limited in the very near term. \par \par \uc2  UBS Warburg said in its note that the next key level for \par \par \uc2  the pair was 1.7795 as it marked the 200-day moving average, \par \par \uc2  and a break of this level would allow the dollar to trade \par \par \uc2  higher toward 1.7850 and then 1.7900. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht edged lower to 44.71 with some U.K. and U.S. names \par \par \uc2  heard buying the dollars. But exporters offers capped dollar \par \par \uc2  gains. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trade was subdued as the market was digesting \par \par \uc2  the Fed's move overnight and monitoring how dollar/yen reacted \par \par \uc2  to the cut. \par \par \uc2      There were rumours the Bank of Thailand was in the market \par \par \uc2  on Tuesday to buy to dollars to repay IMF debt. \par \par \uc2      Baht funding costs were steady, with the offshore one-month \par \par \uc2  forward rate quoted at 8/13 satang per dollar and the 12-month \par \par \uc2  rate quoted at 110/135 satang. \par \par \uc2      Foreign investors sold net 142.70 million baht worth of \par \par \uc2  Thai stocks on October 2. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar dipped, but decided not to stray too far\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from the 34.50-34.60 range, where it has been since September\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 21.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Trading interest in the spot market has dwindled, despite a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par huge fall in local stocks on Tuesday. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the market actively to keep the local dollar within a tight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range, and was spotted on Tuesday \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par behalf around 34.588.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers said the offshore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-deliverable market has enjoyed active trade, with players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banking on a weaker Taiwan dollar in the months to come.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The September 11 attacks have squelched any hopes of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quick recovery in Taiwan's economy, which was already seeing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its worst slowdown in years. The government has forecast the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par island's first full-year contraction ever.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso held onto Tuesday's closing level of 51.60 as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players tested the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's resolve to defend the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Manila said all eyes were on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which has been trying to limit the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's losses in recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sessions. While there have been few fresh factors in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market, the peso has come under attack given the grim picture\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the country's economic outlook and a simple dearth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was a bit of a tussle over interest rates earlier in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the day. Philippine Soci-economic Planning Secretary Danta\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canlas said he expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cut rates by at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par least 25 basis points after the Fed's latest easing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Rafael Buenaventura later said he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par did not know if the bank's monetary board, which meets on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday, would indeed cut rates. He added while the Fed's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decision would be taken into account, the board also had to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par consider the exchange rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Financial markets in Korea are closed for a holiday, and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par will re-open on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Because of the closure of local markets, trading on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore non-deliverable market was minimal.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0141 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.70       120.79         +0.07\par  Sing dlr      1.7787       1.7771         -0.09\par  Taiwan dlr    34.584       34.574         -0.03\par  Korean won   1299.00      1316.00         +1.31\par  Baht           44.71        44.64         -0.16\par  Peso           51.58        51.60         +0.04\par  Rupiah      10000.00     10020.00         +0.20\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.70       114.45         -5.18\par  Sing dlr      1.7787       1.7365     