\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Hit multi-week lows,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  abounds. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,066 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2001\par 11:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 12 (Reuters) -  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank to \par \par \uc2  multi-week lows in late trade on Tuesday, pulled down in part \par \par \uc2  by the yen which fell almost a full percent against the \par \par \uc2  dollar due to Japan's economic gloom and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears. \par \par \uc2      Japan has sold the yen on seven days since September 17, \par \par \uc2  buying dollars and euros in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to halt \par \par \uc2  the yen's rise, which Tokyo fears could hurt the fragile \par \par \uc2  domestic economy. \par \par \uc2      Keeping the market on its toes, Finance Minister Masajuro \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa warned on Tuesday that Japan was ready to conduct \par \par \uc2  further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar fell again. \par \par \uc2      "It's pretty clear the Bank of Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not going to allow the yen to be strong. That \par \par \uc2  reverses concerns that the dollar/yen would continue to fall," \par \par \uc2  said Andrew Fung, head of Asian research at Rabobank. \par \par \uc2      But domestic concerns also weighed on regional sentiment. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah        fell past 10,000 to the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the first time since July 31 on market worries that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par festering anti-U.S. sentiment could scare away foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market is looking foreward to a rate cut from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Federal Reserve when it meets later Tuesday, with analysts\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seeing a good chance the Hong Kong, Taiwan and South Korea will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par follow any easing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Financial futures markets have fully priced in a 50 basis\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par point cut in the Fed's main 3.00 percent funds rate, which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would take it to levels not seen since the early 1960s.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, most also suspect that no amount of monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par easing will stop the U.S. from slipping into recession this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter, taking much of the rest of the world with it.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah sank past the 10,000 per dollar level as growing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par anxiety over anti-American sentiment from a small, but vocal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Muslim minority gripped the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Jakarta dealers said corporates chased the dollar to a high\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 10,120 amid fears that recent anti-American protests would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par scare off foreign investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Though Bank Indonesia managed to staunch the rupiah's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wounds by selling dollars, it could not pull it back from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wrong side of 10,000. Volumes were thin, which made the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exchange rate more volatile and steepened the rupiah's fall.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indonesia's Finance Minister Boediono tried to calm the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market by calling the rupiah's losses temporary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers said sentiment towards the rupiah had soured,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and hopes for a rebound were dimming.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Bank Indonesia is the only supplier of dollars now and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par there's a huge demand for dollar out there. With these\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par protests, they're going to be the only supplier of dollars for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some time," said a European bank dealer in Jakarta.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Sing dollar hit a seven-week low before players took\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par profits on the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  near 1.7790 due to wariness of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said a steadier dollar/yen sparked rounds of dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short covering as the yen carries substantial weight in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore's trade-weighted basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Charts show 1.7835 is the next resistance for the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/Sing dollar as it represents the 50 percent retracement\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the July 16-September 17 dollar downmove.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht fell as far as 44.74 - its lowest level since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par September 11 - as players took cues from dollar/yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said dollar buying intensified after stop-loss sell\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par orders were triggered at 44.65, before dollar profit taking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par helped it from the lows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par News that Thai Petrochemical Industry failed to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par make an interest payment due on October 1 due to liquidity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par problems also dampened baht sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, the government said on Monday it planned to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par issue 38 billion yen ($317 million) worth of samurai bonds with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a maturity of three to seven years around mid-November.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Proceeds are earmarked to refinance debts of state companies so\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the money is not likely to be transferred into baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso ended a whisker away from the day low of 51.61\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par despite rumoured \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as interbank players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par covered short dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Manila said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was heard selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around $30-50 million in the market to shore up the local\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The market turnover was $113 million compared with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $61 million on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been keen to stabilise the peso given\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the country's external debt obligations and large fiscal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deficit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar bowed under the pressure of falling local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks and a pessismistic outlook for Taiwan's economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said while volumes in the spot market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were thin, activity in the offshore non-deliverable forward\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market perked up as investment houses hedged their Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar exposure.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading in the spot market was probably also subdued thanks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's vigilance in preventing volatility in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market, they added. The bank, which has over $110 billion in\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, was spotted offering dollars around the day's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high of 34.588.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But given the dollar/yen's move and the dollar/Asians\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par move, offshore players figure it's just a matter of time before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Taiwan dollar makes another move lower," said a European\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Markets in Seoul were closed for a holiday, and will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par re-open on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Because of the closure of local markets, trading on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore non-deliverable market was minimal.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0923 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.69       119.70         -0.82\par  Sing dlr      1.7774       1.7665         -0.61\par  Taiwan dlr    34.574       34.549         -0.07\par  Korean won   1316