\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Tries, and fails, to elude yen's shadow. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,139 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2001\par 11:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 28 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  wilted \par \par \uc2  late on Friday, taking their cue from the yen as it tried to \par \par \uc2  get back on its feet after yet another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \par \par \uc2  the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2      The Bank of Japan waded into the market to buy dollars for \par \par \uc2  yen on Friday, the seventh day in two weeks it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It also co-opted both the New York Federal Reserve and the \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  into selling yen for it during their \par \par \uc2  trading hours no Thursday. \par \par \uc2      Some had thought that officials were only trying to provide \par \par \uc2  Japanese firms a better rate at which to value their assets \par \par \uc2  ahead of the half-year bookclosing, which is today. \par \par \uc2      But, analysts say if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  next week, it would be a serious signal to the market \par \par \uc2  that it really intends to restrain the yen for the long term. \par \par \uc2      Still, with the U.S. economic outlook going from bad to \par \par \uc2  worse, the dollar did not make much headway against the yen \par \par \uc2  during Asian trade and struggled to hold around 119.00 . \par \par \uc2      All in all, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely suffer in the \par \par \uc2  coming sessions with a hobbled yen on one side and a damaged \par \par \uc2  U.S. economy on the other. \par \par \uc2      Markets in Korea, Taiwan, and Hong Kong will be closed on \par \par \uc2  Monday for public holidays. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar slipped slightly from levels seen late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday in choppy trade as players took their cue from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par softer yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  skirted further falls as a U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investment house and some Japanese players shelled out to buy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the market was generally wary of testing the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/Sing's upside after it corrected downwards from Monday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.5 percent gains. Many in the market feared the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rescue the local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar earlier in the week when it bumped against six-week lows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 1.7750.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, dealers argued the only direction for the Sing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar in the medium term was down given the city-state's poor\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic health.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht was a touch easier in line with a weaker yen, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market was cautious to push the baht much lower due to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wariness of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Few players were willing to take fresh positions ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Fed's meeting on Tuesday and the release of Japan's tankan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par business sentiment survey on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par News of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  easing some restrictions on baht\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par loans to individual non-residents and on foreign individuals\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exchanging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , barely had any impact on the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  circular said foreigners with a valid work\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par permit for at least a year can each borrow up to five million\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht ($112,700) of consumer loans or baht-denominated bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par guarantees.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data released on Friday showed Thailand\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par posted a current account surplus of $1.1 billion in August and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a balance of payment surplus of $350 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso ended firmer at 51.32 to the dollar against 51.365\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at the close on Thursday in a thin market, with only $72.95\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million transacted.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell to an intraday low of 51.395 before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar profit-taking emerged amid talk the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still be defending the peso at 51.40-51.50.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market barely reacted to news of the government\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par planning to raise 30-50 billion yen from the issue of shibosai,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a private placement of bonds in Japan, as it has not given the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par timing for the issue.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, the country's value of production index rose\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 11.4 percent year-on-year in July, while the volume of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par production index fell 2.1 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won was held hostage to the yen, closing at a 10-week\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par low of 1,309.60 compared with 1,306.4 on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Players were focused on squaring positions ahead of a long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend holiday as the market will be closed October 1-3 for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Chusok, or thanksgiving, holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of America said in a daily note that Korea's mild\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation data in September and worsening consumer confidence\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were pointing to lower interest rates and a higher dollar/won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the near term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A struggling rupiah was bolstered by state banks who\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par managed to drag it away from early lows of around 9,715.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jakarta dealers said local corporates were still on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hunt for dollars, with the market nervous about reprecussions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at home of a possible U.S. strike on Afghanistan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fringe groups of Muslim radicals have been calling for a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par holy war if the U.S. retaliates for the September 11 attacks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and have also threatened to take action against foreigners in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While President Megawati Sukarnoputir has condemned the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attacks, she has not backed possible U.S. military action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Political analysts say Megawati, whose hold on power is shaky\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after two months, cannot afford to rile these groups.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar closed virtually flat from Thursday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close of 34.548, after giving up earlier gains as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in to steer it back in line.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dealers said the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opened higher\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par thanks to continued dollar sales by exporters ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month-end. They added players both in the onshore spot and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore non-deliverable forward markets have been caught long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which has deep pockets with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reserves of some $110 billion, was spotted buying U.S. dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to curb the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise around 34.51.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With Taiwan facing the possbility of its first ever full\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year contraction in GDP, analysts say the authorities are keen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not to let the Taiwan dollar strengthen too much and hurt the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par island's export competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0850 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.20       118.63         -0.48\par  Sing dlr      1.7661       1.7612         -0.28\par  Taiwan dlr    34.549       34.548         -0.00\par  Korean won   1308.50      1304.25         -0.32\par  Baht           44.43        44.35         -0.18\par  Peso           51.31        51.37         +0.11\par  Rupiah       9705.00      9655.00         -0.52\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.20       114.45         -3.98\par  Sing dlr      1.7661       1.7365         -1.68\par  Taiwan dlr    34.549       32.900         -4.77\par  Korean won   1308.50      1277.00         -2.41\par  Baht           44.43        43.70         -1.64\par  Peso           51.31        50.75         -1.09\par  Rupiah       9705.00      9470.00         -2.42\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010928dx9s00i8q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
