\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Tired of busy BOJ, but no rest ahead. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2001\par 04:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 28 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  bowed to \par \par \uc2  the dollar in early trade on Friday following after the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet again to to restrain the yen. \par \par \uc2      That made it seven days in eleven that it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  and followed a concerted effort on Thursday where the BOJ \par \par \uc2  called on both the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the New York \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its behalf. \par \par \uc2  The effort nudged the dollar up to 119.45 yen after \par \par \uc2  an early dip to 119.00 and fed speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would stay in the market today to provide Japanese \par \par \uc2  institutions with a better \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate with which to value their \par \par \uc2  foreign assets. Today is the half-year bookclosing in Japan. \par \par \uc2      But that left open the question of whether Japan would \par \par \uc2  continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  once bookclosing was over. \par \par \uc2      "If the authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again from Monday onwards, \par \par \uc2  then it will send a very strong signal suggesting that the \par \par \uc2  authorities have not been aiming to help firms window dress \par \par \uc2  their accounts but do indeed want the yen to weaken," said a \par \par \uc2  UBS Warburg note. \par \par \uc2      If so, then that will tend to limit the upside for regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar. \par \par \uc2      Players were also reluctant to take new fresh positions \par \par \uc2  ahead of a busy schedule next week with the Fed widely expected \par \par \uc2  to cut U.S. interest rates further and Japan is due to release \par \par \uc2  its September tankan business survey. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts reckon the Fed is likely to slash borrowing \par \par \uc2  costs by another 50 basis points when its policy makers meet on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday, and that some in this region will follow with easings \par \par \uc2  of their own. \par \par \uc2  As for Japan, economists polled by Reuters predicted the \par \par \uc2  tankan survey due on Monday would show sentiment deteriorated \par \par \uc2  sharply because of the global economic slowdown and the attacks \par \par \uc2  on the United States. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in the region, Korea is due to publish its August \par \par \uc2  industrial output data at 0300 GMT and Thailand is releasing \par \par \uc2  its monthly key economic data at 0800 GMT. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar slipped from levels seen late Thursday \par \par \uc2  in Asian trade of around 1.7612, but shied away from 1.7700 in \par \par \uc2  a market wary of building long U.S. dollar positions for now. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the U.S. dollar touched a high of 1.7689 \par \par \uc2  overnight as buy orders sent players scrambling to cover their \par \par \uc2  short dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  However, the U.S. unit's gains were limited around 1.7750 \par \par \uc2  - a level where many players suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at earlier in the week. \par \par \uc2  They said the Sing dollar would likely enter a \par \par \uc2  consolidation phase, having recovered from Monday's losses of \par \par \uc2  around 1.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won took its cue from the weakening yen and hit 1,311.5 \par \par \uc2  per dollar early - its lowest level in more than two months. \par \par \uc2  But the won swiftly bounced off intraday lows on \par \par \uc2  expectations that exporters would offload dollars ahead of \par \par \uc2  quarterly book closings, as in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2      The market was gearing up for a likely cut in interest \par \par \uc2  rates if the Fed eases after its FOMC meeting on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      The country's September consumer price index (CPI), the \par \par \uc2  broadest measure of inflation, was unchanged month-on-month \par \par \uc2  compared to a 0.5 percent rise in August, suggesting the Bank \par \par \uc2  of Korea still had leeway to ease credit further. \par \par \uc2      The ministry attributed the latest figures to lower prices \par \par \uc2  of agricultural and petroleum products. \par \par \uc2      On the year, CPI was up 3.2 percent in September versus 4.7 \par \par \uc2  percent the previous month. \par \par \uc2      Meanwhile, core inflation -- which excludes noncereal and \par \par \uc2  fuel prices - rose 3.6 percent on the year, but was below the \par \par \uc2  BOK's upper target of four percent for the first time this \par \par \uc2  year. \par \par \uc2      All eyes will be on August industrial output data due at \par \par \uc2  around 0300 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah continued to languish below 9,600 to the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par despite news that the Paris Club of official creditors has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par backed the second phase of a two-year debt rescheduling deal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with Indonesia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Thursday the Paris Club\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had contacted it and other creditor nations to say there was no\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par disagreement in approving the deal. Indonesian President\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Megawati Sukarnoputri is in Japan on a state visit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jakarta dealers, however, said the agreement was long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected. They added the market was more concerned with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par threat of a U.S. attack on Afghanistan following the September\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 11 tragedy and the possible reverberations it may have at home.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Though a minority, Indonesia's Muslim radicals have raised\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fears of political instability with their calls for a jihad if\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the U.S. retaliates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Megawati condemned the attacks on the U.S. on Thursday, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stopped short of declaring Jakarta's support if the U.S. does\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par take military action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht retreated below 44.40, alongside the yen and other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in early thin trade. But exporter dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offers above that level should provide a solid support for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Charts show 44.50 remained a good barrier for the dollar as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it represents the 61.8 percent retracement of the September\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 11-September 17 dollar downmove.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market awaits economic data to be released by the Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Thailand later in the day, including trade numbers, current\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par account balance and industrial production.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso opened lower at 51.39 to the dollar compared with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 51.365 at the close on Thursday to miror weakness in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers in Manila expected the peso to hold at 51.50 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fears of potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the macro front, the country's value of production index\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rose 11.4 percent year-on-year in July, while the volume of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par production index fell 2.1 percent, according to data released\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earlier in the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar continued to steer a steady course thanks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to month-end U.S. dollar sales by exporters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been in the market to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par keep the local dollar within a well-behaved range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Still, they said the Taiwan dollar would likely weaken in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the long term as the island's economy struggles through the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par double shock of a likely U.S. recession and the electronics\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par downturn.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan's economics minister said on Thursday a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par long-awaited recovery would be further delayed after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par September 11 attacks on the U.S. The government is projecting a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0.37 decline in 2001 gross domestic product - Taiwan's first\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ever full-year contraction.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0127 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.41       118.63         -0.65\par  Sing dlr      1.7638       1.7612         -0.15\par  Taiwan dlr    34.532       34.548         +0.05\par  Korean won   1309.5       1304.25         -0.40\par  Baht           44.41        44.35         -0.14\par  Peso           51.32        51.37         +0.09\par  Rupiah       9675.00      9655.00         -0.21\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.41       114.45         -4.15\par  Sing dlr      1.7638       1.7365         -1.55\par  Taiwan dlr    34.532       32.900         -4.73\par  Korean won   1297.00      1277.00         -1.54\par  Baht           44.41        43.70         -1.60\par  Peso           51.32        50.75         -1.11\par  Rupiah       9675.00      9470.00         -2.12\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010928dx9s003ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
