\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Mixed as domestic factors outweigh dlr/yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,140 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2001\par 11:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 27 (Reuters) - Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  mixed in late Thursday trade with domestic factors for once \par \par \uc2  outweighing the Bank of Japan's latest effort to weaken the yen \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2      A move by dollar/yen above 118 per dollar following yet \par \par \uc2  more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan had a limited impact as \par \par \uc2  genuine corporate flows held sway in cautious Asian trade. \par \par \uc2      The most significant move of the day was seen in the \par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar which clawed back around 0.4 percent of its \par \par \uc2  recent losses, triggering speculation the monetary authorities \par \par \uc2  may have entered the market to limit volatility. \par \par \uc2      Dealers also had a wary eye on other central banks as talk \par \par \uc2  circulated the authorities in the Philippines might sell \par \par \uc2  dollars to shore up peso confidence if it fell to 51.40 levels. \par \par \uc2      Financial markets continued to await America's next steps \par \par \uc2  to avenge the attacks on New York's twin towers and the \par \par \uc2  Pentagon on September 11, fearing that a worse-case scenario \par \par \uc2  could spark a costly war. \par \par \uc2      Markets were also gearing up for next Tuesday's U.S. \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve meeting as more rate cuts in the United States \par \par \uc2  were likely to prompt some Asian central banks to follow suit. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar gained sharply as those who overbought the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar and Australian dollar in the past few sessions unwound\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par their long positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A break above 1.7620 also triggered some stop-loss selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the U.S. dollar, but some bargain hunting emerged once U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dropped to 1.7585.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     There was talk the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might have been in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market to stave off volatility.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "European and American names had sold the U.S. dollar quite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a bit today. There are rumours the MAS was on both ends of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market to smooth out volatility, but we can't get a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par confirmation on this," said a dealer at a European bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Sing/Aussie cross had another wild session, with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Australian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sliding afresh to S$0.8570 after hitting a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high as S$0.8797 on Wednesday. The recent volatility in this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pair has stirred speculation of possible M&A flows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah retained its weak tone as heavy corporate dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand overshadowed news of Paris Club of creditors backing the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par second phase of a two-year debt-rescheduling deal with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It managed to bounce off intraday trading lows of 9,725 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar profit-taking and offers from a state bank, but dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in Jakarta doubted if Bank Indonesia was behind sales.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Of course, the Paris Club news is good news, but its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par impact might be offset a bit by strong seasonal demand for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar," said a dealer at one European bank in Jakarta.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "One onshore company placed a buying order of around $300\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million and another around $100 million. That's a lot for a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par thin market like this," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Concerns over fresh violence also clouded the rupiah. A\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hardline Muslim youth group warned on Thursday anyone backing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Washington's self-declared war on terrorism should leave\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia or risk being forced out.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Corporate demand for dollars as month end approached and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par negative sentiment towards the domestic economy weighed on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par peso although losses were limited amid talk the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around the 51.40 to 51.50 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All eyes were on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which decided to keep its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par key overnight rates unchanged at its weekly policy-making\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monetary Board meeting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The International Monetary Fund said on Thursday that there\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was still some room for monetary easing given that inflation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was likely to remain within official targets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  brought more gloom to the market after\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deputy governor Amando Tetangco told reporters the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's annual imports would drop three percent this year as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par manufacturers adjusted to slowing demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank governor Rafael Buenaventura said on Wednesday that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par merchandise exports were expected to fall by 15 percent on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year in 2001 due to a slowdown in the U.S. and Japan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar eked out some gains despite the weaker\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen, falling local stocks and dismal economic fundamentals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dealers said exporters' dollar sales ahead of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month-end sent the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher. They added trading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest was lacklustre with volumes thin.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The cabinet level Council of Economic Planning and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Development said earlier in the day its index of leading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par indicator rose 1.3 percent in August from the previous month to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 94. However, it said the economy slowed that month, making it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the ninth month in a row of slowdown.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht sat pat in a tight range of 44.30-44.38 as players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remaind wary of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bangkok dealers said trading activity has been subdued\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since a Japanese bank based in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars on Wednesday, sparking talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . However,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some dealers dismissed the rumours.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Offshore players were spotted buying dollars against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht on the back of the greenback's gains against the yen. But\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par those bids were met by offers from exporters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Baht funding costs in the offshore market rose slightly,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the one-month tenor quoted at 7/9 satang per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won closed lower at 1,306.4 per dollar on Thursday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against 1,305.0 at the Wednesday's close on the back of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weaker yen and dollar demand from importers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Sentiment was also dampened by the country's deteriorating\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par external account. The Bank of Korea said the nation posted a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par current account deficit of $110.7 million in August - the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first deficit in 16 months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Vice Finance Minister Kim Jin-pyo told reporters he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected a current account surplus of about $10 billion for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2001 and GDP growth of more than 0.5 percent in the third\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0830 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     118.76       117.30         -1.23\par  Sing dlr      1.7617       1.7693         +0.43\par  Taiwan dlr    34.548       34.568         +0.06\par  Korean won   1304.25      1302.00         -0.17\par  Baht           44.33        44.39         +0.14\par  Peso           51.35        51.30         -0.09\par  Rupiah       9680.00      9620.00         -0.62\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.76       102.21        -13.94\par  Sing dlr      1.7617       1.6640         -5.55\par  Taiwan dlr    34.548       31.380         -9.17\par  Korean won   1304.25      1135.00        -12.98\par  Baht           44.33        37.45        -15.52\par  Peso           51.35        40.20        -21.71\par  Rupiah       9680.00      6975.00        -27.94\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.8000         +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010927dx9r00ida\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
