\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets - Run for cover, nowhere to hide. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Tamora Vidaillet \par \uc2 1,037 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2001\par 12:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 21 (Reuters) - Asian stock markets crumpled \par \par \uc2  to their lowest levels in months on Friday, hit by worries over \par \par \uc2  exactly what kind of war America might wage against terrorism. \par \par \uc2      Sentiment had already been bruised by sharp losses on Wall \par \par \uc2  Street the session before and things turned brutal when \par \par \uc2  President George W. Bush declared the hour for military action \par \par \uc2  was approaching. \par \par \uc2      If a conflict were to erupt, scarring consumer sentiment in \par \par \uc2  the United States and elsewhere, the world could easily tip into \par \par \uc2  recession and bring even more pain to suffering Asian economies. \par \par \uc2      The prospective battle field also happens to be in Asia's \par \par \uc2  backyard, so threats of military action do not go down as well \par \par \uc2  here as they might in the United States. \par \par \uc2      With America rapidly deploying warplanes and aircraft \par \par \uc2  carrier groups to the Middle East and the Indian Ocean, Bush \par \par \uc2  told Taliban rulers in Afghanistan to surrender militant Osama \par \par \uc2  bin Laden and his followers or "share in their fate". \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore's Straits Times Index        and Hong Kong's Hang\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Seng were the hardest hit after their markets gapped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower at the open, fuelling heavy sales from the outset.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taiwan stocks ended at an eight and a half-year low while\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the the Philippine market closed at a three-year trough.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Heightened uncertainties spurred caution in the Asian bond\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market as investors squared positions to avoid potential fallout\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over the weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Spreads on Asian dollar bonds moved out by around 10 to 15\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par basis points (bps) after widening by some five to 10 bps in New\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par York overnight.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     DOLLAR THREAT LIMITED?\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some analysts played down the threat of war, saying likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par events could have a limited impact on markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "When we talk about war I think it is very important to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par qualify the type of war that can happen...there is no declared\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par enemy," Dominique Dwor-Frecaut, director of research at Barclays\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Capital, told Reuters Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Yes, the (U.S.) dollar could lose a bit of its safe haven\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par status but I don't think we are going back to a world war two\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par type of situation," she said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In the relatively illiquid Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par immediate focus remained centred on the yen , with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese officials confirming the Bank of Japan (BOJ) had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unilaterally bought dollars to weaken the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The BOJ had already \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell yen on Monday and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Moves to weaken the export-crimping Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  helped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par distance Asian regionals from their recent highs, calming fears\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the regional central banks at least for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par STILL ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ALERT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, despite the potential for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower, some markets remained wary of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the future.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (MAS) was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to guide its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower given savage falls in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par city-state's exports recently.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The bank could also take a lead from this week's credit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par easing by other central banks around the globe. Unlike most\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian countries which adjust interest rates to tweak monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par policy, Singapore favours its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as a policy tool.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We are seeing such a massive slowdown in Singapore, they\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par really do need to do something to try and ameliorate the impact\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the slowdown on the export side," said Andrew Fung, head of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par treasury at Rabobank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "So long as we're in this kind of behaviour where\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves the yen by only 100 bps, then we will need\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to see some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the MAS," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Otherwise, central banks were likely to keep a close eye on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if their respective\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decoupled from the broader Asian trend, analysts\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was a case in point given that it had fallen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par substantially in recent days amid strong commercial appetite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for U.S. dollars as well as domestic factors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite being export-dependant, particular weakness in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah compared to other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia could give the wrong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par signals to would-be investors and make it hard for corporates to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par re-pay foreign debt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I'm not really sure whether one can characterise some Asian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par central banks being at odds with what the BOJ is doing, apart\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from Indonesia where movement in the rupiah has been out of line\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with what was going on with dollar/yen," said Rabobank's Fung.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Cha