\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Jolted by BOJ, Bush speech digested. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,069 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2001\par 04:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 21 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  see-saw \par \par \uc2  once again as the yen first rises only to fall in the face of \par \par \uc2  apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2      Yen had hit 7-month highs on the dollar around 115.85 \par \par \uc2  following steep losses on Wall Street and mounting concerns \par \par \uc2  that the September 11 assault on the U.S. would push the global \par \par \uc2  economy into recession. \par \par \uc2  But the yen - tracked closely by regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - pared \par \par \uc2  gains in early trade due to fears of potential BOJ \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And they did not have long to wait with the \par \par \uc2  dollar jumping to 116.87 yen on what dealers assumed was BOJ \par \par \uc2  buying. \par \par \uc2  If so this would be the third session this week that the \par \par \uc2  Jaspanese have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try and limit the yen's gains, \par \par \uc2  though with limited success given the dollar started the week \par \par \uc2  around 118.00. \par \par \uc2  Activity was subdued overall in Asia as players watched \par \par \uc2  President George W. Bush giving a keynote speech to a joint \par \par \uc2  session of Congress, hoping for clues on what the U.S. will do \par \par \uc2  to punish the perpetrators. \par \par \uc2  Many also opted to take a wait-and-see stance ahead of a \par \par \uc2  fresh batch of data to be released by the U.S. and the region \par \par \uc2  next week. \par \par \uc2  U.S. consumer confidence data - a key leading indicator of \par \par \uc2  economic growth - are out on Tuesday. This will be the first \par \par \uc2  survey after the aerial attacks on the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand will release its key monthly economic \par \par \uc2  data including trade, balance of payment and industrial output \par \par \uc2  on September 28. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was trapped in a tight range early, \par \par \uc2  having rallied to 1.7375 from intraday low of around 1.7460 per \par \par \uc2  dollar hit the previous day. \par \par \uc2  But the Sing was barely changed compared to levels seen \par \par \uc2  late on Thursday when heavy U.S. dollar sales by at least one \par \par \uc2  U.S. name lifted the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its lows. \par \par \uc2  One dealer from a European bank said the market was still \par \par \uc2  intent on offloading U.S. dollars, with the main market focus \par \par \uc2  centred on movements in dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  But dealers expected potential gains on the Sing dollar to \par \par \uc2  be limited given the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the possibility the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) might enter the market to \par \par \uc2  limit volatility. \par \par \uc2  There has been talk that the MAS may have made efforts to \par \par \uc2  guide the Sing lower this week following credit easing by many \par \par \uc2  central banks in response to last week's attacks on the United \par \par \uc2  States. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar, believed to have been trading at the \par \par \uc2  extreme strong end of its supposed trading range of late, is \par \par \uc2  one of Singapore's main monetary policy tools. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won came off overnight highs around 1,288 to stand at \par \par \uc2  1,295 in line with the yen with the upside was seen limited by \par \par \uc2  declines in domestic stocks. \par \par \uc2  By 0106 GMT, the benchmark KOSPI stock index was \par \par \uc2  down 2.74 percent at 467 points following continued falls on \par \par \uc2  Wall Street in the wake of last week's attacks. \par \par \uc2  Won sentiment was slightly boosted by expected month-end \par \par \uc2  dollar sales by exporters and confirmation that General Motors \par \par \uc2   would buy troubled Daewoo Motor. \par \par \uc2  General Motors said it would sign an MOU this morning to \par \par \uc2  take over two Daewoo Motor plants in South Korea with a final \par \par \uc2  deal expected by year's end. \par \par \uc2  On the non-deliverable forward market, the one-month won at \par \par \uc2  1,298.2/99.2 per dollar against 1,299.3/1,300.3 late on \par \par \uc2  Thursday. The six-month won was quoted at 1,302.0/03.0 against \par \par \uc2  1,308.5/09.5. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht retained its firm tone at 44.15 but the market \par \par \uc2  found few incentives to push it above 44.00 amid wariness of \par \par \uc2  BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, baht funding costs remained largely \par \par \uc2  steady in both offshore and onshore markets because there was \par \par \uc2  not much activity going on. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Tourism Authority of Thailand (TAT) said it \par \par \uc2  had lowered the visitor arrival forecast to 9.68 million from \par \par \uc2  10.3 million in the wake of attacks in the U.S. \par \par \uc2      Revenues from tourists made a substantial contribution to \par \par \uc2  Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  incomes. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso barely traded early around 51.24 as players were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par glued to TV sets, listening to what President George Bush has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to say to a joint session of Congress.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The market is watching for clues on what he is going to do\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as far as military retaliation is concerned," said a Manila\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bush said the evidence the U.S. has gathered all points to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Osama bin Laden's militant group and made a list of demands of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Afghanistan's ruling Taliban.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso closed at 51.29 in on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah was marked up in thin early trade to 9,440 due\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to a combination of firmer regionals and fears of local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank Indonesia was rumoured to have sold the dollar at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 9,550-9,600 on Thursday to shore up the rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But its gains should be capped by persistent dollar demand\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from onshore companies and lingering concerns over the fate of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $8.8 billion debt talk with Paris Club of creditors which has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been stalled since the attacks on the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0132 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     116.45       117.34         +0.76\par  Sing dlr      1.7365       1.7419         +0.31\par  Taiwan dlr    34.569       34.575         +0.02\par  Korean won   1295.00      1298.50         +0.27\par  Baht           44.14        44.20         +0.14\par  Peso           51.20        51.29         +0.18\par  Rupiah       9430.00      9450.00         +0.21\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.45       114.45         -1.72\par  Sing dlr      1.7365       1.7365         +0.00\par  Taiwan dlr    34.569       32.900         -4.83\par  Korean won   1295.00      1277.00         -1.39\par  Baht           44.14        43.70         -1.00\par  Peso           51.20        50.75         -0.88\par  Rupiah       9430.00      9470.00         +0.42\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010921dx9l000md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
