\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Soft as focus stays on BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 1,063 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2001\par 04:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sept 20 (Reuters) - Most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  softened in early Thursday trade, with north asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  in particular looking to the yen for direction amid \par \par \uc2  fears of repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Commercial dollar demand continued to dominate trading in \par \par \uc2  most Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which were expected to remain \par \par \uc2  weak in any case due to shaky investor confidence. \par \par \uc2      The market was on high alert for Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  aimed at weakening the yen after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  bought dollars for yen on Wednesday for a second time this \par \par \uc2  week. \par \par \uc2      But dealers said most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had limited room \par \par \uc2  to move lower given that fears of a U.S. global recession had \par \par \uc2  heightened in the wake of last week's attacks. \par \par \uc2      News that the United States was sending more combat \par \par \uc2  aircraft to the Middle East drew a mixed response. Some were \par \par \uc2  relieved to know the U.S. was doing something but at the same \par \par \uc2  time worried at the potential for a military conflict, \par \par \uc2  particularly as this region is a lot closer to Afghanistan than \par \par \uc2  the U.S. \par \par \uc2      Added to that was nervousness as governments prepared to \par \par \uc2  slash growth forecasts and companies warned of more job cuts, \par \par \uc2  heightening the threat of recession. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar shed around half a percent to 1.7455\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par amid talk that local banks were off loading the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "There is no fundamentral news. The talk is that local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks are selling Sing dollars but we cannot necessarily draw\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par conclusions from this," said a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst from a European\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers have given mixed accounts of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent days, with some saying it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was believed to have bought U.S. dollars in light of thee\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent credit easing by some central banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Others have said they have no evidence of such moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Despite appearing weak compared to its position last week,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is still moving around the stronger end of its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par assumed trading band and probably has room to drift lower,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par according to dealers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won weakened to 1298.0 on dollar demand from energy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par companies keen to hedge against potential volatility in oil\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prices following last week's attacks on the U.S..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Japan's desire to stem relative strength in the yen also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weighed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the non-deliverable forward market, the one-month won at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,300.6/01.6 per dollar, against 1,297.7/98.7 late on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday. The six-month won was quoted at 1,308.6/09.6 against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,305.5/06.5.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso opened unchanged at 51.40 in the onshore market as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market participants were cautious amid rumours the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was in the market to sell the U.S. dollar on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Manila expected the peso to move in a tight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range as corporate dollar demand linked to settlements in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-deliverable forward market was countered by fears of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Activity was brisk, with $36.50 million transacted within\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the first half hour of trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah remained at the wrong side of 9,500 per dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as the appetite for dollars, largely for genuine commercial\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand, continued to hold sway.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said they expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to try\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and guide the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher amid talk they had made efforts\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to do this earlier in the week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "If the authorities had come in this morning at 9,550, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah may have strengthened to 9,500 but as always they were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par too late," said a dealer from a European bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "They probably wil be in later as they've made it clear\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they want to defend the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indonesian President Megawati Sukarnoputri issued a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par statement after meeting Bush in the U.S. on Wednesday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par condemning last week's attacks on the U.S. as "barbaric and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par indiscriminate acts."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Megawati also pledged to cooperate with the international\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par community in combating terrorism.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bush pledged at least $130 million in aid for judicial and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par legal reform in Indonesia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Separately, the U.S. also said it would eliminate duties on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over $100 million of imports from Indonesia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     U.S. officials hope she will take a strong stance against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Islamic militants Washington believes were behind last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week's attacks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But several radical Indonesian Muslim groups have urged\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Megawati not to cave in to pressure and vowed to launch a holy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par war against the United States if Washington attacks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Afghanistan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht was a shade softer at 44.30 but still within its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent range as the market watched where the dollar/yen was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par heading amid a dearth of strong domestic factors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said players were waiting to pick up the dollar at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 44.00 and above, and to take profits below 44.20.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Charts show 44.65 is a strong support for the baht in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par near term as it represents the 38.2 percent retracement of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar's July 23-September 12 downmove.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar opened barely changed at 34.561 before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par edging slightly lower, with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expected to\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  both ways to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  steady.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was in the market on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday to curb gains in local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said losses in local stocks and the country's bleak\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic outlook should keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  below 34.50 in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par near term.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     117.53       118.96         +1.22\par  Sing dlr      1.7463       1.7370         -0.53\par  Taiwan dlr    34.610       34.572         -0.11\par  Korean won   1298.50      1290.00         -0.65\par  Baht           44.27        44.29         +0.05\par  Peso           51.39        51.27         -0.23\par  Rupiah       9580.00      9098.00         -5.03\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.53       114.45         -2.62\par  Sing dlr      1.7463       1.7365         -0.56\par  Taiwan dlr    34.610       32.900         -4.94\par  Korean won   1298.50      1277.00         -1.66\par  Baht           44.27        43.70         -1.29\par  Peso           51.39        50.75         -1.25\par  Rupiah       9580.00      9470.00         -1.15\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.8000         +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010920dx9k001eb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
