\par\par \b \uc2  SGX Nikkei 225 Futures End Up On Wall St,BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2001\par 10:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The Nikkei 225 stock index futures traded on the Singapore Exchange ended higher Wednesday, encouraged by Wall Street's resilience overnight and the Bank of Japan's move to push the yen lower against the U.S. dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Nikkei 225 December contract closed up 290 points at 9925 points, with 19,254 contracts traded. \par \par \uc2  On the spot market, the Nikkei 225 rose 2.7% to 9939.60 points. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they saw solid fresh buying supporting the market, amid hopes the selling pressure in U.S. stock markets may be tapering off. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday, the Dow Jones Industrial Average fell 17.30 points, or 0.2%, to 8903.40, while the Nasdaq lost 24.47 points, or 1.6%, to 1555.08. \par \par \uc2  In addition, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market earlier Wednesday improved sentiment on equities, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0806 GMT (4:06 a.m. EDT), the dollar was trading at Y117.59, compared with Y117.23 late Tuesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  A weaker yen would benefit Japanese exporters. \par \par \uc2  Despite the gains, the market's future direction remains unclear amid the current uncertainty over a possible military confrontation in Asia after the horrifying terrorist attacks against the U.S. last week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese equities markets will continue to take cues from Wall Street, they said. \par \par \uc2  The MSCI Taiwan stock index futures traded in Singapore ended lower, with the benchmark September contract down 3.8 points at 171.3. \par \par \uc2  On the spot market, the Weighted Price Index of the Taiwan Stock Exchange closed up 6.55 points, or 0.2%, at 3781.17 in dealings valued at NT$26.10 billion (US$1=NT$34.518). \par \par \uc2  Both the spot and futures markets for Taiwan equities were closed Monday and Tuesday due to damages caused by Typhoon Nari. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Selling pressure was heavy after two days of market closure, as\par investors tried to catch up with the recent sharp losses on Wall Street\par and other regional bourses, dealers said.\par                         Wednesday  Previous   Change (Pts)\par Nikkei 225 Dec          9925       9635       up 290\par Nikkei 300 Dec          208.0      202.0      up 6.0\par Nikkei 225 Spot Index   9939.60    9679.88    up 259.72\par MSCI Taiwan Sep         171.3      175.1      dn 3.8\par Taiwan Weighted Index   3781.17    3774.62    up 6.55\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Shen Hong, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-4154-156;\par hong.shen@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1095 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010919dx9j000id\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
