\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Roiled as Japan buys dollars for yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,129 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2001\par 04:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 18 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  turned \par \par \uc2  mixed in unsettled morning trade Wednesday after the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen for the second time in \par \par \uc2  three days. \par \par \uc2      Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had mostly started firmer  as the \par \par \uc2  dollar tracked losses in the U.S. stocks which ended at \par \par \uc2  three-year lows overnight. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But as the dollar drifted off toward 117.00 yen        a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par round of buy ordrers hit the market which dealers assumed were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from the BOJ and the dollar duly jumped to 117.75. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  confirmed it had ordered the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par signifying how serious their intent was.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In any case, with global investors more risk-averse after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par last week's plane attacks, they are tending to avoid peripheral\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indeed, traders suspect they would be selling Asian\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more actively if it were not for the lack of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par liquidity in local markets. Instead, they use the much more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par liquid markets in the Australian and New Zealand dollars and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sell those as a  proxy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar reversed early gains and followed the yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower to 1.7405 after the BOJ's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers were also wary of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since many assumed the MAS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par might want a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as a tacit easing in monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par policy following this week's round of global rate cuts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "While the Sing dollar looks set to continue to following\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen, the market needs to watch for any change of policy by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the MAS after this week's (non-oil exports data) showed exports\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par falling by early 30 percent year-on-year in August," said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mansoor Mohi-Uddin, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS Warburg.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Singapore's economy continues to be hit by the slowdown in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the economy globally and so undue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength appears\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unwarranted," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The South Korean won firmed to 1,295.0 per dollar, compared to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday's close of 1,296.9, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank of Korea trimmed borrowing costs by 50 basis points on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday, in line with moves by some other countries following\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par last week's attacks on the United States.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Chon Chol-hwan said there has not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been upward price pressure from the demand side despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par concerns the attacks could lead to higher oil prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Chon also said that the assault against the United States\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would prolong South Korea's economic slowdown.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said they expected dollar/won to trade between\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,292 and 1,297 on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In the non-deliverable forward market, the one-month won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was 1,296.1/97.1 per dollar, against 1,298.4/99.4 late on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday. The six-month won was quoted at 1,304.9/05.9 against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,307.4/08.4.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht also gave up early gains to stand at 44.20 in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wake of the BOJ's action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In any case, players were not willing to push the local\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  above 44.00 yet due to fears of dollar-buying\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, Commerce Minister Adisai Bodharamik estimated on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday that Thai exports were worth around $5.3-5.4 billion in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par August and that Thailand should manage to post a trade surplus\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the whole 2001.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Baht funding costs were mostly steady, with the tom/next\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate quoted at 0.25/0.40 satang per dollar and one-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forward rate at 7/11 satang in the offshore market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso opened at 51.365 to the dollar against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday's close of 51.37. Trading was thin, with only $2.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million transacted at 0120 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The country registered trade deficit of $66 million in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par July. But the trade during the first seven months of this year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remained in surplus.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH The rupiah slipped to the 9,625,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par driven by strong dollar demand in the past two days believed to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be linked largely to genuine commercial needs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One dealer from a European bank said the market looked\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "toppish" given dollar/rupiah had risen from 9,200 to 9,600\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this week despite the dollar's losses against many regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the wake of last week's attacks on the United\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par States.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I think the market will stop around here," said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "People that have gone long (dollars) don't dare keep their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions open for long at these levels," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers have said that they believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par made efforts to stem the rupiah's decline though moves had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appeared to be half-hearted up until now.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indonesia, home to the world's largest Muslim community\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said on Tuesday that it would step up intelligence efforts to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par keep terrorists out of the country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR          The Taiwan dollar remained firm\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 34.45 relative to its position ahead of last week's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attacks on the United States, with some dealers expecting more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollar weakness ahead.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All eyes were on how financial markets would fare following\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a two-day closure dictated by Typhoon Nari which brought floods\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to the island's capital and triggered the deaths of 66 people.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Though sentiment towards stocks was bearish, dealers said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they expected the Taiwan dollar to remain on the strong side of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its recent range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The U.S. dollar is likely to remain weak against North\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and any impact on stocks will be limited after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the government action," said a senior dealer from a U.S. house.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan's minister of finance said on Tuesday that the local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stock market's daily downward trading limit would be cut in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par half to 3.5 percent from September 19-28, while the upwards\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limit would remain at seven percent. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0217 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     117.96       117.90         -0.05\par  Sing dlr      1.7400       1.7376         -0.14\par  Taiwan dlr    34.495       34.575         +0.23\par  Korean won   1295.50      1297.00         +0.12\par  Baht           44.22        44.20         -0.05\par  Peso           51.35        51.37         +0.04\par  Rupiah       9650.00      9540.00         -1.14\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.96       114.45         -2.98\par  Sing dlr      1.7400       1.7365         -0.20\par  Taiwan dlr    34.495       32.900         -4.62\par  Korean won   1295.50      1277.00         -1.43\par  Baht           44.22        43.70         -1.18\par  Peso           51.35        50.75         -1.17\par  Rupiah       9650.00      9470.00         -1.87\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010919dx9j0018y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
