\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Bolstered as dlr wilts ahead of Wall St. \b0\par\par\uc2 956 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2001\par 04:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 17 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged ahead \par \par \uc2  in early trade on Monday as nervous investors stayed away from \par \par \uc2  the U.S. dollar ahead of Wall Street's reopening. \par \par \uc2      Poor U.S. industrial data released Friday also weighed on \par \par \uc2  sentiment. The data showed industrial production fell for the \par \par \uc2  11th straight month in August, while capacity utilisation fell \par \par \uc2  to lowest level since July 1983. \par \par \uc2  But gains were likely to be capped by wariness of potential \par \par \uc2  dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by major central banks, particularly \par \par \uc2  from Japan which is desperate to restrain the yen - a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  closely tracked by the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I don't think Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will rise much further from \par \par \uc2  here. Many in the market expect the Fed to act today when the \par \par \uc2  markets reopen and major central banks are not going to let the \par \par \uc2  dollar fall like a stone," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  "And if the U.S. strikes back, and we believe they will, \par \par \uc2  I'm sure the market will be more risk averse. In that \par \par \uc2  situation, the dollar is likely to be in demand. We still think \par \par \uc2  this is a good opportunity for the market to accumulate \par \par \uc2  dollars," he said. \par \par \uc2  Money markets in the U.S. have already moved to price in \par \par \uc2  further aggressive easing from the Federal Reserve with many \par \par \uc2  expecting it could even cut later today. \par \par \uc2  The market is also watching the Bank of Japan's meeting \par \par \uc2  later this week amid speculation it may take further steps to \par \par \uc2  show its resolve in stemming deflation and preventing a weak \par \par \uc2  Japan from contributing to a global economic slowdown. \par \par \uc2      Elsewhere in the region, Taiwan's financial markets are \par \par \uc2  closed on Monday as the island braced for Typhoon Nari. \par \par \uc2      Singapore is due to release August non-oil domestic export \par \par \uc2  data at 0430 GMT, with most economists expecting a deeper slide \par \par \uc2  in exports after a 24.2 percent year-on-year contraction in \par \par \uc2  July. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was marked up to 1.7315 in early trade - \par \par \uc2  its best level since January 22. There was still no inter-bank \par \par \uc2  trading, with deals going through brokers. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating much \par \par \uc2  past the key level of 1.7300. \par \par \uc2  "There is no good news from the local front but the Sing \par \par \uc2  dollar has strengthened primarily on the back of a firmer yen," \par \par \uc2  said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  "Also, we believe local companies are unlikely to be \par \par \uc2  aggressive in buying overseas assets in this kind of \par \par \uc2  environment," he said. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht moved up to the morning high of 43.98 in early \par \par \uc2  thin trade to mirror gains in the regionals as onshore and \par \par \uc2  offshore players unwound long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2      There is still no direct quotes for the baht in the onshore \par \par \uc2  market. \par \par \uc2      Thailand's macro picture remains bleak. A local newspaper \par \par \uc2  quoted the National Economic and Social Development Board - a \par \par \uc2  government think tank - as saying the country's exports were \par \par \uc2  likely to fall over 6.0 percent in 2001. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won tracked a firmer yen higher as players were \par \par \uc2  reluctant to buy the U.S. dollar, fearing steep losses when \par \par \uc2  Wall Street reopens. \par \par \uc2      The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened at 1,290 before edging lower to \par \par \uc2  1.294 compared with the Friday's close of 1,296.3. \par \par \uc2      Gains were likely to be limited by losses in local stocks \par \par \uc2  which has shed 2.62 percent at 0125 GMT. \par \par \uc2      Meanwhile, the country posted a record $100.04 billion in \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves as of September 15 compared with \par \par \uc2  $99.03 billion at the end of August. \par \par \uc2      The increase was attributed to steady repayment of foreign \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated loans by financial institutions to the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a higher conversion value of euro and yen \par \par \uc2  holdings which increased the dollar value in the reserves. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was little moved from levels seen late on Friday \par \par \uc2  around 9,100 as players awaited direction from U.S. markets. \par \par \uc2  Traders were cautious after last week's terror attacks in the \par \par \uc2  U.S. disrupted a meeting between the government and the Paris \par \par \uc2  Club of creditors. \par \par \uc2      "The focus is very much on the U.S.. We are still looking \par \par \uc2  for direction," said a dealer from a European bank. \par \par \uc2      "Some people are dollar bearish because the U.S. economy \par \par \uc2  will suffer more, but there is little to cheer about in the \par \par \uc2  rupiah," he said. \par \par \uc2      The rupiah was seen trading in the range of 9,000 and 9,200 \par \par \uc2  while corporate activity was expected to pick up later in the \par \par \uc2  day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      Indonesia earlier this month asked the Paris Club to \par \par \uc2  reschedule $6 billion in foreign debt falling due between April \par \par \uc2  2002 and March 2004 to ease pressure on the ailing budget. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0139 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     117.20       118.91         +1.46\par  Sing dlr      1.7322       1.7371         +0.28\par  Taiwan dlr    34.575       34.579         +0.01\par  Korean won   1294.50      1295.00         +0.04\par  Baht           43.98        44.22         +0.55\par  Rupiah       9110.00      9113.00         +0.03\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.20       114.45         -2.35\par  Sing dlr      1.7322       1.7365         +0.25\par  Taiwan dlr    34.575       32.900         -4.84\par  Korean won   1294.50      1277.00         -1.35\par  Baht           43.98        43.70         -0.64\par  Peso           51.05        50.75         -0.59\par  Rupiah       9110.00      9470.00         +3.95\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010917dx9h003v2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw18