\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Firmer as dollar sags, awaits U.S. cue. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,070 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2001\par 04:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 14 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly \par \par \uc2  firmer in early trade on Friday with shakey dollar sentiment \par \par \uc2  undermined further by bearish U.S. consumer confidence data. \par \par \uc2      The University of Michigan consumer sentiment index, \par \par \uc2  released on Thursday, showed a sharp 7.9 point fall to 83.6 in \par \par \uc2  September, its lowest level in nearly eight years. And that was \par \par \uc2  before the terror attacks earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  Cautious market players kept their trading activity to a \par \par \uc2  bare minimum, although there had been few reports of settlement \par \par \uc2  or clearing problems so far. \par \par \uc2  There is still no interbank trading in most markets in the \par \par \uc2  region on Friday, with deals carried out through brokers or \par \par \uc2  electronic broking systems. \par \par \uc2  "The market is waiting for the U.S. stock markets to reopen \par \par \uc2  on Monday to see if they function smoothly, which direction \par \par \uc2  they head, etc," said a senior dealer at an Asian bank in \par \par \uc2  Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "Interbank players in Singapore will reassess the situation \par \par \uc2  again later today, and I believe by Monday or Tuesday we will \par \par \uc2  be able to quote directly again," he said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. stock markets will reopen for business on Monday, \par \par \uc2  nearly a week after an attack demolished the World Trade \par \par \uc2  Center, killing perhaps thousands and triggering longest \par \par \uc2  shutdown in trading since the outbreak of World War I. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was quoted in a 1.7360-1.7385 range in thin \par \par \uc2  trade, tracking the dollar/yen closely amid a dearth of strong \par \par \uc2  local leads. \par \par \uc2  The market is cautious to push the Sing dollar up much \par \par \uc2  higher, fearing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might step in to curb its \par \par \uc2  appreciation due to the country's weak economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  Economists are betting the terror attacks in the U.S. will \par \par \uc2  lower growth rates in Asia and delay economic recovery - a \par \par \uc2  view which puts further strain on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At the current level, the U.S. dollar/Sing dollar is \par \par \uc2  hovering just above the oversold line on the 14-day relative \par \par \uc2  strength index, with a reading of 33. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht also edged higher alongside the regionals although \par \par \uc2  corporate dollar bargain hunting capped its gains at around \par \par \uc2  44.15. \par \par \uc2  But like most centers in the region, trading activity in \par \par \uc2  Bangkok was subdued as most interbank players sat on their \par \par \uc2  hands. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Thailand will go ahead with the sale of more \par \par \uc2  Thai Airways shares in November despite their dive to a record \par \par \uc2  low this week following the attacks in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The government wants to reduce its stake in the national \par \par \uc2  carrier to 70 percent from 93 percent. More than 10 percent \par \par \uc2  could be offered to a strategic partner. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won eased in anticipation of equity-related outflow of \par \par \uc2  dollars and on demand from oil importers. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said overall trade was still subdued \par \par \uc2  on settlement worries and as interbank players awaited \par \par \uc2  retaliatory action of the U.S. against perpetrators of the \par \par \uc2  September 11 attacks. \par \par \uc2  Finance and Economy Minister Jin Nyum said interest rates \par \par \uc2  would be kept low and ample liquidity would be provided for the \par \par \uc2  financial system as the attacks were likely delay a recovey. \par \par \uc2  In a briefing to President Kim Dae Jung, he said the \par \par \uc2  government was ready to inject emergency liquidity to stem \par \par \uc2  sharp fluctuations in the won. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar rose in line with the yen and on an \par \par \uc2  expected inflow of dollars from foreign funds that had been net \par \par \uc2  buyers in local stocks, despite recent losses in the benchmark \par \par \uc2  TAIEX index. \par \par \uc2  But dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in the market on Thursday, was expected \par \par \uc2  to keep the upside capped. \par \par \uc2  Foreign funds were net buyers of 1.49 billion Taiwan \par \par \uc2  dollars worth of local stocks on Thursday, bringing total net \par \par \uc2  buying to 2.46 billion Taiwan dollars over the past three \par \par \uc2  sessions. \par \par \uc2  Amid high expectations of further policy easing, the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it would hold its quarterly board \par \par \uc2  meeting on September 26 to review monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan has trimmed its discount rate and the accommodation \par \par \uc2  with collateral rate eight times since December 2000, bringing \par \par \uc2  them to record lows of 3.250 percent and 3.625 percent \par \par \uc2  respectively. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINES PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso edged up to 51.24 per dollar, taking its cue from \par \par \uc2  other regionals but dealers in Manila said dollar demand from \par \par \uc2  corporates and oil importers could weigh it down. \par \par \uc2      They said uncertainty in global markets would continue to \par \par \uc2  keep most interbank players cautious. \par \par \uc2      Energy Secretary Vince Perez said on Thursday the country \par \par \uc2  would suspend exports of petroleum products to ensure stocks, \par \par \uc2  following this week's terror attacks in the United States. \par \par \uc2      The Philippines imports all its crude requirements but \par \par \uc2  exports a small amount of products when refinery output exceeds \par \par \uc2  local consumption. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Local corporates seeking dollars for immediate import and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par debt payment needs were expected to keep the rupiah weighed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par down.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would cap the downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was in the market on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday at around 9,140 and its dollar sales helped the rupiah\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bounce off session low of 9,175. It was hovering at 9,100 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In what was seen as a major positive development, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government won vital parliamentary approval on Thursday to sell\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its majority stake in the top retail bank - Bank Central Asia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The vote was seen as a test of relations between President\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Megawati Sukarnoputri's new government and parliament.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0135 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     118.89       118.96         +0.06\par  Sing dlr      1.7383       1.7370         -0.07\par  Taiwan dlr    34.537       34.579         +0.12\par  Korean won   1297.00      1290.00         -0.54\par  Baht           44.20        44.29         +0.20\par  Peso           51.23        51.28         +0.10\par  Rupiah       9100.00      9098.00         -0.02\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.89       114.45         -3.73\par  Sing dlr      1.7383       1.7365         -0.10\par  Taiwan dlr    34.537       32.900         -4.74\par  Korean won   1297.00      1277.00         -1.54\par  Baht           44.20        43.70         -1.13\par  Peso           51.23        50.75         -0.94\par  Rupiah       9100.00      9470.00         +4.07\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010914dx9e004bu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
