\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late As Dlr Tumbles After Attacks \b0\par\par\uc2 635 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2001\par 10:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was sharply higher late Wednesday as the U.S. dollar fell against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following suspected terrorist attacks in the U.S. Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0805 GMT (4:05 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7360 down from S$1.7539 late Tuesday in Asia. It traded between S$1.7340 and S$1.7390, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In one of the most horrifying attacks ever against the U.S., terrorists Tuesday crashed two airliners into the World Trade Center in New York and a third plane slammed into the U.S. Defense Department in Washington. A fourth airliner crashed in a field around 128 kilometers southeast of Pittsburgh. No one has yet claimed responsibility for the attacks. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened sharply lower in Asia, following its overnight plunge against the yen, the euro, and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after U.S. markets were suspended. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar dipped several times against the local Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  largely in line with its weakness against other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but was kept fairly buoyed near S$1.7340, as rumors of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  emerged. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was kept to a tight range for much of the Asian day as market participants mainly remained on the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  Market participants were also unwilling to actively take positions on fears that the suspension of U.S. markets would create problems when transactions had to be settled, dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar is expected to come under further pressure in London\par with U.S. markets still suspended. The U.S. dollar is expected to trade\par between S$1.7340-S$1.7370 overnight.\par - - 12/09/01 08-27G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prices of Singapore government bonds were also sharply higher\par Wednesday as the attacks fueled fears of a collapse in the U.S. economy,\par dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bonds were, however, traded very thinly after the early morning jump,\par which was largely perceived as a knee-jerk reaction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yield on two-year bonds was down three basis points at 2.16% while\par the yield on five-year bonds was down two basis points at 2.85%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds was down\par two basis points at 3.23% while the yield on 10-year bonds was down two\par basis points at 3.50%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yield on 15-year bonds was also down two basis points at 3.75%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and\par are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be\par viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:\par \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swaps were lower, tracking local\par bond yields. Swaps were barely traded Wednesday with only some brokers\par seen quoting prices earlier but without any takers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The most liquid seven-year swap offer closed down three basis points\par at 3.36% while the 10-year swap offer closed two basis points lower at\par 3.59%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between the two- and 10-year swaps widened to 101 basis\par points from 99.5 basis points late Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank money market, overnight rates initially inched up on\par liquidity concerns, dealers said. But rates then eased as liquidity\par remained sufficient, while term rates were flat.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Wednesday    Late Tuesday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.0625% 0.1875%   1.6250% 1.7500%\par 3-Month           2.1250% 2.2500%   2.1250% 2.2500%\par 1-Year            2.2500% 2.3750%   2.2500% 2.3750%\par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par -0- 12/09/01 08-50G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010912dx9c000lq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
