\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Bow to dollar, wait on O'Neill. \b0\par\par\uc2 902 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2001\par 04:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 11 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stumbled \par \par \uc2  lower early on Tuesday as dollar bulls bought back the U.S. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Wall Street bounced from the brink overnight \par \par \uc2  while its peers in Tokyo and Europe suffered losses. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were likely to face \par \par \uc2  further downside risks given the yen's bleak outlook and a \par \par \uc2  dearth of good news from the domestic front. \par \par \uc2      "We see recent gains in the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a good \par \par \uc2  opportunity to buy dollars on dips. Fundamental stories do not \par \par \uc2  support the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Syetarn Hansakul, \par \par \uc2  regional economist at WestLB in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      "A major risk would come from the yen which gets little \par \par \uc2  help from either trade or portfolio inflows. We expect the yen \par \par \uc2  to drop to 122 in one month and 124 in three months," she said. \par \par \uc2      The regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly range-bound, alongside \par \par \uc2  the dollar/yen, ahead of a meeting between U.S. Treasury \par \par \uc2  Secretary Paul O'Neil and Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      The market also awaits a string of key U.S. data due later \par \par \uc2  this week, including retail sales numbers on Friday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar lurched lower to 1.7510 as the U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regained its strength against the yen and the euro - both\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par carry substantial weight in Singapore's trade-weighted basket\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market talk that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore (MAS)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was in the market on Monday to support the U.S. dollar at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1.7460 also made players reluctant to get too short of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the greenback.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts believed the Sing dollar's recent gains were just\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a blip as they were not justified by fundamentals and suspect\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would soon encourage the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     WestLB's Hansakul forecast the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would slide\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 1.7550 in one month and 1.7800 in three months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON        -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won, which closely tracks the yen, was trading lower at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,293.5 compared with 1,290.3 at the close on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers in Singapore expected some dollar profit taking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to emerge soon as American International Group is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moving closer to buying control of Hyundai Securities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  and the market assumes some sort of flows into won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par will result if the deal goes through.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In the non-deliverable forward market, the one-month won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par traded at 1,293/1,295 and three-month at 1,296/1,298.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso lingered around the 51 per dollar level with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market focused on moves in other regionals amid a lack of fresh\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local leads.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said sporadic dollar buying by corporates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and importers had kept the peso locked in a tight 51.20-51.40\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par band but few players were showing interest to probe the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said in recent weeks the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had repeatedly\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot and the non-deliverable forward market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to keep the peso from breaching the 51.50 level, a level not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seen since August 13.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  denies the market talk but has said it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would act to stem speculation and volatile moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht edged down taking the cue from other regionals and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers in Singapore said rising baht funding costs in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore market could pull the baht lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen's overnight losses against the dollar prompted some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore players to cover their short dollar positions and to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hedge their recent investments in the local equity market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the baht may test 44.90, the 50 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par retracement of its August 1 to September 4 upmove, a break of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which could lead to lower levels beyond the 45 per dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par boundary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah bobbed around the 9,000 per dollar level,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weighed down by local corporates seeking dollars for debt and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par import needs but supported by fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the market was closely watching\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the majority disinvestment of Bank Central Asia, the country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par largest retail bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The government expects parliament to approve the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par disinvestment in the next couple of weeks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Parliament's approval to sell 51 percent stake of BCA to a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strategic investor is seen as a test of President Megawati\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sukarnoputri's commitment ability to deliver on reforms agreed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the International Monetary Fund.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The IMF resumed lending to Indonesia on Monday, freeing up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $395 million of stalled loans after the government agreed a new\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reform package.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ASIAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.17       120.04         -0.93\par  Sing dlr      1.7510       1.7478         -0.18\par  Taiwan dlr    34.658       34.651         -0.02\par  Korean won   1292.00      1285.00         -0.54\par  Baht           44.63        44.50         -0.29\par  Peso           51.28        51.21         -0.14\par  Rupiah       9030.00      9050.00         +0.22\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7998         +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     121.17       114.45         -5.55\par  Sing dlr      1.7510       1.7365         -0.83\par  Taiwan dlr    34.658       32.900         -5.07\par  Korean won   1292.00      1277.00         -1.16\par  Baht           44.63        43.70         -2.08\par  Peso           51.28        50.75         -1.03\par  Rupiah       9030.00      9470.00         +4.87\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.8000         +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010911dx9b004ms\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
