\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Yen's losses bruise regionals. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,039 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2001\par 11:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 7 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were on the \par \par \uc2  backfoot late on Friday, put off balance by the wobbly yen. \par \par \uc2      Japan's second-quarter economic growth data gave the yen \par \par \uc2   a tiny initial boost as the contraction was not as bad \par \par \uc2  as expected. But the market then realised it was still a \par \par \uc2  contraction of 0.8 percent, even if it beat expectations of 0.9 \par \par \uc2  percent. \par \par \uc2  The yen's tussle with the U.S. dollar dented sentiment \par \par \uc2  towards the regionals, with dealers saying they sensed building \par \par \uc2  confidence among dollar bulls. \par \par \uc2  "People are starting to believe in the dollar/yen move \par \par \uc2  again, so there's a bit of dollar demand against the \par \par \uc2  regionals," said a U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "Korea's got foreign direct investment dropping. Taiwan's \par \par \uc2  stock market keeps collapsing. And Singapore, well, the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's too strong. We just need to get the sentiment and \par \par \uc2  the fundamentals to work together, and the dollar should go \par \par \uc2  higher." \par \par \uc2  After Thursday's poor U.S. economic data, there was \par \par \uc2  lingering doubts as to whether the dollar was seeing a \par \par \uc2  turnaround. The market was awaiting August employmemt data from \par \par \uc2  the United States, due later in the day. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  Dollar demand from local corporates drove the Thai baht \par \par \uc2  lower, with losses in the yen aggravating its falls. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said local corporates were looking to \par \par \uc2  hedge their dollar needs, and were actively looking to pick up \par \par \uc2  the dollar in the spot and forward markets. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. bank based in Singapore was spotted aggressively \par \par \uc2  snapping up dollars, catching local players short on dollar, \par \par \uc2  dealers in Bangkok said. \par \par \uc2  They added that news the Bank of Thailand had tightened \par \par \uc2  supervision of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remissions and transfers did not have \par \par \uc2  an impact on the market. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs were rising with the one-month rate \par \par \uc2  quoted at 7/10 satang per dollar offshore, and -2.5/-1.0 satang \par \par \uc2  onshore. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  U.S. dollar bulls chased the Singapore dollar lower as the \par \par \uc2  yen limped through the Asian day. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the U.S. dollar was struggling in early trade \par \par \uc2  as a European bank dumped some $100 million in the market. But \par \par \uc2  a local bank was spotted bidding for the U.S. unit just past \par \par \uc2  the 1.75 mark, driving it higher. \par \par \uc2  The yen's fall in the afternoon brought more pressure on \par \par \uc2  the Sing dollar. But it managed to avoid the key 1.7540 level, \par \par \uc2  which daily charts showed is a resistance level for the \par \par \uc2  greenback from a trendline starting on August 21. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar faced a sea of troubles, including weaker \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from trade rivals Korea and Japan, the tumbling \par \par \uc2  local stock market and poor trade data. \par \par \uc2      It ended the day at 34.656, against Thursday's 34.616 \par \par \uc2  close. \par \par \uc2      Singapore dealers said Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \par \par \uc2  selling U.S. dollars sporadically during the day, but were not \par \par \uc2  spotted in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2      Taiwanese trade figures for August came in worse than \par \par \uc2  expected, with imports falling 36.5 percent year on year \par \par \uc2  against forecasts of a 26.4 percent dip, and exports down 25.8 \par \par \uc2  percent compared to expectations of a 22.4 percent fall. \par \par \uc2      The Finance Ministry later said exports would not see \par \par \uc2  on-year growth until April 2002. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won took its cue from the yen, giving up early gains\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and touching a four-week low of 1,290.5, as players scrambled\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to cover their short dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore dealers said players panicked after the yen fell\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par through the 121 mark, sending exporters to the sidelines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Export-related inflows and dollar offers by some offshore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players had pushed the won higher earlier in the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the macroeconomic front, August foreign direct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investment data showed a decline of 17.2 percent on the year,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par threatening a government target of $15 billion for the year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, external liabilities continued declining for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 12th consecutive month, and by end of July were at $125.4\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion against $127 billion in June and $136.3 in December\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso edged lower with a rise in dollar demand from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporates and importers, prompting interbank players to build\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par long dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But some equity-related inflows and fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  limited the downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Volume was subdued in lacklustre pre-weekend trade, with a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par total of $77.20 million traded by the end of onshore trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compared to $96 million on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The government said it had concluded a deal for a private\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par placement of 15-year bonds worth a total of at least $250\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million with Credit Suisse First Boston.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    National Treasurer Sergio Edeza said the amount raised would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be used to finance the budget.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah eased to hit a session low past 9,100 as the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market gave a cold shoulder to the draft budget for 2002, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first to be unveiled by President Megawati Sukarnoputri.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and dollar sales by a\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -based bank pushed it back to settle just above the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 9,100 mark.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Jakarta said the budget had no surprises and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some of the assumptions looked too optimistic.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But Jakarta's official creditors, the IMF and the World\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank, said the draft had struck the right balance between\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prudence and stimulating growth.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0843 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.26       121.06         -0.16\par  Sing dlr      1.7533       1.7508         -0.14\par  Taiwan dlr    34.656       34.616         -0.12\par  Korean won   1289.60      1286.50         -0.24\par  Baht           44.69        44.43         -0.57\par  Peso           51.37        51.34         -0.07\par  Rupiah       9085.00      9050.00         -0.39\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     121.26       114.45         -5.62\par  Sing dlr      1.7533       1.7365         -0.96\par  Taiwan dlr    34.656       32.900         -5.07\par  Korean won   1289.60      1277.00         -0.98\par  Baht           44.69        43.70         -2.20\par  Peso           51.37        50.75         -1.21\par  Rupiah       9085.00      9470.00         +4.24\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dx970222z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
