\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Retreat as dollar bolstered by NAPM. \b0\par\par\uc2 889 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2001\par 04:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 5 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ceded ground \par \par \uc2  in early trade on Wednesday after much stronger than expected \par \par \uc2  August U.S. manufacturing data prompted market players to buy \par \par \uc2  back the dollar, which they had sold actively in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2      The National Association of Purchasing Management (NAPM) \par \par \uc2  said its monthly index rose to 47.9 in August, up from 43.6 in \par \par \uc2  July and beating economists' forecasts of 43.9. \par \par \uc2      "The dollar/yen remains the major lead in the market that \par \par \uc2  people follow. But the dollar will need to break convincingly \par \par \uc2  above 120 for the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to get out of their recent \par \par \uc2  ranges," said a dealer at a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      The market was now eyeing Japan's April-June gross domestic \par \par \uc2  product data and U.S. unemployment data for August, both due on \par \par \uc2  Friday. Local media reported Japan's Cabinet Office told policy \par \par \uc2  makers on Tuesday the GDP shrank by 1.2 percent in that period. \par \par \uc2      Otherwise, Korea will release its August producer price \par \par \uc2  index at 0300 GMT and the Philippines is scheduled to publish \par \par \uc2  its August consumer price index at 0100 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar mirrored the yen's losses against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar amid a lack of local leads.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said dollar offers by some U.S. banks around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7480-1.7490 helped the Singapore dollar bounce off its early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par low of 1.7495, but overall the pressure was on the downside\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with local players favouring the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A convincing break of 1.75 was possible if the yen falls\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par past the 120 mark with some support expected at around 1.7530,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the August 23 low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht lost ground on broad-based dollar buying from both\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore and onshore players after the strong NAPM data set off\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rounds of dollar buybacks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But exporters' dollar offers around 44.25-44.30 should help\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slow down the dollar's rise, dealers in Bangkok said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "People have been chasing dollar since last night. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rebound might be sustained in the near-term if Japan's GDP\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par numbers come in worse than expected," said a dealer at a U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank in Bangkok.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Demand for the dollar pushed baht funding costs higher,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the one-month forward rate edging up to 4/7 satang per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar offshore and -2.7/-2.2 satang onshore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah edged up above 9,000 helped by early dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sales by offshore players amid wariness over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday's draft for the 2002\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par budget, which is likely to give clues to government plans to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fix the troubled economy and talks with the Paris Club of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par creditor nations starting on Monday, was likely to attract\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attention.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Jakarta will seek rescheduling of $6 billion in foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par debt with the Club to ease pressure from debt repayments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso opened slightly lower at 51.20 compared with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday close of 51.15, tracking the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The country's August annual inflation came in at 6.3\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent against 6.8 percent in July.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower-than-expected inflation would give the bank more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par flexibility in interest rate policy, but added the bank did not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par need to lower the rates immediately.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar slipped a notch in line with the yen,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with renewed U.S. dollar buying interest in the non-deliverable\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forwards market keeping the greenback firm in the spot market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dealers said interest in buying U.S. dollars was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par perking up in both the spot and NDF markets after a long lull.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They added further falls in the yen could spur the market to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par take more long U.S. dollar positions against the Taiwan dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But dealers were still wary of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been on both sides of the market and kept the Taiwan dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par within a narrow range 34.463-34.686 since August 3.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won gave up some ground as it followed the yen south,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with falls on the local bourse also driving its retreat.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Still, Singapore dealers said the won's losses were an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par early reaction to the softer yen and lower stock prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said trading interest in the market was still minimal,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and expected dollar offers from exporters to emerge around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,285.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0133 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.78       119.43         -0.29\par  Sing dlr      1.7478       1.7450         -0.16\par  Taiwan dlr    34.587       34.548         -0.11\par  Korean won   1280.00      1280.00         +0.00\par  Baht           44.30        44.12         -0.40\par  Peso           51.24        51.15         -0.18\par  Rupiah       9060.00      9075.00         +0.17\par  Ringgit       3.7994       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End pr