\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Riding on yen's coat tail, US data eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2 947 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2001\par 04:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 4 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  retained \par \par \uc2  their gains early on Tuesday as the highly correlated yen \par \par \uc2  advanced further against the dollar despite Japan's poor \par \par \uc2  economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2      Some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were at their best levels in weeks as \par \par \uc2  market participants continued to pare down their long dollar \par \par \uc2  positions. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the yen's strength was a combination of doubts \par \par \uc2  over the U.S. economic recovery, funds repatriation to Japan \par \par \uc2  ahead of end-September book closings, and declines in foreign \par \par \uc2  portfolio investments by Japanese investors. \par \par \uc2      Morgan Stanley Dean Witter said Japanese investors had \par \par \uc2  gradually decreased their investments in foreign assets over \par \par \uc2  the past three weeks because the recent continuous declines of \par \par \uc2  the Nikkei had reduced their risk appetite. \par \par \uc2      The market was watching out for the U.S. NAPM survey due \par \par \uc2  out on Tuesday to see whether it confirms the improvement in \par \par \uc2  manufacturing data reported on Friday. \par \par \uc2      Elsewhere in the region, the Philippines published its \par \par \uc2  latest exports data and Hong Kong will release its July \par \par \uc2  external trade figures at 0800 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar followed after the yen, though the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market was wary of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the authorities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers and analysts say the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading around the upper half of its neutral band, which means\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore (MAS) would be more likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to buy U.S. dollars to cap the Sing dollar's gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A European bank dealer said the MAS was suspected of buying\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollars late last week around 1.7370, which is also the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 100 percent retracement of the U.S. dollar's rise from February\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 27-July 16.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The MAS issued a survey on Monday which showed economists\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expect the city-state's economy to contract by 0.6 percent this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year due to the sharp downturn in the electronics cycle.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht struggled to break convincingly above 44.00 as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate demand for the dollar and fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar bids above that level capped its gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said if the dollar dropped further against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht, there was a good chance the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might step in to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buy the dollar on dips either to top up the foreign reserves or\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to repay debts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market was also cautious about buying the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par actively after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Monday it would review\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading supervision rules to prevent money laundering.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The remark followed the discovery by police last week of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suspected money laundering \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , allegedly involving\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par individuals working at a Singapore bank in Bangkok.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won rose slightly as it rode on the yen's coat tails,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with an early rise in local stocks giving it an added boost.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But Singapore dealers said the market lacked the drive to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par push the won higher as offshore players opted for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sidelines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "There's just no determination out there to test the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/won's downside. We definitely need a bigger move in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/yen," said a European bank dealer in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He added players were not concerned about possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the authorities were probably comfortable\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the cross rate with the yen and won . It was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quoted at 10.77/10.79 at 0045 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah was expected to stay under pressure from local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporates' dollar demand for debt payment and import needs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said rupiah's downside was limited\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par amid fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aimed at keeping\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the rupiah on the right side of the 9,000 mark.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, lack of support from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could pull\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the rupiah down to around 9,200, a multi-week low seen last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was expected to linger in a narrow range around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 51 per dollar mark amid a lack of fresh trading cues.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said most corporates were staying on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sidelines, waiting for the authorities to push the peso higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, interbank players were reluctant to take short\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar positions amid a lack of dollar inflows and an expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise in demand as the import season peaks in September.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar edged higher in line with a steady yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but equity-related outflows and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to cap significant gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors were net sellers of 1.64 billion Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars worth of local shares on Monday, bringing the net\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par selling to 5.86 billion Taiwan dollars over the last five\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sessions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, the recent strengthening of the yen has prompted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players to bail out of long dollar positions. The market tracks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par movements in the yen as Taiwan competes with Japan in several\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par export markets.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0136 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     118.85       118.80         -0.04\par  Sing dlr      1.7392       1.7395         +0.02\par  Taiwan dlr    34.540       34.538         -0.01\par  Korean won   1279.00      1279.00         +0.00\par  Baht           43.96        44.03         +0.17\par  Peso           51.02        51.04         +0.04\par  Rupiah       8990.00      8950.00         -0.44\par  Ringgit       3.7999       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.85       114.45         -3.70\par  Sing dlr      1.7392       1.7365         -0.16\par  Taiwan dlr    34.540       32.900         -4.75\par  Korean won   1279.00      1277.00         -0.16\par  Baht           43.96        43.70         -0.58\par  Peso           51.02        50.75         -0.53\par  Rupiah       8990.00      9470.00         +5.34\par  Ringgit       3.7999       3.7995         -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010904dx94004by\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
