\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Dn Late; Mkts Seek Dlr Direction \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 768 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2001\par 10:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were slightly weaker, languishing in tight ranges late Monday as fears of raising the ire of the region's central banks kept the dollar buoyed, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  As Japanese officials stepped up their verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep a rein on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent strength, the dollar stayed afloat against the yen, in turn keeping the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supported against most of its Asian counterparts, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Suspected bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  in London trade Friday, when the U.S. dollar skidded to as low as S$1.7370, also pressured the Singapore dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Fears of provoking the monetary authorities in South Korea, Taiwan and Thailand also restrained the movements of their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had surged Friday as the dollar floundered on increased despondency over the U.S. economy, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The region's bleak economic fundamentals don't justify the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' recent resilience, which has been inspired by the yen, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  At 0742 GMT (3:42 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y118.81, little changed from Y118.80 late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  With the direction of the dollar still murky ahead of a slew of potentially market-moving data this week, participants were also wary of building any major positions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. National Association of Purchasing Management index of manufacturing will be issued Tuesday, and the August employment report Friday. Japan is scheduled to announce its second-quarter gross domestic product data Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Markets are quite undecided as to what the next direction for the dollar is," said Thio Chin Loo, a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas. "There are mixed signals on the U.S. economy." \par \par \uc2  U.S. economic data issued last Friday, including the Chicago Purchasing Managers Index and July factory orders, came in better than market expectations. \par \par \uc2  "The market, which is a bit confused right now, needs more weak data to justify the dollar sentiment," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  With U.S. markets closed Monday for the Labor Day holiday, trading in the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was subdued. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar skirted around the S$1.7400 level against its U.S. counterpart most of the day, following suspected buying in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  in London trade. \par \par \uc2  Late in the day, the U.S. dollar inched higher to S$1.7413, above S$1.7374 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Thio at BNP Paribas noted that the Singapore dollar, which has been the main beneficiary in Asia from the yen's recent advance, is relatively strong compared with most of its regional peers, which have largely been rangebound. \par \par \uc2  "If the Singapore dollar does outperform against the other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the chances of the MAS coming in will increase," she added. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was marginally weaker at 44.075 baht per dollar, compared with THB44.025 late Friday, with participants unperturbed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reporting requirements for financial institutions, which take effect Monday, dealers said. The requirements are intended to curb speculation on the baht and damp volatility. \par \par \uc2  The baht also ignored a local newspaper report Monday that the Government of Singapore Investment Corp. has signaled to Thai authorities that it isn't interested in investing in Thailand's matching-fund scheme at present. \par \par \uc2  Hopes that the Singapore government's investment arm would participate in the equities fund had in recent weeks stoked expectations of foreign fund inflows, contributing to the baht's recent strength. \par \par \uc2  Dollar demand by local corporations needing to repay their foreign debt continued to weigh on the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was at 9,055 rupiah to the dollar, compared with around IDR8,860 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  In Seoul, the dollar finished at 1,280.1 won, slightly higher than KRW1,278 Friday. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine Dealing System, the dollar closed at 51.040 pesos, higher than PHP50.935 Friday. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar resisted the region's downward draft, finding respite from exporter's dollar sales and sluggish demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by importers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought U.S. dollars to offset the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation, in Taiwan's apparent bid to maintain the price competitiveness of its exports, dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ended at NTS$34.538, lower than NT$34.554 Friday.\par    -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4043;\par netty.ismail@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010903dx93000fj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
