\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late; Hits 28-Wk High On Yen, Euro Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2001\par 11:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was sharply stronger late Friday, hitting a 28-week high against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it tracked a stronger yen and euro, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT (4:30 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7370 - a 28-week low - down from S$1.7473 late Thursday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened lower in Asia and fell sharply in early trade, in line with its fall below Y119. The euro's rise above US$0.9150 also helped push the U.S. dollar lower against its Singapore counterpart, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Interbank market participants and a U.S. investment house were the main sellers of U.S. dollars in the morning, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Subsequent light U.S. dollar buying by some local banks as well as a European and U.S. bank - suspected to have been a feeble \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempt on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  - provided some support to the dollar below S$1.7380, the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar-yen looks heavy and therefore the dollar-Sing is also looking soft," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted that with U.S. dollar stop-loss orders lined up below Y118.50, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could test Y118.30 support later Friday or next week. Such a move would push the U.S. dollar past its initial support at S$1.7350, toward the next support level at S$1.7320. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the U.S. dollar's upside is expected to be capped at S$1.7440, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were mostly higher Friday, boosted by a stronger Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  Bonds opened flat and were thinly traded before lunch with most of the gains occurring in the afternoon session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds fell two basis points to 2.18%, while the yield on five-year bonds fell one basis point to 2.87%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds fell one basis point to 3.28%, and the 10-year yield fell one basis point to 3.55%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the new 15-year bond fell one basis point to 3.81%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mas.gov.sg/sgs}}}\uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swaps generally tracked bond yields\par lower. The most liquid seven-year swap offer closed two basis points\par lower at 3.41% and the 10-year swap offer closed flat at 3.66%.\par ///   The spread between the two- and 10-year swaps was 104.5 basis\par points.///\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank money market, the overnight rate rose on month-end\par and pre-weekend demand for funds, while term rates were mostly flat amid\par ample liquidity in the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Friday       Late Thursday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         2.0000% 2.1250%   1.3750% 1.5000%\par 3-Month           2.1250% 2.2500%   2.1250% 2.2500%\par 1-Year            2.2500% 2.3750%   2.2500% 2.3750%\par -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; (+65) 415-4152;\par amit.prakash@dowjones.com\par -0- 31/08/01 09-23G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010831dx8v000i7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
