\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Boosted by dlr retreat after Fed's cut. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,001 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2001\par 04:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 22 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to higher ground with the yen early on Wednesday as the dollar fell after the Federal Reserve cut interest rates for the seventh time this year to boost the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  The Federal Open Market Committee lowered its benchmark federal funds rate by a quarter-point to 3.50 percent, as had been widely expected, and indicated it was poised to do more to boost the world's largest economy. \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment has been shifted to one of frustration. People have been trying to walk across the valley to the other side of the recovery and they are just a bit tired. They are now beginning to disbelieve in the recovery because the hard data don't seem to support the recovery yet," said Clifford Bennett, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Comments by Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa that he was not considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for now also sent traders rushing to buy back yen, which they sold earlier due to fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to track the yen higher, but with gains capped by Asia's weak fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  On the data front, Singapore is due to release July consumer price data on Thursday and industrial production on Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was weighed by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) was rumoured to have been in the market to check rates during London trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was caught between dollar bargain hunting from U.S. and Australian names and offers by funds and other foreign names. \par \par \uc2  They expected its downside to be supported by a firmer yen and the dollar's weak tone. \par \par \uc2  "While (the Sing dollar) was overbought in relation to the worsening domestic outlook, it can still overshoot on the upside given the bearish sentiment for the dollar, although on a three to six month view the Sing dollar is expected to trade in a 1.78-1.80 range," said DBS in a note. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was steadier, beholden to the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a dearth of strong domestic leads. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected it's upside to be capped at 44.40 for now where corporates were likely to pick up the dollar on dips. \par \par \uc2  The 44.40 level is also a key technical level because it represents the 38 percent retracement of the dollar's February 2-April 9 rise. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs were easier offshore, with the tom/next rate quoted at -0.18/-0.17 satang per dollar while the one-month rate was quoted at 1.5/3.0 satang. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won found inspiration in the yen's gains and clambered higher, though falls in local stocks capped its rise. \par \par \uc2  It was quoted at 1,283 against 1,283.8 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Pessimism over the U.S. economy was also likely to counterbalance the impact of the stronger yen, as the United States is the main destination for Korean exports. \par \par \uc2  While domestic consumption was able to keep the country's economy growing in the second quarter, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said a recovery in the electronics sector and the U.S. were key to Korea's rebound. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar inched higher along with the won and yen, but was expected to remain within its recent range of 34.50-34.70 because of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been spotted on both sides of the market to prevent volatility in the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the authorities want to keep the Taiwan dollar competitive to sell the island's key electronics exports. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso marched in step with the stronger regionals, but local corporate dollar demand below the 51 level was expected to limit its rise. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said the market was still suffering from a dearth of dollars, which added pressure on the peso when interbank players covered their short dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  But they said continued dollar sales from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have kept the peso at the higher end of its recent range. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was likely to keep rates steady despite the Fed cut at its weekly policy meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  It added that it would consider hiking reserve requirements again. The bank has already hiked reserve requirements by four percentage points to shore up support for the peso by draining liquidity in the market. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was locked in an 8,500-8,550 range in early thin trade as the market looked for fresh incentives. \par \par \uc2  Its downside was underpinned by Bank Indonesia-engineered tight rupiah liquidity, bearish sentiment towards the dollar, and hopes for an agreement with the IMF. \par \par \uc2  President Megawati Sukarnoputri was on her Southeast Asian tour to drum up support for her new government. Diplomats said Megawati's decision to go on a regional tour was aimed at displaying confidence in weathering the troubles at home. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0200 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.84       120.18         +0.28\par  Sing dlr      1.7533       1.7485         -0.27\par  Taiwan dlr    34.556       34.586         +0.09\par  Korean won   1281.00      1283.50         +0.20\par  Baht           44.75        44.67         -0.18\par  Peso           50.80        51.25         +0.89\par  Rupiah       8520.00      8540.00         +0.23\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.84       114.45         -4.50\par  Sing dlr      1.7533       1.7365         -0.96\par  Taiwan dlr    34.556       32.900         -4.79\par  Korean won   1281.00      1277.00         -0.31\par  Baht           44.75        43.70         -2.35\par  Peso           50.80        50.75         -0.10\par  Rupiah       8520.00      9470.00        +11.15\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dx8m015d2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
