\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Softer as yen slips on jawboning. \b0\par\par\uc2 941 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2001\par 04:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Aug 17 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped \par \par \uc2  early on Friday as fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japan took away \par \par \uc2  some of the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2      Jawboning from Japanese officials on Thursday finally had \par \par \uc2  its intended effect, with dollar bears backing off as the \par \par \uc2  market turned cautious over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The veiled threats continued into Friday when a top \par \par \uc2  Japanese finance ministry official said recent movements in the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have been excessive and undesirable, and that \par \par \uc2  the ministry was closely monitoring the market. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also stabilised during overnight trade as mixed \par \par \uc2  U.S. data calmed some doubts over the health of the U.S. \par \par \uc2  economy. \par \par \uc2  Trading was expected to be light ahead of the Federal \par \par \uc2  Reserve's meeting on Tuesday. The Federal Open Market Committee \par \par \uc2  is expected to make its decision on interest rates at 1815 GMT \par \par \uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar, which has been setting the tone for \par \par \uc2  Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was bracing itself for July's \par \par \uc2  non-oil exports due at 0430 GMT. Economists polled by Reuters \par \par \uc2  expect exports to fall by as much as 24 percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan was facing second-quarter gross domestic product \par \par \uc2  growth data, due out after 0900 GMT. A Reuters poll showed \par \par \uc2  economists expected on average a contraction of 0.30 percent. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was on the backfoot as it trailed \par \par \uc2  after the softer yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said unwinding of long U.S. dollar positions by \par \par \uc2  funds had lightened up as the dollar steadied during overnight \par \par \uc2  trade. \par \par \uc2  They added the U.S. dollar should find support above \par \par \uc2  1.7400, which it hit for the first time since February 28 late \par \par \uc2  on Thursday. Some dealers said there was market talk the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore might buy U.S. dollars around \par \par \uc2  that level given the weak economy. \par \par \uc2      The market was keeping an eye on July's non-oil exports due \par \par \uc2  out at 0430 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar was reluctant to move out its recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range with players sidelined on wariness over the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Trading was also cautious ahead of the release of Taiwan's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par second-quarter GDP numbers, which is expected to show a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par contraction for the first time in 26 years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But analysts expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent the local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar from straying too far from a range of around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 34.50-34.70, where it has been since August 6.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won eased as players squared out of short dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions on the local stock market's early fall and wariness\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that authorities may try to cap the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers said Thursday's rumours of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after a state-run bank was spotted buying dollars had already\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par made players cautious.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank of Korea governor Chon Chol-hwan said earlier he saw\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par room for further cuts in lending rates, as previous rate cuts\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par have had little effect on existing loans to corporates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Earlier this month, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lowered its target for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the overnight call rate by 25 basis points to 4.50 percent,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par marking it the third rate cut so far this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso stayed within its recent range around 51, torn\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between rising dollar demand from corporates and importers and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fears of more support for the peso from authorities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deputy governor Amando Tetangco said on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday the option of higher reserve requirements was still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par under consideration if the bank felt there was excess peso\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par liquidity to be drained.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The liquidity reserve requirements had been raised twice by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a total of 400 basis points to 11 percent and along with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par statutory requirement at nine percent, banks now have to keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 20 percent of their loanable deposits in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vaults.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht drifted in a paper-thin pre-weekend trading as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players kept a low profile ahead of the Fed's meeting next\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar/yen remains a key factor for the market to watch\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in a dearth of strong domestic leads.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Market reaction to an IMF assessment on Thailand has so far\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been mild. The report said Thailand's economic recovery is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par vulnerable and faces a threat from the slowing global economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     IMF directors repeated their recommendation that Thai\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rates stay low. Dealers said most of those factors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been priced in.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The offshore non-deliverable market for the rupiah was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quiet in the absence of onshore trading as financial markets in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jakarta were closed on Friday and will resume trading on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There is not much going on. The market is slightly long on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar and people are happy with the positions they have,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said an NDF dealer in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0151 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.31       119.27         -0.86\par  Sing dlr      1.7482       1.7419         -0.36\par  Taiwan dlr    34.537       34.520         -0.05\par  Korean won   1274.00      1272.00         -0.16\par  Baht           44.65        44.48         -0.38\par  Peso           51.12        50.95         -0.33\par  Rupiah       8575.00      8725.00         +1.75\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.31       114.45         -4.87\par  Sing dlr      1.7482       1.7365         -0.67\par  Taiwan dlr    34.537       32.900         -4.74\par  Korean won   1274.00      1277.00         +0.24\par  Baht           44.65        43.70         -2.13\par  Peso           51.12        50.75         -0.72\par  Rupiah       8575.00      9470.00        +10.44\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010817dx8h004o6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
