\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Up Late; Singapore Dlr Leads Rise \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 811 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2001\par 11:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended their recent ascent late Thursday, riding on the coattails of the Japanese yen's advance as the broad-based dollar retreat showed no sign of letting up, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0920 GMT (4:20 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y119.32, below Y119.65 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y121.57 late Wednesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is still weak globally, and this should support Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg. "People are selling dollars on any rally in Asia." \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill's unconvincing defense of the dollar has heightened the ambiguity surrounding the Bush administration's commitment to a strong dollar policy, in turn supporting Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There is no upside in talking about the dollar, except to say we have a continuing, continuous policy," Mr. O'Neill said in a CNBC interview Wednesday. "We've still got the same dollar policy." O'Neill didn't use the word "strong" to describe the dollar policy, contrary to the practice of the Clinton administration. \par \par \uc2  As the dollar continued to be clobbered, many Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , led by the Singapore dollar, surged to multi-month highs, ignoring the region's bleak economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  The appreciation of their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had prompted some of the region's monetary authorities to step in to slow the rise, in an apparent bid to maintain the price competitiveness of their countries' exports, dealers believed. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively bought U.S. dollars, especially toward the close of trading, dealers said. The South Korean authority issued a warning against excessive gains in the won. Some dealers believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, though this was unconfirmed. \par \par \uc2  Talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's rally, which gained momentum overnight, as participants continued to sell the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar surged to as high as S$1.7400 against its U.S. counterpart in late trade, before profit-taking in short U.S. dollar positions pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to S$1.7423. Late Wednesday, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7534. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won played catch up with the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains as trading resumed following a national holiday Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  But dollar purchases by the state-run Korea Development Bank and a warning by the finance ministry against "excessive market reaction to a specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move" moderated the won's gains, despite the yen's rally, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at 1,278.2 won, down 0.8% from Tuesday's close of KRW1,288.5. \par \par \uc2  The yen's strength and the local stock market's 1.4% jump thrusted the New Taiwan dollar through the NT$34.50 resistance level against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last 15 minutes of trading - which shored up trading volume to US$950 million from US$611 million - pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back above NTS$34.50, dealers said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounted for more than half of the day's total volume dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ended at a seven-week low of NT$34.520, down from Wednesday's close of NT$34.570. \par \par \uc2  Overall, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely accounted for more than half of the total volume, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht gradually extended its recent gains, but continued to lag behind the region's rally, amid fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dollar demand by oil companies and importers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 44.555 baht, lower than THB44.905 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso ended unchanged, as remarks by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official renewed fears of a further hike in the reserve requirement on bank deposits, helping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recoup its earlier losses, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Amando Tetangco said a hike in the liquidity reserve is an option "in case there is excess liquidity that can influence inflation, or trigger a weakening of the (peso)." \par \par \uc2  Some dealers suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an estimated $50 million to $60 million to counter the pressure on the peso earlier in the day from corporate demand and short covering for dollars by banks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, denied \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 50.950 pesos, unchanged from its level Wednesday. The dollar hit an intraday high of PHP51.160. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was firmer at 8,770 rupiah per dollar, compared with IDR8,825 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4043; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010816dx8g000jf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
