\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar fall enlivens Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 988 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2001\par 04:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 10 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  perked up in early trade on Friday, drawing strength from the dollar's losses against other majors. \par \par \uc2  Local factors also lent support. The peso was bolstered by news of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raising liquidity reserve requirements to keep liquidity in check and defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was closely watching the trend of the dollar which had recently exhibited signs of fatigue, but it was too early to say if the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was reversing course. \par \par \uc2  "A grim picture painted by the Fed's beige book is seeping in. The dollar seems to have recently displayed sensitivity to bearish data, news and lost its momentum," said a senior dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  "Now the question being asked by the market is this: If the U.S. economy is slow to react to rate cuts and tax packages, will U.S. policymakers soon turn a blind eye to dollar weakness? But I still think this is just a correction," he said. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso nudged up to touch a high of 52.84, against Thursday's low of 53.18 as commercial banks adjusted their positions after another hike in their reserve requirement. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday raised liquidity reserve requirements of commercial banks by two percentage points to 11 percent to mop up excess liquidity. The rise was in addition to a two percent hike on July 27. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said the move would suck about 12 billion pesos from the system in the next few days but with the import season at its peak, demand for the dollar was likely to persist. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar broke the key 1.7650 mark for the first time since March 19 in thin overnight trade, helped by a firmer yen and improved political situation in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investors continued to pare long dollar positions early on Friday. \par \par \uc2  However, they expected the pace of the U.S. dollar decline against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be slow because most players had already unwound dollar longs quite actively ahead of the National Day holiday on Thursday. Charts show the Sing dollar is still in its upward channel against the dollar, dating back to July 17. \par \par \uc2  The government confirmed that the growth rate turned negative in the second quarter due to a sharp slowdown in electronics manufacturing and warned of worse ahead in the third quarter. \par \par \uc2  Second quarter GDP fell 0.9 percent on-year and 10.7 percent on an annualised quarter-on-quarter basis. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won firmed up to touch a high of 1,278.5 on the back of a rising yen and a strong opening in the local stock market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the won's rise prompted players to square out of dollar shorts as the won broke through the 1,280 mark for the first time since June 1 when it touched a high of 1,277.5. \par \par \uc2  They said some state-run banks were spotted buying dollars, sparking rumours they were acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Talk of brighter prospects of the sale of troubled Daewoo Motors to U.S. giant General Motors also buoyed overall sentiment. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah held on to its recent gains, hovering around 9,100 on euphoria over the new government, and support from a state bank, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One state bank sold around $5 million into a thin market in early trade, sparking speculation Bank Indonesia might be behind the move. \par \par \uc2  President Megawati Sukarnoputri will swear in her new cabinet on Friday. Her choices of ministers won rave reviews from the market and media. \par \par \uc2  But strong rupiah gains are unlikely given the dollar is heavily oversold, with charts showing a reading of 7.2 on the 14-day relative strength index. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar edged up in line with a firmer yen but a bearish stock market outlook on poor July corporate sales and worries about economic growth prospects were expected to keep the upside limited. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors were net sellers of T$2.19 billion worth of local shares on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to stall the Taiwan dollar's rise above 34.60 would also keep players cautious. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht nudged above 45.30 on the back of firmer regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but dealers saw its gains capped at 45.20 due to active corporate dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand is yet to announce changes in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  disclosure rules, but the market has largely discounted the possibility they will be streamlined and more market-friendly. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs in the offshore market were mostly steady, with the tom/next rate quoted at -0.12/-0.06 satang per dollar, one-month rate at 3/12 satang and 12-month at 135/155. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0217 GMT \par \par \uc2